. Is that what you've found?\par \par \uc2 JORGE VENTURA, "DAILY CALLER" FIELD REPORTER: Yes, Laura, the key word that I get from speaking to Latino voters is abandoned. So when I was down there, they say the Democratic Party has abandoned us. They haven't been here in 40 years. One voter even mentioned to me that when he goes to the congressional offices just to speak to a candidate about their issues, no one is there anymore.\par \par \uc2 And the reason that for Congresswoman Mayra Flores her message has been resonating with these voters is because she speaks God and country, which they can connect. All Hispanics around America are overwhelmingly middle- class, working class folks. They have been getting hit hard with inflation. They feel that the Democrats are not serving their economic needs, and as well the border crisis. That's an issue that really impacts all those border towns. And it has really been fascinating because all of these border towns are overwhelmingly Democrat, but we see these huge swings that we have never seen before, and we have three congressional races right now that the GOP is investing millions of dollars that they feel that the Latino vote can be the key to victory there.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Jorge, remember we were told after that 2012 lost by \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  that there was the autopsy for the GOP and that they had to be more pro- immigration, amnesty, more open borders, more globalists. That was totally wrong, wasn't it?\par \par \uc2 VENTURA: Yes, it wasn't even close. You go down and talk to working class Latinos down there, they want a strong border. And the reason why they support the strong border, legal immigration, is because they want to protect their wages. Illegal immigration actually hurts Hispanic workers all over the country. And those wages are not seeing that growth there. So it's a true humanitarian crisis what they're seeing. They're completely overwhelmed. Law enforcement, Governor Greg Abbott had to call in the National Guard. You have Texas law enforcement helping out border patrol. Everyone down there is trying to assist each other in what is a true humanitarian crisis.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And most of the Border Patrol, at least the ones I have met down in Del Rio, they're Hispanic.\par \par \uc2 VENTURA: They're Hispanic, and morale is the lowest it's ever been. They don't feel like they have any support from this current administration.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Jorge, it is great to see you. Thank you for that great report.\par \par \uc2 VENTURA: Thank you, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, \uc2 Beto O'Rourke\uc2  was supposed to be in the great blue hope, right, in Texas, he was going to turn the whole state blue. But his second statewide run looks like it's going to be another dud. Governor Greg Abbott is swamping him in the polls and joins me next to reveal how Hispanics are helping to drive that surge. That's next when we return to our Retaking America townhall in Houston, Texas.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: You're really excited about Beto. You want to vote for him for governor. Talk to me about why that is.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I feel like, again, I haven't brushed up before this particular thing. I like Beto.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: One thing you like about Beto?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: What is that big policy that Beto has put forth that you really like that captured your attention?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I'm not really sure, to be honest.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: No?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: No. I'm not the most political person on earth, but he seems cool.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: So you said you like Beto because of the abortion issue. Talk about why that is important to you.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I don't know, I just feel like women should have a choice to have an abortion.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Do you hope that abortion is also an option for women just in case get a girl pregnant.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Yes, I guess.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Yes, of course.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I am going to be voting for Beto this time.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: For Beto, how come?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It's a lot of different -- it is very -- let me think about that. I'm a big pothead, and I really want him to legalize weed.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Abbott or Beto?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Beto.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: How come.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It's more like a family thing. I don't really know a lot of the stuff that he is doing.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Can you feel that Beto-mentum? Oh, yes. Now, remember, Beto was the one, right? The former punk rocker, the rockstar who could turn it all blue in Texas.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Is the third time really the charm? \uc2 Beto O'Rourke\uc2  hopes that it is. Is the name recognition enough for Texans to turn Texas blue for Beto?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: If Democrats want to make inroads and actually flip Texas from red to blue, then they need candidates like \uc2 Beto O'Rourke\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He's the only one feeling blue these days, because a recent poll from the University of Texas shows him down to Governor Greg Abbott by 11 points.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But it was something inside the poll that really caught our eye, and it's based in that reason we are here tonight. In his 2018 election win, Governor Abbott lost Hispanic vote by 11 points. In that University of Texas poll, but he and Beto are now tied at 48 percent amongst that slice of the electorate, huge shift.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now, Texas Governor Greg Abbott himself.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Governor, good to see you, man. Great to be with you.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, that's a big shift. That is a double-digit shift for you. What is happening? Why are the Hispanics coming to the Republican Party?\par \par \uc2 GOV. GREG ABBOTT, (R) TEXAS: Two things. One is we constantly reach out to the Hispanic community. No governor has gone down to the Rio Grande Valley more than I have. We are constantly reaching out and connecting with the Hispanic community. And like your other guests tonight, the policies that I'm running on are the policies that the Hispanic community supports. They believe in hard work, entrepreneurs, and hence, they want a state that creates jobs and a strong economy.\par \par \uc2 As we gather here tonight, Texas has the fastest growing economy of any state in the United States.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Also, also, Texas -- since these folks reelected me, Texas has added far more new job than any other state in America. Texas is the place for economic opportunity.\par \par \uc2 But at the same time, Hispanics, whether you are on the border or in Houston, Texas, or north Texas, they don't want Biden's or the Democrats open border policies. They want a secure border. And because Biden is not doing it, they have to have a governor to step up and secure the border. And that is exactly what I'm doing by taken unprecedented action to build a wall, to deploy the National Guard to secure the border. And those who make it, we are going to bus them up to sanctuary cities, to New York, Washington D.C., and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. Now, we want everyone to get out and vote because I don't want people to feel complacent, like we got this. No, no. Everybody has got to get out and vote. Every American who is eligible to vote has to get out there and vote. And I want to play Beto's pitch to MSNBC last night.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BETO O'ROURKE, (D) TEXAS GUBERNATORIAL CANDIDATE: And or reduce significantly gun violence in the state, especially when it comes to --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 O'ROURKE: Let's restore a woman's right to choose. Let's get behind our public educators who are under attack and are leaving the profession by the thousands. The majority of Texans art with us on this. We are going to have the political will to get the job done.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He is anti Second American. He will talk a good game, but he is against then rights in this state and across this country, is he not?\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Let's use his words. He said he would confiscate your guns. So he wants to ignore the Second Amendment to the United States Constitution and take your guns.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He is also pushing the abortion issue, because the Democrats for a long time thought that that was going to be their golden goose here. After the Dobbs decision came down in June, they thought that was going to turn this state blue and others like it. On that question, how is Texas handling this given all the suburban women out there who do have a different view on this issue?\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Very different than in other states. On the abortion issue, the recent polling that showed, I think in that same poll that you made reference to, it showed who do you choose most on the abortion issue? We're even among women. And so this is an issue where in Texas, Texas is a pro- life state.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What's going to happen?\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Here's, here's --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Other Republicans are kind of running away from it. You're not.\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Hold on a second. Very importantly, what everyone in the state now knows because we have exposed Beto on this issue, Beto is in favor not just of abortion but abortion of a child to the very last second before a fully developed child is born and was even against providing medical care for a baby who survives an abortion. That is horrible what Beto stands for.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So he is the radical on the issue is your claim?\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Beto is the extremist on abortion.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: On the issue of ESG and what's happening, the equity agenda for corporate America and how the energy industry, which is so critical and vital to this state, is just under siege. They're making a lot of money because the quantity of oil and so forth is down, so prices are up. But the attack on the ability to borrow money for companies that want to drill or want to be exploring for oil to the extent that they can, it can be devastating. How are you going to fight back on that issue?\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Unlike Beto, I do support the oil and gas industry. Texas ranks number one in the United States for oil and gas production, and we will continue to do so. But let me explain to you what we are doing to fight back.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Because what we're doing to fight back is last session I signed a law that exists in Texas now where we are fighting back against any business, like \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  or USB or \uc2 UBS\uc2 , or any of any of these banking companies that discriminate against oil and gas companies and do not lend them money. We are blackballing them.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They are already starting to dry up the money for these companies.\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: We're blackballing them from doing business in the state of Texas. They cannot participate in any --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How about the pension funds in this state?\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: We are blackballing all of these companies.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Are you cutting them off from the pension funds?\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: We're government cut them off from the pension funds.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wow, OK. That's good.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Governor, I can't wait to talk to you after your reelection. But congratulations for everything you have done in this state, and everyone get out and vote for Greg Abbott. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Thank you, Laura.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, one of the largest Hispanic owned businesses in the United States is based right here in Houston, Texas. The CEO of \uc2 Goya Foods\uc2 , I'm so excited he is here, \uc2 Robert Unanue\uc2  is here next on why Latinos are rejecting the left over their disastrous economic policies when our Retaking America townhall returns live from Houston, Texas.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Big warning sign tonight, 65 percent of Latino voters, the fastest growing demographic in the United States, disapprove of Biden's handling of the economy.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: For a lot of Latino voters, the economy is such a huge issue, maybe an overriding issue.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Those folks who are most feeling the pinch, that is going to going to have a huge impact.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Latino voters, for example, where they are feeling the brunt of that economic impact.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Houston is home to the largest Hispanic owned business privately held in America, \uc2 Goya Foods\uc2 . We are honored to have our old friend, Goya's CEO \uc2 Bob Unanue\uc2  with us tonight. He's on set. Bob, thank you for joining us. It's so good to see you.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT UNANUE\uc2 , CEO OF \uc2 GOYA FOODS\uc2 : Great to see you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, these policies are just at war with small business, but medium-size business, business, period. So why are big business giving so much money to the Democrats still? Why?\par \par \uc2 UNANUE: First of all, Laura, congratulations on your anniversary, five years with your values and your faith, your incredible voice for this country. Our country has been hijacked and we need to take it back.\par \par \uc2 What has happened over the last couple of years with the shutdown, with COVID and all of that, we have declared war on the working class. It has given rise to the pajama class. We have -- they have attempted to kill our spirit. I like the genie in Aladdin who says to Aladdin never drink from that clip of power or money because you will never be satisfied.\par \par \uc2 And we've got to fire these people who are using and abusing the working class of this country and all of us. This country is unrecognizable within two years, and we need to take it back. I'm very excited about the candidates you have on here, Mayra, Monica, and Cassy, and this group. They hold the values -- God, family, work. And we've got to work.\par \par \uc2 Jose Marti, the Cuban philosopher said, there are those who are born to love and build and those who hate and destroy. We have taken the path, this administration has taken a path of hate and destroy. We need to love and build. And you can't build unless you work.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 UNANUE: And we need to work.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Bob, there's so many people here tonight who own businesses, run businesses, make payrolls, most people in Washington don't know how to make a payroll, never did. And they are talking about the lack of work ethic that this shutdown and the Biden bucks that were sent out to people. How concerned are you that we're conditioning a new generation to put me time ahead of actual responsibility?\par \par \uc2 UNANUE: We're all over the world, we never stop working, because we are an essential business. But all business is essential. We need a reason to get up every day -- God, family, work. Look at what has happened, we don't have purpose. Look what has happened with our children. I have 12 grandchildren and six children. There's suicide, mental health, all of these things are happening because we don't have purpose. We've got to move closer to God, and we've got to work, because working is so important, because you need a reason.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Thank you so much. Great to see you.\par \par \uc2 All right final thoughts when we return.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We had an amazing show here in Houston, an incredible crowd, an incredible team. America, we have a country to save. We had incredible power with the Hispanic community across this country. Don't marginalize them, and certainly don't characterize at them as one voting bloc or another. Amazing people.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for watching. It's America now and forever.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020221027eiaq00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Many Revealing Moments At The Big Fetterman Debate; Alarming Pickaxe Incident Caught On Video; Powerful People Want To Stop Elon's \uc2 Twitter\uc2  Deal; Musician Shocks Viewers With Live Genital Stunt; Liberal Democrats Withdraw Their Letter To Biden That Urged Him To Rethink His Ukraine Strategy; State-Sanctioned Murder Of Vulnerable People\b0\par\par\uc2 Tucker Carlson, Matt Finn, Trace Gallagher, Tulsi Gabbard \par \uc2 7,017 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2022\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: Tucker Carlson Tonight\par \uc2 TCARL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Well, that was funny, and we're going to give Columbus a harder look.\par \par \uc2 Char from Wisconsin. Is that a real name? Char?\par \par \uc2 "Jesse politics aside, are you more excited about the \uc2 Phillies\uc2  or the Eagles?" Obviously, the Eagles, obviously. Go fighting.\par \par \uc2 Tucker is next. This is my world.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Good evening and welcome to TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT. Good night, everybody.\par \par \uc2 Two days before the Democratic Senate primary in Pennsylvania back in May, staffers for the \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  campaign announced that their candidate had tragically suffered a stroke, but no problem. In a written statement purportedly written by \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  himself from the hospital, Fetterman announced that he was absolutely fine.\par \par \uc2 "I'm feeling much better," the statement read. "Doctors tell me I didn't suffer any cognitive damage." Okay, so the primary continued as planned with Fetterman's name on the ballot and Fetterman won. He became the Democratic nominee and that was the last that most voters heard about \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 's stroke.\par \par \uc2 For months, Fetterman remained in semi-seclusion. Then as the campaign progressed and the polls tightened, he began to venture out. He had no choice, and video clips surfaced of Fetterman speaking at rallies in what seemed to be a bizarre and highly disjointed way. Some began to wonder if he'd really suffered "no cognitive damage" from his stroke.\par \par \uc2 It was at this point that Fetterman's personal physician, a man called Clifford Chen, who also happened to be a campaign donor to him and other Democrats, rushed forward to bring science to bear on this question.\par \par \uc2 In Clifford Chen's considered opinion as a respected medical professional who works at a major research university, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  was absolutely fine. Fetterman was "recovering well" from his stroke. He had "no work restrictions and can work full duty in public office."\par \par \uc2 In other words, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  was as sharp and as healthy as you or me, as anyone in America. In fact, more so, ready for the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman's wife, who presumably would know, seconded this assessment and attacked anyone who disagreed -- so did a group of Democratic officeholders who wrote a piece in "The Huffington Post" about how their own strokes had only enhanced their public service.\par \par \uc2 A stroke? No big deal. It's a good thing, actually, ought to be a prerequisite for service in the Senate. For their part, most of the reporters who covered \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  day-to-day worked hard to calm concerns about his health.\par \par \uc2 Is \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  a silver-tongued wordsmith? No, they conceded, he never has been, but brain damaged? Come on. Don't be a bigot. That's ableist.\par \par \uc2 Until last night, that's pretty much where things stood. Some people, mostly Republicans, thought \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  might not be mentally fit to work in the Senate. Others, mostly Democrats, agreed with Clifford Chen, his doctor, that Fetterman was absolutely fine.\par \par \uc2 It was a neat partisan split. Then, Fetterman appeared on stage for his first and only debate and settled this question for all time. \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , it turns out, is not capable of driving a car. He should not be allowed to operate a microwave oven. There is no chance that under any imaginable circumstances, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  could "serve in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 ." It's not a close call. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MODERATOR: You're running for a seat that could decide the balance of power in Washington. What qualifies you to be a US senator? You have 60 seconds.\par \par \uc2 JOHN FETTERMAN\uc2  (D), PENNSYLVANIA SENATE CANDIDATE: Hi. Good night, everybody.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: What? That was the moment, right at the top that you know, this was not a debate like the debates you'd seen before. Most of it feel pretty scripted and in fact, this debate actually was scripted. \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  had a script. He was reading it, but he was still incapable of following that script.\par \par \uc2 Here, for example, is how Fetterman responded to maybe the most obvious question of the night, one he knew was coming and of course, would have prepared for it. Here's his answer.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MODERATOR: You're saying tonight that you support fracking, that you've always supported fracking, but there is that 2018 interview that you said, "I don't support fracking at all." So, how do you square the two?\par \par \uc2 FETTERMAN: Oh, I do support fracking and I don't -- I don't -- I support fracking and I stand and I do support fracking.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Okay, so a lot of conclusions here. The most obvious, why is Clifford Chen still practicing Medicine? If you're a physician, are you allowed to lie for partisan reasons? Don't we have enough of that in this country? Should doctors be allowed to do that? He clearly was lying.\par \par \uc2 That's not a man who can work with no restrictions in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 . Far from it. And everyone watching, every honest person, would come to that conclusion. We could play you a lot of clips like that, probably seen them already today, but not everyone is an honest person and to prove it, we're going to show you how MSNBC covered this debate the moment it ended.\par \par \uc2 Here is "New York" Magazine's Rebecca Traister.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REBECCA TRAISTER, "NEW YORK" MAGAZINE: Clearly, this was a candidate who was feeling stress and there was such intense scrutiny, often ableist scrutiny on how he was going to communicate, and he just did a debate in front of, you know, the nation, you know, an audience of anyone who could listen and it was so transparent.\par \par \uc2 He did fumble. He did make verbal mistakes, you know, and it was all on view, but, you know, I think it's also really interesting. You played a lot of clips. There were moments where he was really strong, including that \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  quip, including his very fluent and direct response on raising the minimum wage, I thought was a really strong moment.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, we just keep clips like that around just for future historians to assess what went wrong in America and we wanted the hackiest possible response, the most dishonest assessment ever offered of any public event, and we just played it for you. He was facing ableist scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 Because we literally can't control ourselves, you just heard her say that Fetterman had a strong answer to a question. Talk about patronizing, by the way. Well, we thought we'd go and check what was his answer. You can assess for yourself whether this was "strong." Here it is.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MODERATOR: What do you say to small business owners who have told us that if the minimum wage were increased to $15.00 an hour, it would put them out of business? You have 30 seconds.\par \par \uc2 FETTERMAN: We all have to make sure that everyone that works is able to -- that's -- that's the most American bargain that if you work full time, you should be able to live in dignity, is well true, and I believe they haven't, have any businesses being -- being -- we can't have businesses being subsidized by not paying individuals that just simply can't afford to pay their own way.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Again, we could fill the hour recapping \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 's sad responses, but it's not really that surprising. Anyone who's been following \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  for the past five months, you knew that he was profoundly cognitively impaired and it turns out he is.\par \par \uc2 So, you learn really not that much new about him. What you learn is that everyone around him, from his doctor to his wife to the media, to the Democratic Party, they're all liars and they all just got caught lying.\par \par \uc2 The debate went on and on and on like this. During Dr. Oz's closing statement, Fetterman began shouting uncontrollably about Social Security until the moderator hushed him. Really? Look it up.\par \par \uc2 The effect over an hour is to make you feel very sad for \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 . This is humiliating. The guy looked exactly like Billy Bob Thornton in the movie "Slingblade." He really did. He couldn't even read the canned lines his staff was writing for him. It was pathetic. You do wonder about his wife, as you do about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's wife. It seems cruel to do this to a man, even for political power.\par \par \uc2 But again, it's the media who cover \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , who should be the most ashamed. They've known the truth for months. With only one exception, that would be NBC reporter, Dasha Burns, the media lied to voters about it. We don't know anything about Dasha Burns, but she at least tried to be sort of honest. Here's what she said after meeting \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DASHA BURNS, NBC NEWS REPORTER: You'll hear he also still has some problems, some challenges with speech and I'll say, Katy, that just in some of the small talk prior to the interview, before the closed captioning was up and running, it did seem that he had a hard time understanding our conversations.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Oh, that's not allowed. Here you have a young reporter who clearly doesn't know the rules. No matter what you actually see or experience or report, you can't reveal anything that might hurt the fortunes of the Democratic Party; that might slow down the team.\par \par \uc2 So, clearly Dasha Burns hadn't gotten that memo and for daring to say that, for honestly reporting what she saw, liberals tried to destroy her.\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Traister again, of "New York" Magazine, said Fetterman "is not at all impaired. He understands everything." Molly Jong-Fast said she spoke to Fetterman and, "He understood everything I was saying and he was funny."\par \par \uc2 Podcast host Kara Swisher -- this is like the worst people on social media -- wrote this on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , "Sorry to say, but I talked to @JohnFetterman for over an hour without stop or any aides and this is just nonsense. Maybe this reporter is just bad at small talk." Blame the girl, will you, Kara Swisher? Of course.\par \par \uc2 And then Charlotte Alter of "Time" Magazine, whatever that is, also interviewed Fetterman recently. She knew perfectly well he is incapacitated, they all did.\par \par \uc2 But Charlotte Alter decided to cover for \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  because supporting a Democratic Party is, of course, her job. In the hours before the debate, Charlotte Alter did the bidding, the direct bidding of the Fetterman campaign, by trying to lower expectations. That was their goal, and she worked on their behalf.\par \par \uc2 "Fetterman has never been a good debater." Alter added, "Everyone will be watching for Fetterman stroke symptoms. I can tell you already what they are. He sometimes says the slightly wrong word or conjugates something the wrong way."\par \par \uc2 Okay. They're not embarrassed. They're caught working for a Democratic Senate campaign and they just shrug it off