le of weeks here.\par \par \uc2 So, let's bring in Sandra Smith, who's joining us, co-host of "AMERICA REPORT". Sandra, great to have you here.\par \par \uc2 SANDRA SMITH, FOX NEWS CHANNEL ANCHOR (on camera): Hi, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Hi, there.\par \par \uc2 You know, it's pretty tough to turn the ship at this point. But we see a pretty significant effort trying to do that for the Democrat.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: And it's really remarkable when you read through that piece. You mentioned \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  reading about fearing a new shellacking, and Democrats are rushing for an economic message. Not a new economic, and economic message.\par \par \uc2 And when I dig through this piece, a lengthy piece, I don't find the message. So, they're still looking 14 days out from Election Day, if anything. What this told me is, because the piece quotes for veteran Democratic strategists, who published a piece in The American Prospect, which is a liberal magazine, it -- they are pleading with Democrats to find this new message.\par \par \uc2 But, what they're saying is empathize with the voters, acknowledge the pain that they're feeling. We have this new LendingClub Survey that just came out. This shows 63 percent of people in this country are living paycheck to paycheck right now.\par \par \uc2 I spoke to a man the other day who owns a regional energy company in the northeast, who's -- he said he's never seen anything like it. He fears his customers who he's known for 26 years might not make it.\par \par \uc2 They're choosing between rent, and their mortgage, and heating their homes. He's predicting foreclosures.\par \par \uc2 I spoke to a woman in Maine who for a nonprofit, who tries to help these people get through the winter. She says some of them are choosing between groceries or heating their homes.\par \par \uc2 I mean, it's a brutal environment out there. We haven't even really entered the heating season yet. And you've already gotten that gas prices