chul\uc2 ? But it's probably too late for her. She is losing to a Republican in New York.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania is almost as Democratic as New York is, but the Lieutenant Governor now running for Senate there, John Fetterman, is also losing for the same reasons, we guess. His challenger is Dr. Mehmet Oz who joins us .\par \par \uc2 Dr. Oz, thank you very much for coming on.\par \par \uc2 DR. MEHMET OZ (R), PENNSYLVANIA GUBERNATORIAL CANDIDATE: Good to be here.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, in the case of Fetterman since he is currently an officeholder, he can be traced to very specific policies that have increased violent crime in the State of Pennsylvania. Did they not think that anyone was going to notice that when they put this man up for office?\par \par \uc2 OZ: Well, it's shocking when you hear Krasner speak there about a city he thinks he's protecting, but I've been in Philadelphia a lot during this campaign. I live in Philly. I went to school in West Philly and when you actually talked to the people there, what they say is they don't want to be part of a White woke experiment, a social experiment where they're left with the consequences.\par \par \uc2 And Fetterman, to your point, said that if you had a magic wand to do anything he wanted to, his goal would be to release murderers from life in prison.\par \par \uc2 Now, Tucker, can you imagine having a magic wand to do anything you want. I mean, you could take care of inflation, although you don't need a magic wand for that, but there are lots of things you could do, but releasing murderers from life in prison without asking the families what they think and oftentimes voting against the other members of the Parole Board, even other Democrats is not aligned with the values of Pennsylvanians, yet, that's the position he has taken.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So many Pennsylvanians have died of fentanyl OD and opioid more broadly, but fentanyl, I would say specifically in the last year, that it really is -- the numbers are almost beyond belief. And yet, I don't think stopping fentanyl importation, dealing punishing fentanyl peddlers is a feature of any Democratic campaign. Why is that?\par \par \uc2 OZ: Because they're ignoring the humanitarian crisis they have created with feckless policies on the border. They have funded cartels inadvertently, who make money trafficking human beings, take the money, buy fentanyl from China. They don't say anything to China about that, by the way.\par \par \uc2 The fentanyl was brought to America like pieces of candy and unfortunately, ends up in people's mailboxes. But Fetterman goes beyond that. That's what all the Democrats do.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman says, "I want to legalize all drugs. I want heroin injection sites." And he actually embraced a measure in Oregon, which was enacted two years ago with exactly those rules and listen carefully, this is critical. Forty percent increase in overdose death rates, that's to be expected if you legalize all drugs.\par \par \uc2 But here is the part that catches me, 50 percent increase in homicides. You create a lawless environment, police aren't allowed to do their job, which is to confiscate narcotics. And this is the world that he is trying to create for us.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, if you're bothered by this, and I was bothered enough to run against them, please go to doctoroz.com and support me because the Democratic Party doesn't even know this about him. They're just trying to get the 51st Senate seat, so they're pouring money into Pennsylvania. So, doctoroz.com will at least give me some support against them.\par \par \uc2 But we're going to win on the issues just like all the Republicans that you've mentioned today. The debate we're having tomorrow night is going to reinforce John Fetterman's radical positions.\par \par \uc2 The momentum we have is a direct response of focusing on kitchen table issues -- crime, drugs, we mentioned both at the border, and of course, the economy everyone is focused on although, if you're in Philadelphia right now, you're worried about your life and companies are leaving. Big chains leaving the city because they're done with the experiment.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I've got to just ask you and I'm sure you don't like to go to motive, but it's just -- it's amazing to me, 107,000 Americans die of drug ODs last year and he is a guy promoting drug legalization when we know it will result in more deaths. Why would anyone push an idea like that at a time like this?\par \par \uc2 OZ: Because they're more concerned about the perpetrator or the criminal than the innocent and the victims. They don't hear the stories that I've been witnessing as I campaign of moms telling me that they've found their children blue and dead because they went on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and signed up for, you know, an over-the-counter pain pill and ended up having fentanyl in it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 OZ: We confiscated seven times more fentanyl in Pennsylvania this quarter than two years ago, according to the State Patrol and by the way, and all the law enforcement groups have endorsed me because they know Fetterman doesn't have their back and I'll fight hard to let them do their job.\par \par \uc2 But Tucker, that's part of the problem. When you talk to the left-leaning politicians and the far left, especially, they don't want the police to do their jobs. They don't want anyone to do their jobs. And they don't want to therefore deal with the consequences of it, so they don't come downtown to the prayer vigils I've attended. They haven't gone to Kensington, which is the largest open air drug market in the country that we created with these bizarre beliefs that you can give people drugs and it's okay.\par \par \uc2 Believe me, taking heroin long term is not a good strategy. You're not going to do well. And because I know that, and I love these people, and I see the divine spark going out in their eyes, I want to take them to detox, put them in rehab, and I'll fund that when I'm in the Senate. Why wouldn't you want that?\par \par \uc2 And again, this is something we should all be rooting for. This should be a bipartisan desire to make the country stable.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I know. It's really stunning to me. And what is also stunning is, I think you're going to win this Senate seat in a Democratic State because of the things you're saying right there, and I appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Oz, thank you.\par \par \uc2 OZ: God bless.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, if you're starting get the sense that these are not ordinary Midterm Elections, you're right. They could determine the course of the country.\par \par \uc2 So for our original series or documentary series, we embedded for months with one campaign that is trying to flip control \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 . The documentary is called "The Candidate: Blake Masters." It is out tomorrow and we got really remarkable access to the candidate. Here's a look at it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Ladies and gentlemen please welcome to the stage, endorsed candidate for Senate in and Arizona, Blake Masters.\par \par \uc2 BLAKE MASTERS (R), ARIZONA SENATE CANDIDATE: Thank you for your support, for making me your Republican nominee to the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 [CHEERING AND APPLAUSE]\par \par \uc2 [BOOING]\par \par \uc2 MASTERS: Most Americans -- no, not most Americans -- all Americans, you're sick.\par \par \uc2 We are sick of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democrats destroying our country.\par \par \uc2 [CHEERING AND APPLAUSE]\par \par \uc2 MASTERS: And soon we're going to send a fighter to DC, and that's me. I am the one. I am the one. We're going to fix it.\par \par \uc2 [CHEERING AND APPLAUSE]\par \par \uc2 MASTERS: You know, if there's one person in Arizona who has done more than anyone to drag this country in the wrong direction, that's Senator Mark Kelly. Kelly.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It's Mark Kelly.\par \par \uc2 MASTERS: That's Senator Mark Kelly.\par \par \uc2 Mark Kelly, he campaigns as a moderate, but he voted as a radical.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You know, the President, has he done a good job do you think?\par \par \uc2 SEN. MARK KELLY (D-AZ): Hey, you know -- I -- you know --\par \par \uc2 MASTERS: Everything about Mark Kelly, you don't know this, everything about this guy is managed by consultants and handlers. Drop an F-bomb. Yay or nay?\par \par \uc2 At least, you weren't here. You're like here. I can -- okay so that's a no. Because if you go here, then I'm like, I've got to do it.\par \par \uc2 Tell me I can't do something unless we're reviewing it.\par \par \uc2 As we head into this General Election, the media, they're going to want to tell you that we live in a closely divided State, and most Arizonans turns out, they want commonsense policy. That's what we're going to do in November.\par \par \uc2 We're going to beat Mark Kelly. We're going to turn this country around --\par \par \uc2 [CHEERING AND APPLAUSE]\par \par \uc2 [BOOING]\par \par \uc2 MASTERS: Let's go.\par \par \uc2 MASTERS: Because remember, me or the vast majority.\par \par \uc2 Thank you and here's to victory in November. God bless you.\par \par \uc2 [CHEERING AND APPLAUSE]\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: You just can't overstate how deeply unappealing most politicians are, even in private, their lines are canned because there's nothing real about them. Fundamentally at the core, they're hollow.\par \par \uc2 Blake Masters is quite an exception to that sad rule. He is interesting. He thinks for himself. He has ideas that in the view of us, anyway, this country badly needs.\par \par \uc2 And for the purposes of this documentary, he gave us remarkable access to his campaign. Like him or not, you will know more about Blake Masters by the end of this than really any politician running this year.\par \par \uc2 It is a great documentary only on FOX Nation.\par \par \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  just got a new COVID booster because every jab offers more protection than the last, that is why they're forcing it on kids now. So how did that work out for \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  of the CDC? Well, we have an update on her condition.\par \par \uc2 We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, it was just a year and a half ago, the Director of the CDC, \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , who claims to be a physician went on MSNBC to say that the COVID shot stops the transmission of COVID.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DR. \uc2 ROCHELLE WALENSKY\uc2 , DIRECTOR, CENTER FOR DISEASE CONTROL: Our data from the CDC today suggest, you know, that vaccinated people do not carry the virus, don't get sick.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: "Vaccinated people do not carry the virus. They don't get sick," said the head of the CDC, and to prove it, Walensky took the shot and the boosters. She took her most recent shot, the omicron specific booster just a month ago and then what happened? You know how the story ends.\par \par \uc2 This week, \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  tested positive for COVID, but she is reportedly grateful for the protection the vaccine provided. Now, why are we telling you the story? For two reasons: One, in order to preserve the credibility of Federal agencies and of our healthcare sector more broadly, \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  should apologize for the misinformation that she spread throughout the American media, A.\par \par \uc2 B., this doesn't work and we should not be pushing it on kids. Now, if \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  wants to get 11 boosters, that's up to her, but kids should not be required to get this as a precondition of being educated in this country. That's insane.\par \par \uc2 Well, the Congressional Black Caucus says its mission is to -- we read the website -- "Ensure that African-Americans and other marginalized communities in the US have the opportunity to achieve the American Dream." Okay, well, that sounds positive.\par \par \uc2 But in fact, that Congressional Black Caucus is completely corrupt as everyone who lives in Washington knows, but worse than that, it is just a Political Action Committee designed to elect Democrats. They don't care about African-Americans and marginalized communities, of course, and we know that for many reasons, but here's the latest. They're currently backing a White Democrat over Jennifer Ruth-Green who is running for Congress in Indiana.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer-Ruth Green joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer-Ruth Green, thanks so much for coming on.\par \par \uc2 Now, you would think, you're African-American, the Congressional Black Caucus would be, I guess, on your side, it's a race-specific group, but why aren't they backing you?\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER-RUTH GREEN (R), INDIANA CONGRESSIONAL CANDIDATE: Thank you very much for having me, Mr. Carlson.\par \par \uc2 The hypocrisy in this decision is so incredibly clear. We see that this is about power and this is about policy. This is about process. This is not about progress.\par \par \uc2 These are the liberal elites who want to have power and are focused on retaining it. And so, their decision to back my opponent is hypocritical at best, BECAUSE largely when you think about the fact that I understand the Black cultural experience better than any White men ever will, I understand the growth that needs to occur. I understand what needs to happen and I'm committed as a Black woman and as an Asian-American woman, to progressive minorities in our country, I seem like the very clear choice.\par \par \uc2 But because they want power over politics, the hypocrisy continues to be loud and proud.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, maybe you know how corrupt they are. Maybe that's why they don't want to back you.\par \par \uc2 GREEN: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 I mean, I think --\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, I'm sorry, go ahead.\par \par \uc2 GREEN: You know, as I am sitting in our district, we have a third of our people in Gary, Indiana who are some poverty level. We have a third of the people in Gary, Indiana who live in food deserts. And so here are people who are hurting.\par \par \uc2 And so the economy that Congressman Frank Mrvan has voted for has consistently put them in a place where they have to choose between gas and groceries, where Congressman Frank Mrvan has voted for $3 trillion in spending and has spent their grandkids' money, and these are African- Americans who are clearly hurting and he has zero regard for them, and they are focused on trying the \uc2 CBC\uc2 , specifically, focus on trying to elect -- continue to elect him because overall, they believe he's doing a good job.\par \par \uc2 But I can just tell you this, Mr. Carlson, there is a line a mile-and-a- half long of cars that sit outside my headquarters, people who need to get to the food pantry who need help and this is the America that the Congressional Black Caucus wants to act as if it is helping Black people and it is very clearly not in Indiana's first congressional district.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, I have been to Gary, Indiana. It's one of the toughest places I've ever been in my life in this or any other countries overwhelmingly African-American. It's really bad, I would say.\par \par \uc2 What has the Democratic Party done for Gary, Indiana, ever?\par \par \uc2 GREEN: You know what? We have some amazing people that live in Gary, Indiana.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, I believe that.\par \par \uc2 GREEN: I have some amazing friends, some people that love God, love others, want to serve both and I am proud to have Gary, Indiana in our district.\par \par \uc2 But when I think about the reality of people that are hurting because of these economic choices, this is a plan that has no action behind it. The Congressman has no plan.\par \par \uc2 But if you go to JRG.gop, you will see a plan, a plan to help figure out the economic processes that need to move forward and I am disappointed in the hypocrisy that the Congressional Black Caucus continues to provide because they don't have a plan and they would rather continue to crush people because it's all about again, their power and the liberal elites versus regular America, people who want to stay in power, although they are doing absolutely nothing to make progress on the mission that they continue to talk about.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, of course. If they cared, they'd be talking about Gary, Indiana and not Ukraine, but they don't care. That's obvious.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer-Ruth Green, I appreciate your coming on tonight.\par \par \uc2 GREEN: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Good luck.\par \par \uc2 GREEN: Thank you, sir.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So we pretty much stopped playing video of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  breaking down in public and saying bizarre things, garbled sentences, but the clip we're about to show you we just could not resist because it's just too unbelievable. So, stay tuned for that.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the media are casually preparing Americans for nuclear war like it's no big deal. You know, inflation, nuclear war, just the things a country faces. Really? We're going to give you an update on where we are in that war, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So if you're in the media, you sit down and interview a President in his first term, you don't typically ask if you're going to run for reelection, because they all do because that's who they are, running for election is the whole point of going into politics.\par \par \uc2 And yet Biden sat down with MSNBC the other day, and they asked him "Are you going to run again?" And the implication is maybe you've got such profound cognitive decline that you can't run again, and as if to prove that, in fact, yes, I'm completely demented. I'm a mannequin at this point, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , nodded off in the middle of the interview.\par \par \uc2 We're not making this up. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I have not made that formal decision, but it's my intention. My intention to run again. And we have time to make that decision.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Dr. Biden is for it. Mr. President?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Dr. Biden thinks that -- my wife thinks that -- that I -- that we're -- that we're doing something very important.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Whoa. He literally nodded it out in the middle of an answer about whether he was running again and right before he nodded out, he said, oh yes, I'm probably going to run again.\par \par \uc2 So take three steps back. Only a guy who was supremely confident in the effectiveness of voter fraud could do something like that, because like, he is not even trying, uh, huh? Yes, I'm running again. Yes, Dr. Biden, no, she is a doctor, really?\par \par \uc2 And then, because everything with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can in fact, get weirder, he blindly announced he could drop dead at any time. He actually said that. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Am I slowing up? Am I -- I don't have the same pace or, you know, and that old joke, you know, everybody talks about the -- you know, the new 70s and 50s and all that stuff. You know, I -- you know, it could be -- I'm a great respecter of fate. I could get a disease tomorrow. I could, you know, drop dead tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, I could drop dead tomorrow. Eighty-one million votes. He got 81 million, without even campaigning from his basement in Delaware, he got 81 million votes. Shut up. You have to believe that Russia and insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 It is like it is not even real. But it is real.\par \par \uc2 Well, suddenly, you've seen a lot of stories about nuclear war. Well, we could have a nuclear war, not a