nd roofs over our head, and that's what we're fighting for.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You bet. Kelly, I'm very, very excited about this race. I cannot wait to see what happens on election night. It's going to be a late night because of the time difference in Alaska, but you go out there and you keep doing what you're doing. I think you're going to win this, and we're with you all the way. Thanks so much, Kelly.\par \par \uc2 Oh, wow, another surprise shoutout for THE INGRAHAM ANGLE'S fifth anniversary is up next. I can't wait to find out who it is. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, nine more days until THE INGRAHAM ANGLE'S big five- year anniversary. I cannot believe it. It's crazy. Now, you just heard from Jason Chaffetz and THE FIVE. My team has more surprise shoutouts from friends of the show, so let's check out another.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 NEWT GINGRICH\uc2 , FORMER SPEAKER OF THE HOUSE: Laura, it's hard to believe that this is the fifth anniversary of your show, but I can tell you that day in and day out, every chance I get, I'm amazed at how you combine humor and anger and revelations about news in a way that nobody else on television can match. You picked up something somewhere that makes you truly unique. And I think it's a great tribute to you that your audience loves you, sticks with you, looks forward to hearing from you. And I can tell you as one of your occasional guests, I always find it fascinating to be with you, and I look forward to another five years of your show.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: \uc2 Newt Gingrich\uc2 , what a man and what a dear friend, and I have no words to respond to that. That's just beyond generous. This is a show that is possible only because of our team, so those words are directed at the larger INGRAHAM ANGLE team, and you know who you are.\par \par \uc2 All right, don't forget, set your DVR for next Wednesday night, October 26th, when THE INGRAHAM ANGLE hits the road and heads to Houston, Texas, for our first Retaking America townhall. You're not going to want to miss it.\par \par \uc2 And Greg Gutfeld takes it all from here.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020221022eial00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Republican Candidate For Governor Of New York, \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  Talks To Tucker; \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  Sentenced To Four Months In Prison For Contempt Of Congress; White House Can't Tolerate A Free And Open Internet; The Most Interesting Republican Candidates This Cycle Are Political Outsiders; Up To Date And Accurate Voter Data Is Essential To Ensure Confidence In Our Future Elections\b0\par\par\uc2 Tucker Carlson \par \uc2 7,917 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 October 2022\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: Tucker Carlson Tonight\par \uc2 TCARL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: It was just right there.\par \par \uc2 Butch from Kempton, you don't hear Butch as a name much anymore. Does everyone at FOX News get along off camera as well as they appear on camera?\par \par \uc2 Now, Julie and I hate each other. Hate each other.\par \par \uc2 JULIE BANDERAS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL ANCHOR: He is so annoying.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Well, that's all for tonight.\par \par \uc2 Tucker is next up. I am Watters and this is my world.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  was not at the Capitol Building on January 6th. He didn't break any laws that day, he is not even accused of breaking any laws that day, but he was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's chief political adviser.\par \par \uc2 So today, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  was sentenced to nearly half a year in prison by the January 6 Committee. Why? Well, because in 2022, the Democratic Party puts its political opponents in jail. That's why.\par \par \uc2 In a moment, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  will join us for his first interview since the sentence was handed down.\par \par \uc2 But first, good evening and welcome to TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT.\par \par \uc2 It feels like permanent Washington has always hated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But actually that's not true.\par \par \uc2 For years, Trump was considered merely a joke in DC, a celebrity sideshow, people were happy to have him to the \uc2 White House Correspondents\uc2 ' Dinner.\par \par \uc2 And that was true as late as the 2016 primaries. There were still many professional Republicans, people you wouldn't expect, people like Bill Kristol, Joe Scarborough, people were making highly positive noises about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And then it changed in a moment. It changed on February 13th of that year, at the Republican debate in Greenville, South Carolina. That's when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  criticized the Iraq War: "Obviously, the war in Iraq was a big fat mistake," he said. And of course, by that point, it certainly was obvious that it was a mistake, but that didn't mean you were allowed to admit it in Washington, you weren't.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of lobbyists, think-tank analysts, hack beltway journalists owed their salaries and their reputations to perpetuating the lie that American foreign policy was succeeding. Everything was fine.\par \par \uc2 No one really believed that. The evidence was too strong on the other side, but everyone had to say it. Too many careers were at stake.\par \par \uc2 And yet suddenly, here was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  refusing to play along, giving away the game in public, on TV. The reaction to this in DC was violent and immediate. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  must be stopped. If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was going to criticize the Iraq war as a Republican, God knows what else he might say.\par \par \uc2 The Never Trump Movement that resulted from that year's South Carolina debate and that is where it began, that movement went on to do all kinds of things, including subverting the rule of law in this country, as well as entire Federal agencies.\par \par \uc2 But one of its first efforts was a little remembered spoiler campaign designed to siphon votes from Trump in the General Election. A group of liberals in Washington and formerly headed by Bill Kristol, recruited a longtime Federal bureaucrat called Evan McMullin and convinced him to run for President.\par \par \uc2 McMullin didn't seem like a presidential candidate. He was 40 years old, never married and very obviously odd, very odd. He had no trouble raising money. There are a lot of liberals happy to write him checks.\par \par \uc2 The problem was voters, they were not impressed by Evan McMullin at all. By the end, he won half of one percent of the popular total and zero electoral votes and he was soon forgotten except on Wikipedia.\par \par \uc2 And yes, and here's the point, six years later, Evan McMullin has reemerged. He is running for Senate in the State of Utah against incumbent \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2 , and amazingly, he could win, he could actually win.\par \par \uc2 Now, if McMullin does win, his vote could very well give Democrats control the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 . How did this happen? How is this possible, you wonder? It doesn't make sense. Utah is a conservative, highly Republican State. Evan McMullin has the same politics and worldview as \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 . He is a Liberal Democrat.\par \par \uc2 Ah, but he is not running as a Liberal Democrat and that's the key to his success this year. Evan McMullin is running instead as an Independent and many voters appear to be under the impression that he actually is Independent, but he is not. That's a lie -- a transparent lie.\par \par \uc2 Evan McMullin is roughly as Independent as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is. He is considerably less independent than say \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 . Evan McMullin is anything but Independent, he is entirely controlled and has always been.\par \par \uc2 McMullin even uses the Democratic Party's fundraising platform Act Blue. His campaign has paid nearly $2 million to Democratic Party consulting services in the last year alone. That would include Precision Strategies, cofounded by a Biden adviser. Other firms include Foundation Strategies, Blueprint Public Affairs, and KMM Strategy. These are all partisan Democratic Party firms.\par \par \uc2 In politics, you pick a side in the consultants you hire, and Evan McMullin has picked his side, the Democratic side.\par \par \uc2 Not surprisingly, the creepy liberals at The Lincoln Project who lie for a living are busy pretending that Evan McMullin is not one of them, oh no. "Republicans," they write, " Evan McMullin truly represents your values." Really? Which values are those?\par \par \uc2 Does Evan McMullin oppose amnesty for illegal migrants? Does he oppose race crazed teachers unions? Does he oppose even \uc2 Tony Fauci\uc2 ? No, of course not. Evan McMullin is fully on board with every anti-family scheme the Democratic Party has dreamed up over the last decade. As a supposedly faithful Mormon, he can't even acknowledge that Roe v. Wade was a bad decision. He is a neoliberal robot. There is nothing Independent about him.\par \par \uc2 Watch him read the Democratic Party's talking points, for example, on abortion.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EVAN MCMULLIN (I), UTAH SENATORIAL CANDIDATE: I am committed to the sanctity of life, but I think that means the lives of women, that means the lives of the unborn, of course, and it means the lives of children and I think we've got to take a more comprehensive approach to that.\par \par \uc2 MEHDI HASAN, MSNBC HOST: But just to be clear, you don't support overturning Roe v. Wade anymore as you did in 2016? I'm just trying to get clarity.\par \par \uc2 MCMULLIN: I do not -- I do not think that that is the way for the country to move forward on this issue.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Oh, so keeping Roe v. Wade is the way for the country to move forward. But of course, Roe v. Wade, whatever you think of it, froze everything in amber in 1973 and imposed the most radically pro-abortion regime from the Courts on all 50 States. So of course, you can't move forward under Roe v. Wade in either direction. This doesn't make sense. It's effectively pro-abortion.\par \par \uc2 You don't typically hear Mormons talk like that. And in fact, Evan McMullin, as you just heard, suggested, did not used to talk like this. In fact, back in 2016, he denounced \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the guy who would eventually get Roe v. Wade overturned, because he said Trump wasn't pro-life enough.\par \par \uc2 "I'm the only pro-life candidate in the race." McMullin wrote in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Four years later, after Trump's successfully appointed several pro-life Justices to the Supreme Court who overturned Roe v. Wade, McMullin has clarified what he means when he says pro-life. It turns out being pro-life has nothing to do with protecting children.\par \par \uc2 Here is what McMullin said: "You aren't actually pro-life if you can't say black lives matter." Oh, right. \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2 , which is an explicitly pro-choice organization. You following all this? It doesn't make any sense. He is a Liberal Democrat.\par \par \uc2 And it would be fine if he ran as one. Utah voters should know what they're voting for and he should be honest about who he is.\par \par \uc2 If you pay any attention at all to McMullin's last three years in, "public life," it's very obvious. In 2020, he endorsed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  because he cares about Republican values. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCMULLIN: For many, choosing between these two Americas will require us to do something we've never done before, crossing party lines to support a unifying presidential candidate of another party.\par \par \uc2 I believe Joe to be an honorable Patriot who is loyal to the Republic.\par \par \uc2 And that's why I plan to put country over party and in November, cast my vote for Joe.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: He is putting country over party by voting for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who not one time in his entire life has put country over party.\par \par \uc2 So after endorsing Biden for office, and again, lots of people did, that's okay, but don't call it Independent. Evan McMullin did not act independently, just the opposite. He proceeded to cred his personal opinions directly from \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  and the other geniuses in the White House PR office.\par \par \uc2 There isn't a stupid Democratic buzz phrase he didn't use and then overuse again, and again, and again. We could give you a million examples. Here is one. Watch him accuse, "A majority of House Republicans" who voted to overturn the election results.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCMULLIN: And then to see that violent, that deadly insurrection happen that threatened our democracy and then to watch a majority of House Republicans still vote to overturn the results of the election, all of that just describes, of course, a party that is sick, that is rotten to the core.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Okay, so he's an MSNBC contributor, that's what he is. And if the voters of Utah want to elect one, they should just elect Joe Reid, at least she is not pretending to be something that she is not, and she is also probably a little smarter than Evan McMullin.\par \par \uc2 No one voted to overturn the results of the election actually, not a majority of House Republicans. What happened is that Republicans did exactly what Democrats did in 1969, in 2001, in 2005, in 2017. Republicans objected to the certification of the results pending an audit.\par \par \uc2 Hmm. That's what actually happened. We watched.\par \par \uc2 But McMullin doesn't mention 1969, 2001, 2005, or 2017 because he is just repeating talking points he gets from his handlers in the Democratic Party, and he has been doing this for years. Here he is accusing millions of Republican voters of racism.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCMULLIN: There is a taboo within the Republican Party about attacking racism in America and I know that that's the case because when you do it as a conservative, you get attacked by elements within the party.\par \par \uc2 There is an element of the Republican base that is racist.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes. "There's a huge taboo in America against opposing racism." We've organized the entire society on a bipartisan basis to oppose racism, but somehow Evan McMullin is the only man brave enough to oppose racism in public. He's also against polio and car crashes.\par \par \uc2 The guy is a moron, well he is false. There is a lot of morons in politics, he is probably not the stupidest person in politics, Mazie Hirono still serves in the Senate, but he's a fraud.\par \par \uc2 If he reminds you of anyone else, a guy pretending to be Republican so he can undermine his own voters once he gets an office, actually he sounds little bit like \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , the other senator from Utah.\par \par \uc2 In a recent debate with \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2 , McMullin just came out and said it. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCMULLIN: Senator Romney has worked hard and consistently over the past three years. I think it's important. He works with Republicans and Democrats, Senator Lee, to deliver for Utah, and he voted in favor of the Bipartisan Infrastructure Bill that you voted against.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Right. So look, if voters in Utah want to elect a Liberal Democrat if they want to elect another \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , and if they think that \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 's politics or Evan McMullin's politics represent the politics of the families of Utah, then go ahead and do it.\par \par \uc2 But don't lie. Be transparent. Say who you are. You are a Liberal Democrat.\par \par \uc2 So, that's the update from Utah.\par \par \uc2 We want to go to New York, where something equally surprising is happening. Something surprising in a good way.\par \par \uc2 So New York is an overwhelmingly Democratic State. No Republican is going to get elected Governor of New York, obviously. But this year, a Republican looks like he may be elected Governor of New York.\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  is running against \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 . She is currently the Governor of New York. She has never been elected, she was appointed after they threw the old guy out for some kind of sex crime that no one ever really explained.\par \par \uc2 Hochul has done a lot to make the State even worse, particularly New York City, which is now dirtier and more dangerous than a lot of third world cities, much dirtier and much more dangerous.\par \par \uc2 This year in New York City, robberies are up 34 percent, felony assaults are up 14 percent, grand larceny 40 percent, motor vehicle theft 36 percent. Murders in the subway system are as high as they'd been in a quarter century. So, that's the population center of the State that \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  runs.\par \par \uc2 Now before you say, well, maybe she's not responsible for all this. Of course she is not responsible for all of it, but she is responsible for the change that made the worst crimes possible and that would be New York's so- called bail reform law. That law lets criminals out on the street immediately and \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  supports it.\par \par \uc2 Why does she support that? We're not sure because she will not debate \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So, what is she spending your time doing? Improving New York? Cleaning up the Calcutta-like encampments in Midtown? Actually, they're far worse than anything in Calcutta right now. No, she is not doing anything to make the State better, instead, she is dividing it and attacking people who are "unvaccinated." Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 KATHY HOCHUL\uc2  (D-NY): I wear my vaccinated necklace all the time to say "I'm vaccinated," all of you. Yes, I know. You're vaccinated. You're the smart ones. But you know, there's people out there who aren't listening to God and what God wants. You know this. You know who they are.\par \par \uc2 I need you to be my apostles. I need you to go out and talk about it and say, "We owe this to each other. We love each other." Jesus taught us to love one another, and how do you show that love, but to care about each other enough to say, please get vaccinated because I love you. I want you to live.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: This woman is a joke. She is an embarrassment. That might be the most embarrassing tape ever shot of a sitting Governor, even an unelected Governor. And the truth is, it has done nothing.\par \par \uc2 Sermons like that have done nothing to improve the condition of New York, not in the city and not upstate, and that's why people are leaving New York by the thousands for Florida and Texas and Tennessee. Why? Because it's too expensive, it is too dirty, and above all, it's too dangerous. People are getting hurt by crime.\par \par \uc2 That includes your political opponent by the way, \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , whose life intersected with crime earlier this year. Someone attacked him during a campaign event. And earlier this month, a gunman opened fire outside his home on Long Island. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: A gunman opened fire outside the family's Long Island home.\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 LEE ZELDIN\uc2  (R-NY): Grazed here and then the bullet was found right here.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: The Congressman and his wife were away campaigning, but his daughters were in the kitchen when they heard gunfire. They hid in the bathroom and called for help.\par \par \uc2 Two 17-year-olds outside were shot and took cover in the front yard. The shooter got away.\par \par \uc2 Police say it was a drive-by shooting not linked to the Zeldin's except for the random location perilously close to where they live.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Now, what's the link? It could have been anybody. That's kind of the point. Living in New York now is dangerous. That State needs new leadership and it looks like it's about to get it.\par \par \uc2 As we told you, \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  is running for Governor. A new poll today, an Independent Coefficient Survey shows Zeldin leading the incumbent in the race for the first time.\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  joins us now.\par \par \uc2 Congressman, thank you so much for coming on.\par \par \uc2 It is pretty remarkable, not that we didn't have faith in you as a person, but I mean, it's an overwhelmingly Democratic State, and you're now winning the Governor's race.\par \par \uc2 First, congratulations. Second, what do you attribute this to?\par \par \uc2 ZELDIN: I mean, you have a Governor who is just not doing a good job. She is unlikable. She's corrupt. She is pandering to criminals. She is pandering to tax and spend liberals. She is advancing woke policies as opposed to just focusing on what is most important to New York voters.\par \par \uc2 If she was tackling rising crime, if she was tackling skyrocketing costs, then this might be a different campaign. But here we are talking about how we need to remove District Attorneys when they refuse to enforce the law. We don't have recall elections in New York, but the Governor does have the Constitutional Authority to get rid of a DA who refuses to do their job.\par \par \uc2 We're over here talking about the need to get rid of cashless bail and some of these other pro-criminal laws and we need to support our men and women in law enforcement who are being hung out to dry, getting the handcuffs thrown on them as opposed to putting the handcuffs on criminals.\par \par \uc2 We have a State ban on the safe extraction of natural gas and now \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  wants to get rid of all gas-powered vehicles here over the course of the next decade.\par \par \uc2 We just had the new CDC guidance come out where they are adding the COVID vaccine into their list, and you have a Governor who is talking about as a possible consideration. Her past remarks have indicated that maybe she would mandate that for kids, but we already have it being required on college students, and we have people who are getting fired for their refusal to get the COVID vaccine like our healthcare workers who used to be hailed as heroes now treated as zeros.\par \par \uc2 I'm somebody who believes that there should be no COVID vaccine on anyone, whether it's grade school, higher ed, employment or otherwise, and everyone who should was fired should be getting their jobs back with back pay.\par \par \uc2 So the contrast is clear and even Democrats and Independents are saying, "You know what? We have to go in a new direction or to save this State. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  has to go," and she will on November 8th.\par \par \uc2 COOPER: It sounds like she will. It's just a remarkable story. It kind of comes out of nowhere, because again, it's so overwhelmingly Democratic. It almost seems like she is trying to wreck the State.\par \par \uc2 ZELDIN: Where we are out here campaigning our tails off to earn the support of voters to do our part to save the State, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  right now is crawling across the finish line. She is trying to survive this campaign. And clearly, her goal here is to save \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  and the average voter out there in New York hitting their breaking point in the State.\par \par \uc2 Listen, there's a reason why New York leads the entire nation in population loss, Tucker, and I don't even think that \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  can finish this sentence that New York leads the entire nation in population loss because - - and if you can't finish that sentence, no one is going to ever expect you to actually fix this and a lot of people pick up on it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So Nicely put. Wow. Congratulations, Congressman \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  of New York. Hopefully the next Governor, it looks like you will be. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 ZELDIN: Thank you, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  committed no crimes on January 6th, the whatsoever \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's chief political adviser, and effectively for that he was just sentenced to prison for refusing to comply with the January 6 Committee.\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  joins us for his first interview since that sentencing. That's next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  had nothing to do with January 6th. He wasn't there. He committed no crime. But that didn't stop the January 6 Committee from trying to destroy him anyway.\par \par \uc2 Today, Bannon was sentenced to four months in Federal Prison at the request of that Committee. As Congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  has pointed out, the Department of Justice official who prosecuted \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , a man called Matthew Graves is a partisan Democrat. He was on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's domestic policy committee in the 2020 campaign and work for other Democratic campaigns.\par \par \uc2 So what we are seeing clearly is the corruption of the rule of law. Congress held Lois Lerner and \uc2 Eric Holder\uc2  in contempt famously, but of course, they never spent a day in jail and they were never going to because they were faithful Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  joins us for his first interview since his sentencing.\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , thanks so much for coming on tonight. Do you agree with \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  that this is partisan?\par \par \uc2 STEVE BANNON\uc2 , FORMER WHITE HOUSE CHIEF STRATEGIST: That's a hundred percent. I mean, the whole Justice Department under \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  has become radically partisan, and I think that's after we win on November 8th to deliver this crushing blow against the Democratic Party and this regime, Tucker, I strongly believe you'll see \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  impeached next year by the new Congress.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I certainly hope so. People who say four months in prison is not a big deal. I've ever been to a prison, it is a big deal. How are you going to respond to this? Do you plan to submit?\par \par \uc2 BANNON: Well, number one, we have the Judge laid out today a number of areas of appeal. I've got a great legal team. My legal team is working on the appeals right now. We've got the appeals on use of attorney, separation of powers, executive privilege, the structure of the January 6 Committee. So we've got a lot of appeals and we will work through the appeals process.\par \par \uc2 And so this is all -- my sentencing is all pending the appeals process, and we'll work through it. Like I said on your show the first time, at the end of the day, I've got to go to prison by this illegitimate machine. Hey, I respect what the Judge did today. I'm prepared to do it, but we've got a long appeals process.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: What do you think this says about our system more broadly, however? I mean, you're saying that you're being sent to prison, because you advise \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  politically. I mean, that doesn't sound like a free country where something like that could happen.\par \par \uc2 BANNON: It's not free right now. You see this whether it's the \uc2 FBI\uc2  rolling up individuals praying in front of abortion centers or designating parents -- going to parents rights at -- School Board meetings for parents rights as domestic terrorists.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department is completely and totally out of control, and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is out of control. That's why I'm a big believer in defund the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . Use the appropriations process to defund both these apparatuses until they come to the table and start cleaning up the rat's nest.\par \par \uc2 I think the only way you're going to do it is you got to start at the top. We've got to impeach Wray and we have got to impeach \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , after full investigations. I think \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  can be impeached on the Southern border. I think we can impeach by what he's trying to do to these parents, the Parents Rights movement. I think that \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  will be impeached next year by the new Congress.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: One of the reasons that our system has become partisan and the rule of law is evaporating is because no one is pushing back against it. Are you satisfied with the response from elected Republicans to what's happened to you? Is anyone sticking up for you, do you think?\par \par \uc2 BANNON: I think it is fine. Look, elected Republicans, what they need to do now is focus on the eighth of November. Tucker, there is no substitute for victory. We have a very good opportunity here to shatter the Democratic Party as a national political institution, from School Boards, to State Legislatures, to Attorney Generals, Secretaries of State