ck. I'd be -- you don't seem worried. I'd be worried if I were you. You're a brave man and I appreciate your coming on.\par \par \uc2 BANNER: I am not worried. Thanks, Tucker. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So it's looking like \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  will succeed in buying \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . This is a huge problem for the Biden administration because \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has promised to stop censorship on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and censorship is the only thing that keeps the Democrats in power.\par \par \uc2 So, the administration has decided to use the Federal government to destroy \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Remarkable story. Details next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, it looks increasingly likely that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  will soon own \uc2 Twitter\uc2  maybe within the next week, and for the Biden administration, this is an existential problem. They cannot tolerate a free and open Internet.\par \par \uc2 Censorship is the only thing that allows neoliberal leaders to stay in power. They can't have a debate, they have to shut you down.\par \par \uc2 And so the Biden administration is now finding ways to stop \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , not to argue against his position, but to crush him with the power of the Federal government. They are not even pretending there is a legal basis for doing that, they don't have to.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  reports that "Biden administration officials are discussing whether the US should subject some of Musk's ventures to national security reviews, including the deal for \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 's Starlink satellite network." On what grounds you ask?\par \par \uc2 Well, according to Bloomberg: "US officials have grown uncomfortable over Musk's recent threat to stop supplying the Starlink satellite service to Ukraine (for free by the way). They are also concerned by his plans to buy \uc2 Twitter\uc2  with a group of foreign investors." Oh, foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 Every publicly held company in this nation is owned in part by foreign investors, every single one. And of course, thousands -- tens of thousands of acres of US farmland are owned by the Communist Chinese government.\par \par \uc2 But because apparently, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  plans to form some sort of partnership with "foreign investors," maybe the Saudis, he needs a national security review. Don't fall for it.\par \par \uc2 This is about censorship and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's promise to end censorship, which is the single worst thing that could happen to the Biden administration and to the Democratic Party and to the people currently running the country into the ground. They can't have free speech.\par \par \uc2 So on the campaign trail, as you well know, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  promised to end fossil fuels. Once he took office, he made good on that promise, he cancelled oil and gas leases, he shut down a major pipeline. Apparently, the \uc2 US government\uc2  helped blow up the pipeline from Russia to Western Europe. I mean, they did.\par \par \uc2 And yet on Wednesday, Biden insisted that the cost of energy, the rise and the unprecedented rise in it has nothing to do with him. Here is who he blamed.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Because of Putin's invasion of Ukraine, the price of oil and gas increased dramatically.\par \par \uc2 The Strategic Petroleum Reserve is more than half full with about 400 million barrels of oil. That's more than enough for any emergency drawdown.\par \par \uc2 My message to the American energy companies is this: You should not be using your profits to buy back stock or for dividends, not now, not while a war is raging. You should be using these record breaking profits to increase production and refining.\par \par \uc2 Invest in America, for the American people. Bring down the price you charge at the pump to reflect what you pay for the product.\par \par \uc2 And the American people will catch a break they deserve and get a fair price at the pump as well.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, there are so many lies in that script. We're not even going to attempt to reverse engineer it and correct them. Instead, a man much smarter than we. Victor Davis Hanson, a senior fellow at the \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2  joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Professor, thank you for coming on.\par \par \uc2 How do you assess the President's claims about energy?\par \par \uc2 VICTOR DAVIS HANSON, SENIOR FELLOW, \uc2 HOOVER INSTITUTION\uc2 : It's very pathetic. He is trying to square a circle of two things that are incompatible. I mean, he came in here with his green religion, which is God is renewable energy and Satan is fossil fuel. So he canceled ANWR. He cancelled \uc2 Keystone\uc2 . He didn't push the Constitution pipeline.\par \par \uc2 He has fewer Federal leases than any other President. He got his wish, Tucker. He got production down by one and a half to two million barrels on scheduled increases he canceled.\par \par \uc2 So he got everything he wanted. It was \uc2 Steven Chu\uc2 , the Energy Secretary's dream. It was \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 's dream when he said electricity would skyrocket as he cancelled coal and then guess what? Inflation came and there was a spike in demand and the American middle class is being liquidated because they have to choose between food and fuel and he wants to be reelected.\par \par \uc2 But being reelected and destroying fossil fuels are incompatible. And the result is this, I guess, you'd call it Orwellian paradox where he goes around the world to the most illiberal regimes, Venezuela, Iran, even Russia before the war, and Saudi Arabia and his message is, "Would you please pump this filthy dirty fuel that we don't like, but we desperately need and you can do it, but we won't. But you'll do it for our interest. And oh, by the way, we just called you a pariah."\par \par \uc2 Or he goes to this Strategic Petroleum Reserve and he thinks, "Well, I'm not actually pumping it out of the ground, which I can't do. So I'm pumping it the second time so if you pump what has already been pumped in, I don't get blamed for it. The green people will give me a pass," or he goes to the oil companies and he thinks, "Well, yes I wanted to put you out of business and yes, I said you're greedy and yes I said you're price gouging and yes, I cut back on your Federal leases but you owe it to me to get reelected to go out and start pumping more fuel that I don't want."\par \par \uc2 And so it is so incoherent that the American people don't even want to attempt to try to understand, that they just don't want him anymore, and it's really hurt him. It's hurt us around the world.\par \par \uc2 And remember, we impeached \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the mere allegation that he used national security policy issues for his own political career or agenda, and what is Biden doing? He is dabbling with some of the worst regimes in the world against our national interest to pump fuel that we have in abundance, so that he will do better in the midterm.\par \par \uc2 And I don't think -- I think the American people are furious about this to the extent they can understand it, it is so incoherent.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: You've got to give him some credit for hutzpah, though in attacking energy producers for the shortage, please.\par \par \uc2 HANSON: He is shameless. He is very shameless, that's for sure. After saying that these executives were sort of sinister creatures and price gougers and dabble in this filthy dirty oil that is warming the planet. Now, he is saying you have a patriotic duty to ignore everything I've ever said on the campaign trail and pump more of it so I can get my guys reelected. That's the message.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: It's unbelievable. Victor Davis Hanson, thank you for that explanation. So smart.\par \par \uc2 HANSON: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So it looks obvious, the Republicans are going to do