c2 If you -- if you have that level of urgency, guess what? You'll win.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, I call him the great one, the host of the number one show on weekends here on FOX, "Life, \uc2 Liberty\uc2 , and Levin", nationally syndicated radio host, the great one -- thank me. God bless us. How am I?\par \par \uc2 MARK LEVIN, FOX NEWS HOST, LIFE, \uc2 LIBERTY\uc2  AND LEVIN: Sean, I'm going to do something now that's never been done I don't believe in the history of cable. I don't need all the time you gave me to tell the American people what's at stake here.\par \par \uc2 First of all, the idea that they're bringing in \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , people forget, under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , two terms as president, the Democrats lost 1,030 Democrat seats in the state legislatures, federal, governors.\par \par \uc2 So I say if \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  wasn't coming and the \uc2 RNC\uc2  should pay him to come in. He's a disaster when it comes to elections.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is the Herbert Hoover of our time, except that Herbert Hoover had compassion and he had a heart. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  does not, neither do the Democrats. They deny there is inflation. They deny there's recession.\par \par \uc2 They are obsessively focused on partial birth abortion. That's sick. You wake up every morning thinking about that.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, they don't support law and order. They don't support the cops who protect women's bodies. Rape is going through the roof and so forth.\par \par \uc2 Here's the problem and let me say this to you, Democrats. We don't want your socialist crap. We don't want your centralized power. We don't want bureaucrats making our health care decisions. We don't want you destroying our economic system.\par \par \uc2 We're not buying off on this climate change that's destroying our energy independence. Keep your damn hands off our children. Keep your pornography out of our elementary school libraries. You can stick your critical race theory where it doesn't shine. We're not interested in any of it.\par \par \uc2 We don't want an open border where foreigners come across here like they own the country and so many of them. We don't know the number. We don't know who they are and we do know some are bringing fentanyl and killing the people in this country, 18 to 49 years old in record numbers. Keep that border secure.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is completely lacking in compassion. You have all kinds of sex trading going on down there. Little kids being molested down there. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's sort of shuffling around going from one point of the country to the other. The one place he won't go to is the southern border.\par \par \uc2 In fact, I don't know of any Democrat who wants to go to the southern border because they don't want to see what they've done to the country. This country was rolling along. The economy was expanding.\par \par \uc2 People had jobs. Gasoline was affordable. We had no inflation. The border was secure under Trump. All these things were going well.\par \par \uc2 And the Democrat Party comes in with a wrecking ball, his name's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and he's got a Congress that marches right behind him. I hear this said that they're moderate Democrats out there.\par \par \uc2 There's no moderate Democrat out there. Every damn one of them voted for socialism. Every damn one of them voted for inflation. Every damn one of them voted to drive up energy costs in this country. Not one of them except a few on the border have fought his open border policies, not one.\par \par \uc2 Not one of them has taken any serious stance for law and order period. We have mayhem in the streets. Most of the streets where the mayhem is occurring are controlled by the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 We have lousy education system in this country because the teachers unions are too political and they bought and paid for the Democrat Party. And so our teaching scores are -- excuse me -- our student scores are in the toilet. Now, if you want more of this, America, it's there for you. It's only been less than two years. You want four years of this, you want five million illegal aliens coming across the border because the Democrat party is a disaster.\par \par \uc2 Now, I've got two minutes left and I'm giving it back to you. If you don't vote in 19 days, you're going to lose your country. It's that simple.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Mark, let me add one thing and that is -- and we really don't talk a lot about it. If the Democrats did win, what does that mean for the country? As bad -- as bad as things are now, all the issues you touched on, all the issues I'm touching on, think about this. Then we get the elimination of the legislative filibuster, then we get court packing, then we get D.C. statehood, then we get Puerto Rico statehood, then we get the authoritarianism of the Democratic Party and they will forever alter the greatest system of governance ever created for man.\par \par \uc2 That's how deep. That's how profound this will be on this country and I don't know if we get to the point where we could never recover at that point.\par \par \uc2 LEVIN: Now, we won't. Let me tell you what we'll get, a depression, because these fools believe the more you spend, the more you control inflation. If they win, they will consider themselves being empowered and having a mandate. If they win, we're going to have a depression. If they win, we're going to have 5 million illegal aliens.\par \par \uc2 If they win, your children have no hope in our public schools. If they win, the police state that they've put together with the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , and the Department of Justice will not only focus on parents and focus on pro-life groups and so forth, they will continue their assault on Republicans, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and other potential candidates. It's completely out of control.\par \par \uc2 What else if they win? Mayhem in the streets will continue. It's just incredible. It's like the Democrat Party has done more, listen to this, hold on now, the Democrat Party has done more to damage our country, to damage our country economically, in terms of law enforcement and crime, in terms of the border than communist China and Russia could do together on their best day.\par \par \uc2 We're being destroyed from within right now and that includes the military. That's how bad this is.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When you look at the polls and it's 44-44 in Georgia for the Senate, and it's 46-46 in Pennsylvania for the Senate, and then you look in Nevada and Adam Laxalt up by one, and you look at Arizona, Blake Masters down by one, why do you think it's so close or do you not believe these polls?\par \par \uc2 LEVIN: I don't care about the polls. I don't know if it's close or not, whether it's politics or military operations, you act like you're behind. You act like the enemies on the offense.\par \par \uc2 We can enjoy the polls afterwards and all the rest. At this point, these polls to me are deleterious. You act like you're 10 points behind in every one of these races.\par \par \uc2 And I have a comment for \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  -- two months ago as the Republican leader, you criticized our candidates. Let me tell you something, we have great candidates. We have citizen candidates, people with all kinds of backgrounds. Just because they don't come out of Washington and the establishment, you don't condemn them.\par \par \uc2 So I think these candidates are doing a great job and, America, it's up to you. That's it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm done. You're supposed to say, you forgot the "I'm done" part. Where's the -- I'm done. Where's that part?\par \par \uc2 LEVIN: I was done two minutes ago.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. That's why we call him the great one. "Life, \uc2 Liberty\uc2 , and Levin", Sundays, 8:00 p.m., number one show on weekends right here on FOX.\par \par \uc2 All right. Straight ahead, as usual the left playing the race card with voting laws in Georgia. It has now backfired in a big way. We will expose their lies, their hypocrisy and them playing the race card, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Early voting in the great state of Georgia is underway and the voting numbers so far are far surpassing 2020 presidential election vote totals over the same time period, once again debunking the media mob and the Democrats false narrative that Georgia's election laws Jim Crow 2.0.\par \par \uc2 That did not stop the Democrats and their sycophants in the media mob from launching one smear after another, lying over and over and over again that the Georgia law was going to suppress voting access.\par \par \uc2 Here's a quick trip down memory lane, you may remember.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This is the end of democracy in America. This is the beginning of the South -- the South Africa strategy. It's old school American. It's Jim Crow America.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Very much, sort of reminiscent of Jim Crow era tactics that are designed to have a chilling effect on participation.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This is a party that does not like the browning of America. This is a party that is cheating at the polls.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This is the GOP strategy. You can't beat the Democratic candidates, block their voters.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Always was a lie. Remember the Georgia voting law actually expanded -- expanded access to voting, gave voters more flexibility on when to vote, but still, there were endless lies and even the MLB all-star game boycott pushed by \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , that cost the state of Georgia, well, over a hundred million dollars in business.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, former Trump senior adviser \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , along with the host of "The \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2  Show" for "The Epoch Times", \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Larry, start with you. Amazing, was setting one record after another in terms of vote totals in Georgia with the new laws that we were told were Jim Crow 2.0.\par \par \uc2 LARRY ELDER\uc2 , RADIO TALK SHOW HOST: You know, Sean, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is a bigger race card hustler than \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2 , and that's a high bar because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has more credibility, he has more power.\par \par \uc2 I remember when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said of the voter suppression laws that this is worse than Jim Crow, it's Jim Eagle. My father is from Georgia when there really was voter suppression. My father was called the N-word in open court when he went to court to get a license. And now, Blacks are voting in Georgia as a percentage of eligible voters at a higher rate than Whites.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has done this time and time again. He lied and claimed that he segregated desegregated restaurants in movie theaters in Delaware. No evidence that he ever did it. He lied and claimed he tried to visit \uc2 Nelson Mandela\uc2  and got arrested while doing so. He lied and it never happened.\par \par \uc2 And finally as you pointed out, I know Major League Baseball is watching your show, Sean. Are you guys going to give Atlanta back the all-star game next year when you took it away from them and moved to Denver, causing people over $100 million, including small business people, many of these businesses owned by the very Black people that you guys claim you care about? Are they going to get the all-star game next year?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's a great question. And you know what? That's a hundred million dollars in lost business.\par \par \uc2 You know, it and it's ironic, \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , listening to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . I mean, he's the guy that partnered with the former Klansman Robert Byrd to stop the integration of schools. To use Joe's words, he didn't want public schools to become racial jungles, his words.\par \par \uc2 Ironic that he's talking about Jim Crow 2.0.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , FORMER SENIOR TRUMP ADVISER: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made his career in the Senate finding common cause with Democrat segregationists. That's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's origin story and he has never gotten the segregationist instinct out of him and that's why his administration to this day is pushing critical race theory, a policy designed to segregate and divide Americans based on skin color.\par \par \uc2 What's happening right now in the Democratic Party, Sean, is they're panicking, and why are they panicking? Because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has achieved the realignment in American politics Republicans have so long talked about. We have larger numbers of black voters voting Republican, we have massive numbers of Latino and Hispanic voters going Republican, more Asian voters going Republican.\par \par \uc2 The Republican Party is bringing in all of these minority voters and so Democrats are having a meltdown. They're accusing people of being racist because it's the only thing they can think of to do and that smear has stopped working and it will backfire as never before in 19 days.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What do you see happening in these close Senate races, \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2 , as you examine Georgia and Pennsylvania and Ohio and Nevada and Arizona and Washington state and New Hampshire? What do you see happening?\par \par \uc2 ELDER: I see the economy, the economy, the economy -- inflation, crime and borders that are overrun.\par \par \uc2 One more point though about Georgia. Polls have shown over and over and again blacks support not only voter ID, but photo voter ID, almost to the same degree that Whites do. So it is a lie that Blacks do not want to make sure that the elections are safe and secure, and it's a lie that Black people are too stupid to be able to figure out how to get ID to vote.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why are these races at least in the polls so close, Steve Miller?\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Very simple, Sean. For most of the summer, late summer into early fall, because of Democrat connections to Wall Street and Silicon Valley, they had a titanic financial advantage. You look at a state like Arizona, Mark Kelly amassed an almost $60 million dollar war chest and hard campaign cash not counting tens of millions of dollars in outside money. That is a astonishing amount of money for a single Senate race.\par \par \uc2 But what's happening is the American people are now seeing the issues and our candidates are now pulling even and pulling ahead because of the issues Larry mentioned. Rampant crime, rampant inflation, rampant illegal immigration, poverty, joblessness, critical race theory, crazy gender ideology in our schools. We are going to see a red tsunami.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I hope you're both right. It's a little too close for comfort as -- but -- however, I like that it creates urgency and you can't take any state, any vote, any election, any race for granted.\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you both. \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2 , Steve Miller, we appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 We have three announcements to give you but we'll only give you one tonight. More "Hannity" right after the break.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, a few announcements before we go but I can only tell you one of the three. Anyway, Monday, we will be in the great state of Arizona for "Hannity" town hall with Senate candidate Blake Masters. He's down by one. Gubernatorial candidate Kari Lake up by three. That is coming on Monday. We hope you'll join us.\par \par \uc2 And set your DVR so you never, ever, ever miss an episode of "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left, but the good news is, let not your heart be troubled, there she is, Laura Ingraham ready to crush it as always.\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020221021eiak00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  Resigns As British Prime Minister; Labour Party Leader Demands Immediate General Election; President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  Mostly Absent From Campaign Trail; Georgia On Pace To Beat 2018 Midterm Early Turnout; Pentagon To Provide Troops With Travel Funds; Justice Barrett Rejects Appeal Over Biden Plan; CDC Recommends Adding To Immunization Schedule; Large Amount Of Fentanyl Packaged As Candy Seized At U.S. Border; Senators \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  And \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2  Interviewed On Steps Federal Government Taking To Reduce Influx Of Fentanyl Into U.S.; Woman Assaulted On Washington D.C. Bus\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Peter Doocy, Jennifer Griffin, Rich Edson, Alex Hogan,  Steve Harrigan, Jonathan Hunt \par \uc2 7,486 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Special Report with Brett Baier\par \uc2 FNSPBB\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Do you still have that lettuce?\par \par \uc2 PIERS MORGAN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Yes, in fact --\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL LEGAL ANALYST: Where are you taking it?\par \par \uc2 MORGAN: I'm going off obviously, it'll be back to the homeland soon for my 25th prime minister of the year, but you can have the lettuce.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 DANA PERINO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: We need to make a wedge.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: There you go.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: That's it for us, SPECIAL REPORT is up next. Hi, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Hi, Dana. I'm out in L.A., tell Greg his West Hollywood pad is fine, I was just there.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Awesome.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, thanks.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Bye.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Good evening. Welcome to Los Angeles. We're here live tonight but breaking tonight, Great Britain is in the market for a new prime minister again, as you just heard from Piers Morgan.\par \par \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  made it only 44 days before resigning under heavy pressure today. She could not recover from an economic plan calling for major tax cuts, a policy that triggered turmoil in the financial sector there and rebellion within her own party.\par \par \uc2 There are big questions tonight. What does it all mean for the U.K. now and going forward? And what will the economic spillover from Europe mean for us here in the U.S.?\par \par \uc2 Correspondent Alex Hogan joins us now from London with the latest. Good evening, Alex.\par \par \uc2 ALEX HOGAN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT (on camera): Good evening, Bret. It is a historic day on Downing Street. In just a 92nd speech, \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  forfeited her fight to hold on to her seat in the same spot more or less than two months ago she vowed to serve the country.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HOGAN (voice over): The British public now preparing for the third Prime Minister in just four months as \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  announces she's officially stepping down.\par \par \uc2 LIZ TRUSS, BRITISH PRIME MINISTER: I have therefore spoken to His Majesty the King to notify him that I am resigning as leader of the Conservative Party.\par \par \uc2 HOGAN: The Tory Party leader started the job holding an audience with Queen Elizabeth II days before the monarch's death. Truss promised tax cuts which propelled the downward spiral of the economy. All of the plans have been completely reversed just six weeks later. Truss's approval rating sunk to new record lows and her resignation comes less than 24 hours after she said she wouldn't walk away.\par \par \uc2 TRUSS: I am a fighter and not a quitter.\par \par \uc2 HOGAN: Truss will go down in history as the shortest serving U.K. Prime Minister in the job for just 44 days.\par \par \uc2 Today, President Biden thanked Truss for her partnership. When asked about the changes impact on the U.S. economy Biden answered:\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I don't think they're that consequential.\par \par \uc2 HOGAN: And just hours after Truss's announcement, the pound began trading higher.\par \par \uc2 Nominations for a new party leader are open until Monday afternoon, candidates would need the backing of 100 M.P.s. If conservatives cannot agree on one, they'll hold a vote by next Friday.\par \par \uc2 Tory party members expected to stand up for the opportunity include \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2 , the former P.M. candidate who lost to Truss and even former Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , an idea liberal politicians want banned given Johnson's scandalous ousting several months ago.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HOGAN (on camera): Labour Party politicians labeled these last few months as a revolving door of chaos, demanding a general election for the public to choose the next leader rather than the party in power, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Alex Hogan in London. Alex, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now to talk about this situation is author and former foreign policy adviser to Prime Minister \uc2 Margaret Thatcher\uc2 , \uc2 Nile Gardiner\uc2 . He's also director of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 's Margaret Thatcher Center for Freedom. Nile, thanks for being here.\par \par \uc2 NILE GARDINER\uc2 , DIRECTOR OF MARGARET THATCHER CENTER FOR FREEDOM, THE HERITAGE FOUNDATION: My pleasure.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: This is quite something and 44 days, now the Conservative Party looks for another leader. And there is a lot of turmoil. How do you read it?\par \par \uc2 GARDINER: Well, a great amount of turmoil in London and a spectacular decline and fall for \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 . It started so well with a series of tax cuts, which I thought were overall extremely positive, forward looking, and designed, of course, to kick start the British economy.\par \par \uc2 But she met tremendous opposition from the sort of ruling liberal elites in the -- in the United Kingdom, including inside the Conservative Party, but also from the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  condemned her tax cutting approach.\par \par \uc2 And she basically performed a series of U-turns, and she surrendered really to the demands of the (INAUDIBLE) Chancellor \uc2 Kwasi Kwarteng\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And so, this was a spectacular reversal of fortune for \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 , a third woman prime minister of the United Kingdom, and she has just resigned.\par \par \uc2 So, we now have a Conservative Party leadership contest with the strong prospect I think that \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  could potentially return as the prime minister, so it's going to be extremely interesting in a few days.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Do you really believe that?\par \par \uc2 GARDINER: Yes, actually, I do think that \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  is serious about running. And if he does run, I think he stands a very good chance of winning because he is very, very popular among the grassroots of the Conservative Party, many of whom were opposed to his removal several months ago.\par \par \uc2 So, I think the possibility of \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  returning is definitely, I think realistic. And we'll have a new prime minister by Friday next week.\par \par \uc2 But we do need to see strong, bold conservative leadership in the United Kingdom, we can't have the kinds of U-turns that we saw with \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 , we do see a prime minister standing up for Britain on the world stage who's willing to implement conservative policies and advanced economic freedom.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Let me play this sound bite from the Labour leader. Also reaction from parliament. Obviously, everyone knows here in the U.S., it's a different system. But some of the criticism is pretty scathing. Take a listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KEIR STARMER, BRITISH LABOUR PARTY LEADER: This is not just a soap opera at the top of the Tory party, it's doing huge damage to our economy and to the reputation of our country. And the public are paying with higher prices, with higher mortgages. So, we can't have a revolving door of chaos.\par \par \uc2 A book is being written about the prime minister's time in office, apparently it's going to be out by Christmas. Is that the release date or the title?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: I mean, they're having a good old time there with all the lines. Bottom line, the economic situation in the U.K. and really throughout Europe is pretty severe.\par \par \uc2 GARDINER: It is and you do have soaring inflation in United Kingdom, which actually is lower than many other parts of Europe. It's in fact, it's doubled in some parts of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So, the U.K. is in a relatively bad shape. But I do believe that the British economy can fully recover. But you need to see the kinds of policies that advance economic liberty rather than restrain them.\par \par \uc2 We do have to see cuts in government spending, we have to see a reversal of the kind of big government mindset that has been in place for many years. And you showed footage earlier of \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 , the leader of the Labour Party.\par \par \uc2 Well, the Socialist Labour Party, of course, offers nothing but tax rises, and more and more government spending and heavier debt.\par \par \uc2 And so, the Conservatives I think do have a chance over the course of the next two years to turn things around. But you need to have conservative leadership that actually adopts and stands for conservative principles. When you make concessions to the left, it's all over as we saw with \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BAIER: It'll be quite something to watch who emerges and whether it's \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  or not. Nile, thank you for the time.\par \par \uc2 GARDINER: My pleasure, Bret. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Breaking tonight, President Biden is in Philadelphia for a campaign event. Normally less than three weeks from a midterm election, a sitting president would be a hot commodity on the campaign trail, but that is not the case this year.\par \par \uc2 White House correspondent Peter Doocy tells us why live from the North Lawn. Good evening, Peter.\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT (on camera): Good evening, Bret. In October of their first midterm cycles, Trump had 26 rallies, \uc2 Obama\uc2  had 16 rallies. That means President Biden has some catching up to do because on the campaign trail with the exception of P.A., the President has been MIA.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: My staff said to me, you realize how many times you've been to Pittsburgh? I said no, he said 19.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): This time to boost the Democratic Senate candidate \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  again.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: You're going to win. You're going to win.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: President Biden claims he's helping more than a dozen Democrats.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: There haven't been that many candidates campaigning with you. Why are more --\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: That's not true. There have been 15. Count, kid, count.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: OK, and they're going to be even more?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: It was even more, 3-1/2 hours later.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: 16 I've already done in four (PH) years and a lot more than that.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: But these appearances are often at official events. Appearances at traditional campaign style rallies are rare. The last big one was in late August in a state where none of the races are competitive, Maryland.\par \par \uc2 President Biden's approval rating has improved recently to 46 percent. But the headliner for Democrats is \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  with planned stops in Wisconsin, Michigan and Georgia. President Biden's schedule is apparently wide open.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I don't know where I'm going. I've got about 16, 18 request.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: There are at least 29 competitive House districts where gas prices are higher than the national average according to the Associated Press, the White House Chief of Staff remains upbeat.\par \par \uc2 RON KLAIN, CHIEF OF STAFF, WHITE HOUSE: We are planning to work with the Democratic House and the Democratic Senate next year. That's our plan.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports about the president, his decision not to participate, so far at least, in rallies that are normally a staple of campaign season highlights how little the president can do to help his fellow Democrats even with the megaphone of the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 So, for now, Biden is talking a lot about his own accomplishments like the bipartisan infrastructure bill repairing failed roads and bridges.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I'm coming back to walk over this sucker.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (on camera): The President once referred to himself as a bridge to the next generation of Democratic leaders, but now the candidates hoping to represent that next generation are trying to see if they can establish themselves without them, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Peter Doocy live in the North Lawn. Peter, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Stocks were down today as rising bond yields and rate hike worries offset upbeat earnings. The Dow lost 90. The S&P 500 fell 29, the NASDAQ was off 66.\par \par \uc2 In our spotlight races tonight, we take a closer look at an early in person voting effort. Almost every state offers that with four notable exceptions.\par \par \uc2 Alabama, Mississippi, New Hampshire and Connecticut, where it is on the ballot this November. The measure would change the state's constitution in Connecticut to allow the legislature to pass laws to provide for early voting in person.\par \par \uc2 A record 1.86 million Connecticut residents voted in the 2020 election, a turnout of nearly 80 percent of registered voters there.\par \par \uc2 Turnout is already strong in the Georgia governor's race based on just a few days of early voting in Georgia. That fact itself seems to be working against Democrat \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  who is and was highly critical of Georgia's new voting law, as were many Democratic lawmakers and pundits.\par \par \uc2 Here's Senior National Correspondent Rich Edson.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RICH EDSON, FOX NEWS CHANNEL SENIOR NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT (voice over): Georgia voters including candidates are breaking early voting records. The Georgia secretary of state says as of Thursday morning, nearly 400,000 voters took advantage of early in-person poll hours. At the same point in 2018, 225,000 had done so.\par \par \uc2 This year's early voting trails 2020 presidential election by only about 15,000 ballots. Democratic nominee \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  says voting access is still a major issue in her state.\par \par \uc2 STACEY ABRAMS (D) GUBERNATORIAL NOMINEE OF GEORGIA: Having more people turnout does not mean there aren't barriers. That's like saying because more people get in the water, there are fewer sharks.\par \par \uc2 EDSON: Earlier this year, President Biden said