on is, do you think from the Democrats' perspective that Biden can beat Trump? Who is the best person to beat the Republican likely nominee? And, of course, Biden has beaten Trump.\par \par \uc2 And the second thing to say, picking up on what Doug was talking about, is messaging. There are a lot of Democratic candidates right now who are really struggling for an effective message. You think about crime, inflation, immigration, those have been strong assets for Republican messaging. What should the Democratic messaging be? Well, you can say Biden has achieved on a bipartisan basis passage of an infrastructure bill, Build Back Better, COVID relief. You stop and think about our economy. It's better right now, obviously, than what \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  was dealing with in Britain. But somehow, those messages are not being conveyed. I think that's bigger than anybody is saying that Biden shouldn't run.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yes. Katie, to that point, here is Congressman \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2  being asked about why the prices are where they are.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Where do you place blame?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 RO KHANNA\uc2 , (D-CA): We're not making enough things in America. We didn't make baby formula. We didn't make masks. And so when the global pandemic happened we were shipping things from offshore, and that increased prices and created supply chain disruptions. We need to make more things in America.\par \par \uc2 Second, I blame Powell with the quantitative easing. He was buying mortgage-backed securities way too long.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So with that, we kind of dug into what is behind inflation always. And it brought us back to Milton Freidman, the late economist, 1978. And he was asked at that time where inflation was spiking about inflation. Take a listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MILTON FRIEDMAN, ECONOMIST: Inflation is made in Washington because only Washington