t state income tax cut in our state's history last year, refunding a billion dollars of taxpayer money to help put more pocket into hard work in Georgians wallet and pocket books, so they can deal with top high food prices when they go to the grocery store.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Governor, do you think you'll be able to give a significant boost to \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , obviously his campaign has had some controversy to say the least as has Warnock's. But it's obviously an incredibly important Senate seat for the direction of the country. The conservative movement growth in America safety. How confident are you about his chances?\par \par \uc2 KEMP: Well, I kind, I kind of see Herschel's race like a hard hitting football game. You know, he took some early licks in the first and second quarter came out of halftime regrouped, took a few shots in the third quarter. But it seems like though the team is starting to wear out to me and I think Herschel is going to have a strong fourth quarter. I'm helping in regards to that with our whole ticket. We've got a ground game like people haven't seen, really in over a decade.\par \par \uc2 We're knocking doors. We did that in the primary, which was very successful for us. But also the race is moving away from the Democrats. I think, Americans the 60 percent of the people that are living week-to-week 70 percent of the people across the country, they feel like their paychecks, not keeping up with Joe Biden's inflation. They're getting more centered on those issues and not on things that the Democrats are trying to distract with. And that's what we're talking to him about. You know, people don't support defunding the Police like \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  who wants to do or ending cash bail. And she's or hitting home and Herschel's hitting we'll rock on those issues too, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, well Governor, you opened your state before any of the other States that were temporarily closed and for that, I will never forget that you did that. That was you helped lead the way on that issue. And that was so important. Thank you so much, Governor, we appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 And up next we examine Joe Biden's destructive and self-serving move on depleting America's strategic petroleum reserves. It's not a wonky issue, it affects your future. Plus, Missouri Attorney General Eric Schmidt is here with some breaking news. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN, PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: The Department of Energy released another 15 million barrels from the strategic petroleum reserves, extending our previously announced release through the month of December. Right now the strategic polymer - Strategic Petroleum Reserve is more than half full with about 400 million barrels of oil. That's more than enough for any emergency drawdown.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, when he mumbled through that, what he didn't mention is that the Strategic Petroleum Reserve is now at his lowest point in 40 years. Now replenishing it is going to take a lot of time and cost Americans a boatload of money. But he doesn't care, he doesn't even understand where he is. The main point is that, this is not what the reserve was made for. Now it was conceived to protect all Americans in an emerging crisis, not the Democratic Party ahead of the midterms.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now is Steve Milloy, Former Trump \uc2 EPA\uc2  Transition Member, Founder of JunkScience.com. Steve, since no one else in the media will we're going to take the audience through a few statements Biden made today at his big energy talk, and then we're going to fact check him. Let's begin with this.\par \par \uc2 STEVE MILLOY, FMR TRUMP EPA TRANSITION MEMBER: OK.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: My administration has not stopped or slowed U.S. oil production. Quite the opposite. You can increase oil and gas production now,