timate for how much this war is actually contributing to these pipe prices?\par \par \uc2 MILLOY: Yes, he's done nothing. We went through earlier the list of things he's not done and the Strategic Petroleum Gambit, that's not reducing the price of oil, although he's taking credit for it. All its doing is going to make Americans pay more for gas for oil later, as he has to replenish it. You know, we need that strategic petroleum reserve for actual emergencies, not just reelecting Democrats.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And just to get back to this point, there have been no offshore lease sales, right. Since he'd been he's been in office for oil, there's no offshore leases at all.\par \par \uc2 MILLOY: No he's, he has he has completely shut down leasing. They'd been in court about this. They have not gotten it straight yet. But, you know, they are not encouraging any sort of drilling, despite the fact that you know, they got Joe Manchin to agree to that inflation reduction act with the promise of more oil drilling, but that's not happening.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, Luci in the football on that. Steve, great to see you. Thank you. And on the issue of energy, this just breaking today, 19 Republican led States are launching an investigation into six large U.S., banks to examine their involvement. And something called the United Nations Net Zero banking Alliance.\par \par \uc2 Now the bank served are, \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 , \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 , \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2 , and \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 . Now leading this investigation is Missouri Attorney General Eric Schmidt, who says the \uc2 UN\uc2 's Environmental Social Governance Policies, ESG require banks to set carbon dioxide emission reduction targets in their lending and investment portfolios. But of course, that's all very subjective.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now is the Missouri Attorney General and Missouri Senate Candidate, Eric Schmidt. Mr. Attorney General, your state is already divested, your state pension funds, I know from places like \uc2 Blackrock\uc2  over these ESG concerns, which is fantastic explain how this move today represents the next step.\par \par \uc2 ERIC SCHMIDT (R) MISSOURI ATTORNEY GENERAL: So Missouri is leading that investigation, as you said, Laura, with 18 other states into the into the sixth largest financial institutions in the world for this \uc2 Net Zero Banking Alliance\uc2 , which is in partnership with the United Nations with the stated goal of having a carbon neutral portfolio by 2050. And that might sound good to the coastal elites, it might sound good on some term paper at Harvard, or maybe even some white paper at a liberal think tank.\par \par \uc2 But for the rest of America, this stinks to high heaven, and not to scare the be Jesus out of everybody. Because here's what it really means. It means that for credit worthy applicants who happen to be in the oil and gas industry or the coal industry, or auto manufacturing industry, or agriculture, where they have diesel vehicles or cows that in hit, you know, the stench that everybody's complaining about that pollutes the pollutes the world, I suppose, as they think, it means that they're going to shut down lending, and make everything more expensive.\par \par \uc2 And that's a real problem. And you know, this is, this is nefarious, we've launched this investigation, we've now issued subpoenas, because what they're going to do is essentially shut down lending to credit worthy applicants because they don't check some box on a wolf bingo card. And these are these. And Laura, this is 40 percent of the, of the banking assets in the United States. This is not small potatoes. I mean, these are the big financial institutions. We've watched this investigation because there's a lot of legal issues at play, including antitrust issues, and unfair lending practices.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, now this is hot. When I saw this, I was like, OK, this is where the rubber meets the road. This is exactly what needs to happen. But you do have people defending ESG practices out there. We've exposed that on The Ingraham Angle, but others, including multibillionaires on CNBC, watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BILL GATES, CO-FOUNDER OF \uc2 MICROSOFT\uc2 : Anyone who says that climate shouldn't be a factor in how you evaluate the future of a company. You know, isn't that's not capitalism because companies that have emissions, you know, they aren't going to be subject to border adjustment tariffs or taxes appear dealing with severe weather events that's got to be factored in.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Your response to this argument from Gates?\par \par \uc2 SCHMIDT: All they are doing is shifting these jobs to China. That's really what's happening, right, is we have got all the energy we'll ever need right under our feet in the United States, and they're going to shift all of these jobs to China. China is not going to stop building coal-fired plants. They are building them at a record pace. That's not going to slow down. All we are doing is doing on a long-term basis what we are doing on a short-term basis, which is declaring war on American energy.\par \par \uc2 And Inflation, Laura, is not some act of God. It's not a tornado, it's not a hurricane. There is actually a formula. If turns out if you spend trillions and trillions and trillions of dollars and you declare war on American energy, the prices go up on everything. And what this net zero banking alliance will do in the long term is more of that on hyper-speed.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Mr. Attorney General, I am already hearing from folks in the oil and gas industry that the money has already dried up. The big banks already are not lending to oil and gas companies, correct? And they are losing hundreds of millions of dollars in potential investments. So they are pulling the money out of the industry in an act of almost domestic warfare, economic warfare, against one of the engines of our economy, one of the main drivers of our economy.\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: And great American jobs, and inexpensive energy. And I'll tell you, winter is coming. Here in the Midwest, in Missouri, people start turning that furnace on, utility rates are going to be through the roof. And people are starting to see it. You are seeing blackouts in Europe you're going to see this winter.\par \par \uc2 And the idea of having rolling blackouts in the United States of America, the most powerful country in the history of the world, is totally nuts, and it's self-inflicted. It's coming from the Biden administration. Now it's coming from these woke banks. And we need to stand up and we need to push back and say we are not going to do this anymore, which is why we've launched this investigation, because the left is going to do what they could never get done legislatively, which is stuff like this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We've got to pull the money back from these banks. That's what we've got to do. Mr. Attorney General, thank you, and good luck on the trail.\par \par \uc2 A new documentary on Joe Biden's first year hits \uc2 HBO\uc2 , but is it going to help him at all? Raymond Arroyo is here with all the details and our own documentary, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's time for our "Seen and Unseen" segment where we explore the cultural stories of the day. And for that we turn to FOX News contributor, author of the bestselling "The Wise Men Who Found Christmas," Raymond Arroyo. All right, Raymond, tell us about that big new Biden documentary that just dropped.\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Laura, \uc2 HBO\uc2  has unveiled a perplexing film. It's called "Year One, A Political Odyssey," and it focuses on Biden's first year in the White House. Naturally, it starts with January 6th concerns.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 JEN PSAKI\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: There was a huge security issue that day. Fears after January 6th and a lot of steps and precautions that were being taken. We couldn't even get close enough to drive here on our first day.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Even though it's meant to help, Laura, just before the midterms, I'm not sure reminding people of the Biden COVID restrictions that destroyed kids' educations or his Afghanistan withdrawal is going to end up being a positive.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN, (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: It's time to end the forever war.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Biden's cabinet, not stupid people, and they got this really wrong.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I think they got more than that wrong, Laura. The problem with this documentary is, like so many of these things, Biden is absent. He's not interviewed. And they conveniently skip over the immigration crisis as well as the COVID difficulties and inflation, the two major burning issues of this midterm election.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But these never do anything. These documentaries are always just major puff pieces, unless it's about Trump and then they slam him. So it doesn't -- people are living the nightmare right now. So this glossy view of his first year in office really doesn't cut to our core because people are living the inflation and the crime and everything else that's going on because of Biden. So this is a nice fantasy.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yes, they don't need \uc2 HBO\uc2  documentaries to tell them how they feel.\par \par \uc2 And the other thing is, Laura, "Year One, A Political Odyssey," which is what this is called, it misses so much, that we decided we would create our own mini documentary of Biden's year one. Here it is.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN, (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: If you have a problem figuring out whether you're for me or Trump, then you ain't black.\par \par \uc2 My whole soul is in this, bringing America together, uniting our people.\par \par \uc2 What a stupid son of a bitch.\par \par \uc2 (MUSIC)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: We are in a battle for the soul of America. We will win.\par \par \uc2 (MUSIC)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: We are the United States of America. There's nothing beyond our capacity. God bless you all and may God protect our troops. Thank you, and I'm sorry.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: "I'm sorry" -- that could be the ultimate signoff, Laura. This could be called "2021, A Political Space Oddity." That's what I think we are dealing with here. Why would they even make a documentary, though, of this first year? Just do a puff piece of the parties he held or something. This would be a little bit like creating a documentary, maiden voyage, the first sailing of the Titanic. Why do you do this? Why would you do that?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I would have him, at the end, if we want to tweak the ending, when we have the big premiere party, you just have him on one of his stage left and then right, and then --\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He has been doing that robotic thing for a while, so trying to get off the stage.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: That will be the Ingraham director's cut. We'll release that on DVD later.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. OK, good. Good, good, good.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, the big problem here, and you see it in some of those clips, you've seen it over the last two years, the president is clearly being managed and choreographed by the White House team. And the problem is they are not very good at what they do. For instance, the president's digital team attempted to produce a piece touting the ease of Biden's student loan forgiveness program.\par \par \uc2 Well, a little piece of advice to them. If you are going to add sound to the president typing on his phone, it helps if his fingers are actually moving.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: This is so fraudulent when I saw this. He is typing once, and you hear tick, tick, tick. But we obtained a little bit of behind-the-scenes footage from that clip from another angle. Watch this. Here he is typing.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (MUSIC)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It all makes sense.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: "Candy Crush" can be challenging. There is no way he can do "Candy Crush." That is --\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: That's not called "Candy Crush." That game is called economy crush, Laura. You just keep pulling the oil barrels off and the economy collapses.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, my gosh.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It's a new fun game we're going to try out, and we all get to suffer the results.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: There was a little -- he had a little trouble at the big speech on energy today. He seemed to lack the energy needed for the energy speech, so that was also problematic.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: He did say I'm sorry. He did say I'm sorry at the end of that other clip. So apology accepted, apparently.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Being a liberal member of the Biden family means never having to really say you are really sorry for what you're doing. But Raymond, great to see you, and congrats again on the book.\par \par \uc2 File this under hilarious irony. A new poll finds that no one cares about January 6th, and further, many believed Democrats to be the true threat to democracy. Obviously, they're watching. Congressman Jim Jordan, Charlie Kirk react to these delicious findings, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 NICOLLE WALLACE, MSNBC HOST: We spent all those days together covering public phase of the January 6th committee hearings. Democracy shot to the top of the list. And not just Democratic voters, but independent voters have this a top ratio. We haven't seen that in a generation.\par \par \uc2 ALI VELSHI, MSNBC HOST: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Republicans who follow him are a threat to democracy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, sorry to dash your hopes there, but two new poll findings show Americans have totally tuned out these loons. "\uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " reporter Aaron Blake seemed very sad to tweet the following, "Despite the January 6th hearings, the many GOP election deniers running, et cetera, just 52 percent of Biden voters and 23 percent of independents view the GOP as a major threat to democracy. In fact, more independence actually view the Democrats as a threat to democracy." That is so sad. It surprises him that the party who wants to expand the Supreme Court, right, they want to get rid of the filibuster, they want the Electoral College gone, and he's surprised that they are the true threat to democracy?\par \par \uc2 But there is another pole that will upset Aaron and all his friends. The same "New York Times"-Siena poll found that more voters view the media as a threat to democracy than any politician or any political party, a whopping 80 for percent. Didn't Trump call them the enemy of the people?\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Ohio Congressman Jim Jordan, ranking member of House Judiciary, as well as Charlie Kirk, founder of Turning Point USA, author of "The College Scam."\par \par \uc2 Congressman, I think the American people were treated by the Democrats as just idiots that could be led along by the nose regardless of how bad the economy got, that everyone would hang on \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 's every word. But it seems like people were just bored by her in the end.\par \par \uc2 REP. JIM JORDAN, (R-OH) HOUSE OVERSIGHT COMMITTEE RANKING MEMBER: Yes, I think you are right. And I think the American people have common sense, and the American people understand as these recent polls point out that it's the Democrats who are a threat to democracy. You did the list there, Laura. They've kicked Republicans off committee, won't let us serve on select committees, enacted proxy voting, trying to end the Electoral College, trying to end the filibuster, trying to pack the court.\par \par \uc2 Most importantly, they have weaponized the Justice Department to go after their political opposition. That is a huge threat to democracy, a huge threat to the First Amendment. And never forget, two years ago this month the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was involved in suppressing the number one story that would have made a difference in the presidential election, our most important election, when they went and talked to \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , and the mainstream press that no one trusts suppressed the Hunter Biden story just days before a presidential contest.\par \par \uc2 So the American people always get it right. They know that's the real threat to democracy, not Republicans who are fighting for the Bill of Rights, the Constitution, the First Amendment.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Charlie, we played something from this really weird cat on MSNBC yesterday, but we actually missed something else. He said this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANAND GIRIDHARADAS, MSNBC POLITICAL ANALYST: The scary thing right now is that the people who want to end liberal democracy as we know it in America and who don't want to include, who would rather break the republic than share it, they are offering a vision that reads too many Americans as more welcoming and more inviting and more fun, frankly. And the people who are on the pro-democracy side trying to build a better movement are failing at that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Charlie, this is all they have, if you can make heads or tails of that logic.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE KIRK, TURNING POINT USA FOUNDER: I actually agree with part of it. Our side is more fun. We smile. We don't take ourselves as seriously. We don't scold our political opponents. But he's right in the sense that our ranks are increasing. You look at the candidates like Kari Lake, Blake Masters, J.D. Vance, they are drawing huge crowds. And there's this young, energizing movement that the Democrats are not able to match, and including this massive shift of Hispanics to the conservative Republican movement.\par \par \uc2 And you could already see they are beginning the groundwork, the foundation of what their excuse is going to be. And I can't wait to hear it on election night or the days that follow. The reason that they won is that they hate democracy. Wait a second, you mean the people that hate democracy got more votes than the people that love democracy? How does that one work, exactly? Isn't the whole point of democracy is getting more votes?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, no, no. It's not when the wrong people vote.\par \par \uc2 Btu Congressman, they don't want people to really vote, do they? Not on the issues that matter, because when the issue of abortion went back to the states, they're like you can't do that. That's anti-woman, that's anti- democracy. How is that anti-democracy? Kansas decided to keep abortion. Other states will choose differently. They don't want that choice, not when it comes to babies.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Great point, Laura. In the end, they don't trust the people who get in elective office. They want the experts, the scientists. They want Fauci running our lives. They don't want the folks who get elected by we, the people, who under our Constitutional system are supposed to make the laws and supposed to enact things. That's our constitutional system. And those are the individuals directly accountable to we, the people, to the American people. They don't want that. They want the, quote, elites in D.C. who think they are so much better than us, who drink their $12 cups of coffee and want to run our lives. They want them running things, not the folks whose name goes on the ballot and get elected to office.\par \par \uc2 That's going to change, I think, on November 8th. I think in 20 days, the American people are going to put in office, people are going to fight for the values and principles they care about and that make our country the special place that it is.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And Charlie, really quickly, Native American Senator Elizabeth Warren, she thinks Democrats are doing just fine.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. ELIZABETH WARREN, (D-MA): I think that we have a very strong message as Democrats on the economy, particularly up against Republicans who can do nothing but shout and have no ideas.\par \par \uc2 Abortion is on the ballot in 2022. Democracy is also on the ballot in 2022. They are the ones putting our democracy at risk.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's their bumper sticker, democracy at risk. Charlie, is it going to work, real quick?\par \par \uc2 KIRK: Good luck. Maybe in Boston if you are making an academic argument. It's not going to work with the muscular class in our country. It's not going to work with everyday people that are getting crushed by inflation, crime, and an open border.\par \par \uc2 And I will just say one thing in closing here. Elizabeth Warren, she is a perfect example of the lack of honesty of the Democrat Party. They are going to lose because they can't admit they've messed things up, and voters hate being told things are good when they are awful.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They are inauthentic from the DNA on out. Congressman and Charlie, good to see you both.\par \par \uc2 KJP finally tells the truth from the briefing room. I kid you not. It happened. The last blight (ph) -- bite, will tell you about. I sound like Biden.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, check out what happens when KJP finally stops reading from her briefing book.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Does the president want more migrants to come to Delaware?\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE DEPUTY PRESS SECRETARY: I don't even understand that question. I'll move on.\par 