ers about those livability, daily, hourly issues that they're confronted with?\par \par \uc2 STACEY ABRAMS (D), GEORGIA GUBERNATORIAL CANDIDATE: Let's be clear, having children is why you're worried about your price for gas. It's why you're concerned about how much food cost.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Oh, it is your fault for having children. Go back to Citibank. What?\par \par \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  who is not married and has no children lives only for herself, has contempt for people who dare to have children. We can just import those. Don't have your own.\par \par \uc2 And if you had children, maybe you're the one to blame for gas prices you can't afford. So you've got a politician that says stuff like that and you've got something to talk about. And by the way, she is welcome on the show any day of the week.\par \par \uc2 But reporters, including the one who was moderating the gubernatorial debate in Georgia this week decided not to ask about this. Watch this. Watch this bag of Jell-o Chuck Williams with a local news station ask \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , he didn't really ask actually -- this is like sucker -- this is thrown sniffing disguised as a question and this is real. We did not -- this is not a deep fake. This is an actual question from Chuck Williams, which cannot really be Israel. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHUCK WILLIAMS, RADIO SHOW HOST: Miss Abrams, public opinion polls in our State show support for the right to abortion, Medicaid expansion, and banning assault weapons. You err on the side of public opinion in each of these issues. Yet, you are behind almost every poll. Why?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So since you're Jesus, does it shock you that a prophet gets no respect in his hometown? \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , beautiful, brilliant.\par \par \uc2 Mollie Hemingway is beautiful and brilliant as well, but she doesn't expect to be sucked up to. She is the editor-in-chief of "The Federalist." She joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 I'm sorry. These are serious topics, but watching Chuck Williams, if that's his real name, ask a question like that, you know, needed levity.\par \par \uc2 Why is it anyone asking \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , why she is telling people who are upset about gas prices to go ahead and kill their kids? That seems like a real question.\par \par \uc2 MOLLIE HEMINGWAY, EDITOR-IN-CHIEF, "THE FEDERALIST": Yes, it does seem -- you know, it is worth remembering that \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  was put forth as the rising star of the Democratic Party, and here you have this moderator claiming that she is on the side of public opinion. But quite clearly, even Georgia voters are rejecting this, even though they were told that she is - - you know, she has the great hope for the Democratic Party.\par \par \uc2 She has a track record of saying very bizarre things about children. You know, she said -- even went on from that MSNBC segment that inflation is the reason why people need to have abortions, that they -- suggesting that killing unborn children is a solution to (abortion), rather than offering ideas about what could be done differently through the Democratic Party agenda.\par \par \uc2 She previously denied scientific reality about when children are conceived. She also claimed that ultrasound technology, which enables you to hear your unborn child's heartbeat, that's one of the first things you get to do when you're pregnant, it is very cool, she said that it was a manufactured sound and that it was a patriarchal plot to control women.\par \par \uc2 I mean, she has really weird issues on this and I think Georgia voters are rejecting them.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I mean, you can be -- there are a lot of -- I'm not one of them, but there are a million decent people who are "pro-choice." But you've got to think being pro-choice is very different from having some politician say, stop complaining and have an abortion. Like, it's your fault for having children. I mean, that is so anti-human. That's so evil.\par \par \uc2 I can't even believe that pro-choice people are for that, are they?\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: I do think she kind of represents the end of the Democratic Party right now. They have put a lot into this idea that abortion is the number one thing that they want to offer people as their closing argument.\par \par \uc2 It is not the wisest thing, given that American opinion is actually pretty mixed on this, but something like 75 percent of Americans seek at least some protection for unborn children and their mothers, and you've seen it in states across the country, Democrat candidates are refusing to say that they would support any protection for unborn children, no matter if we're talking about the third trimester, or if we're talking about protecting children from being killed for being the wrong sex or for having minor defects.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are saying that they will not support any protections and that's not just \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , that's pretty much nationwide for a lot of Democrat candidates.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes. It's so foolish and sad. Ask anyone over 50, you know, what matters in your life? It is not your stupid job. "I'm Governor of Georgia." Who cares? It's your children, right?\par \par \uc2 We're stripping meaning from people's lives and this is really not good, I would say.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: Amen.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Mollie Hemingway, Amen. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 So they've been telling us for years, the people who lecture you about what's right and wrong that the hallmark of a dictatorship is a government that goes after journalists.\par \par \uc2 So, then they went after James O'Keefe. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  showed up at his apartment with guns and we kind of ignored that because it's just James O'Keefe, then the Bureau raided a former ABC producer who is now missing, for real, that story is straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, here's a completely bizarre story. We can't even really guess as to what's really going on here, but an ABC News reporter gets a visit from armed men with guns from the Biden administration at home and then disappears and hasn't been heard from since. What?\par \par \uc2 FOX's Trace Gallagher has the story for us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Hey, Trace.\par \par \uc2 TRACE GALLAGHER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Hey, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 The missing journalist is 52-year-old James Gordon Meek who covered national security and terrorism for ABC News. In April of this year, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  conducted a heavily armed raid on his sixth floor apartment in Arlington, Virginia.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  called it a "Court authorized law enforcement" meaning the search warrant was approved by a Federal Judge. And during the raid, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  also seized Mr. Meek's laptop. Anonymous sources told "\uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2 " Magazine the laptop included classified information.\par \par \uc2 James Gordon Meek's attorney believes only a source inside the government would know that and says the leak is highly inappropriate. But on top of that, the Biden administration prohibits seizing documents from journalists without authorization from US Deputy Attorney General Lisa Monaco, leaving many to ask why would the Deputy AG give that kind of approval?\par \par \uc2 Well, it's notable that James Meek was the award-winning producer of the \uc2 Hulu\uc2  documentary called "3212" Unredacted. The 3212 refers to the Special Forces Unit that was ambushed in Niger in 2017. Four US soldiers lost their lives, and The Pentagon kept giving the families of the fallen soldiers different versions of what happened.\par \par \uc2 I also covered that story and talked to one of the widows at the time, Michelle Black. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE BLACK, GOLD STAR WIFE: He always knew his odds before he went in, because I think he knew he was probably not coming home. But I think he knew that if he took a risk, some of his friends might.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: So the Pentagon finally blamed the Special Forces for embarking on a rogue mission.\par \par \uc2 Another ABC journalist who also worked on the \uc2 Hulu\uc2  documentary, also inexplicably left the network a few months before James Meek disappeared.\par \par \uc2 So as for Meek being raided by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , having his documents seized, never being charged and disappearing, we asked ABC News why they or correspondents like Jonathan Carl are not covering this.\par \par \uc2 ABC News responded saying only Meek resigned very abruptly and hasn't worked for us in months. Very odd -- Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, that's a really weird story and maybe there is a normal explanation for it. Hard to see what it might be.\par \par \uc2 Trace Gallagher, host of "FOX News at Night," right here, midnight Eastern, we're always grateful to have you on the show. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Thank you, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, there's zero scientific basis for sexually mutilating children, but some guy dressed like a woman in a military uniform he did not earn who works for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says it doesn't matter, voters should just shut up and do what the experts say. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ADMIRAL RACHEL LEVINE, US ASSISTANT SECRETARY FOR HEALTH: It's very important to note that the fact that the appropriateness of a range of medical treatments, evaluations, and treatments of people who are transgender and transgender youth is thoroughly grounded in medical research.\par \par \uc2 And we do not need State laws and actions that dictate principles of transgender medical care by us, pediatric experts.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Just absolute cartoon world and the cost is destroying the lives of children. Almost nobody is saying a 