aged her reputation.\par \par \uc2 Up next, following the trail of terror, that is the fentanyl crisis all the way to small towns in the U.S. We'll bring you there.\par \par \uc2 First, here's what some of our Fox affiliates around the country are covering tonight. Fox 5 in New York as 10 shelters for migrants open on Randall's Island. The city moved the tents from Orchard Beach due to flooding concerns a few weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 The mayor's administration says it cost the city $325,000 to move those tents and the similar amount to set them up again.\par \par \uc2 Fox 11 in Los Angeles as the captain of a Santa Barbara based boat that caught fire near Santa Cruz Island in 2019 is indicted by a grand jury once again. Jerry Boylan is charged with abandoning ship and other failures. 34 people were killed in that accident.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, manslaughter charges were thrown out on a technicality.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at Tampa from Fox 13, our affiliate down there. One of the big stories there tonight, philanthropist MacKenzie Scott donates $84.5 million to \uc2 Girl Scouts USA\uc2  and 29 local Girl Scout councils. It is the largest single donation from one donor in the organization's history.\par \par \uc2 The West Central Florida chapter will receive $2 million, that's a lot of cookies.\par \par \uc2 That's tonight's live look outside the Beltway from SPECIAL REPORT. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: The causeway linking Sanibel Island to the Florida mainland has reopened after sustaining damage in Hurricane Ian. The three-mile causeway is back in use just three weeks after the storm, a big accomplishment.\par \par \uc2 Temporary repairs have been made, work will continue on permanent solutions there. Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  credits what he calls a can-do spirit.\par \par \uc2 In tonight's report on "THE POISONING OF AMERICA", the fentanyl epidemic is not just in big cities. Many smaller