\par \uc2 But back to the broader picture, back to the broader scope of things, ultimately the American people are rejecting the climate change agenda that the Biden administration has said is their number one focus, their number one priority. it's not that Americans don't want answers to climate change. They do. They just don't want the answers that Biden and his team are delivering, because the answers that they are providing are destroying the oil and gas industry and are making it hard for average, everyday Americans to fill up their gas tank and to fill up their grocery carts. It's very simple.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Howie, the administration, the president today saying, hey, listen the oil companies have it good. We are still allowing them to produce. And there was a bit of a fact check there. Take a listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN, (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Let's debunk some myths here. My administration has not stopped or slowed U.S. oil production. Quite the opposite. We're producing 12 million barrels of oil per day.\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE CHASE, MACK ENERGY CORPORATION: From day one, President Biden has signaled that he does not want oil and gas production on federal lands. He canceled \uc2 Keystone\uc2  pipeline. We can read the tea leaves. We hear the signals that you are sending.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: When we create a negative climate, you produce less. Isn't that true, yes or no?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It tends to be a chilling effect.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So chilling effect, if you look at the U.S. crude oil field production, there is a reduction. It's not significant but it's 11.31 million in 2020, 11.25 million in 2021. But there was a height in the Trump years. The bottom line is you talk to people in the industry and they say this administration is obviously against their industry overall.\par \par \uc2 HOWARD KURTZ, FOX NEWS HOST: Well, that's the broader 