orce, very weak, the Marine Corps, strong, the Space Force, weak nuclear capability as strong. Would you agree with that assessment, sir?\par \par \uc2 JACK KEANE, FOX NEWS SENIOR STRATEGIC ANALYST: Oh, yes, very much so. As a matter of fact, I'm speaking to the members of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  on this subject tonight. This is the eighth report that they have read on an annual basis. And for a number of years, they have been making this clarion call that you are giving emphasis to. And I'm delighted that you're doing just that.\par \par \uc2 But yes, I mean, we have a serious problem here. What we're trying to do with China is the same thing we do with the Soviet Union, and that is having effective military deterrence so that is no incentive for them to go to war with the United States. But the facts are, as that reports indicated and others like it, is that that deterrence has eroded through the years, Trace. I mean, I don't care what category you pick, the Chinese have more capability than we do. If it's airplanes more, if it ships more, offensive missiles more, defensive missiles more, land power more, that you put all of that together, and is dramatically significant.\par \par \uc2 And what we don't want is Mr. Xi's military leaders looking at the United States and say, well, they really are a declining power. They have a weak. We can take advantage of them, and in one full swoop will be the dominant world power, and that will force all of the United States allies to make a deal with us. They will be running the world order.\par \par \uc2 Now, some people will roll their eyes and say, oh, that's never going to happen. But yes, it can happen. That is the reality of what we're dealing with. We have got to get serious and wake up. So we wondered who is really in front of us.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: And I wonder, general, you just brought up President Xi. We know that he's about to we anticipate he will now take a third term and unprecedented third term