e with incomes below $125,000 a year or households that make less than 250,000 annually.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice-over): Now, strong bank earnings led to a big day on Wall Street. The Dow surged 551 today. The S&P 500 gained 95. The NASDAQ jumped 354.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (on camera): Iowa Republican Senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2  says new whistleblower documents reveal President Biden was aware of son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's business arrangements, and may have been involved in some of them.\par \par \uc2 Senator Grassley has written to the attorney general, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, and the Delaware U.S. attorney. Saying, the Bureau may have failed to follow up because of improper disinformation claims tied to Russia, prior to the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 President Biden has repeatedly denied speaking to Hunter about his business dealings. \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is currently under federal investigation for tax issues. No comment tonight from the White House, the Justice Department, the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , or the Delaware U.S. Attorney.\par \par \uc2 Tonight's midterm spotlight begins in New Hampshire, where Republican Senate nominee Don Bolduc is pushing back hard against the idea he's too far right and controversial for the state.\par \par \uc2 Republicans believe he does have a chance to pull off an upset over the incumbent \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fox Business correspondent Hillary Vaughn is in New Hampshire tonight.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 MAGGIE HASSAN\uc2  (D-NH): Don Buldoc is possibly the most extreme nominee for the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  that New Hampshire has seen.\par \par \uc2 HILLARY VAUGHN, FOX BUSINESS NETWORK CORRESPONDENT (voice-over): Senator \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 , says her opponent, retired General Don Bolduc is extreme, but he's being embraced by a former Democrat \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TULSI GABBARD, FORMER REPRESENTATIVE OF HAWAII: He is doing what is right because 