e Biden\uc2  has been an awful president, then how in the world could you vote for someone to be a rubber stamp for him? Look, Herschel needs to win. It's a big deal.\par \par \uc2 We're 27 days out. The people of Georgia have a chance to redo the error that they made in January of 2021, when they put \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  in office. He needs to be gone.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  quite simply cannot do the job. If he had any sense of decency, Sean, he would step down and allow someone else to run because he doesn't have the health ability to do this.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He doesn't have that, but he's the most radical candidate ever to run in the country.\par \par \uc2 And, Larry, I didn't even mention he wants, you know, Pennsylvania to be a sanctuary state. I didn't mention that as mayor of Braddock, Pennsylvania, he chased an innocent African-American jogger down the street, held him with a shotgun to his face. The guy did nothing and nothing even happened in the town to justify that. Imagine if a Trump did that or any Republican had done that.\par \par \uc2 ELDER: They've got two issues. Their issue is abortion and their issue is, by the way, these Republicans over there are systemically racist. They've got that and that's it.\par \par \uc2 They can't talk about prices. They can't talk about gas prices. They can't talk about the borders. They can't talk about the pull out of Afghanistan. All they can do is pound the table about abortions and about calling the people on the right systemically racist.\par \par \uc2 That's all they've got and come November, they are going to be toasts in the House and hopefully in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I hope you're right both of you. Anyway, thank you both. Clay, appreciate it. Larry as always, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Straight ahead, we're going to bring you the latest on the deep state as the Danchenko trial continues. Senator Ron Johnson is surging in the polls ahead of the midterms in November, 27 days from now. He will join us on the latest against the radical he is running against, Mandela Barnes. That's straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Big breaking developments in the state of Wisconsin and the Senate race tonight as Republican Ron Johnson, he continues to surge and now has a six-point lead according to a brand new poll from Marquette of likely voters. But like I always say, you have to run as if you're 10 points behind, take nothing for granted.\par \par \uc2 And also tonight, the trial for the sub source for Hillary Clinton's bought and paid for dirty Russian disinformation dossier, the Steele dossier is continuing in Washington this week, as we learn more and more about the \uc2 FBI\uc2 's abuse of power, how they've been politicized all about the Russia hoax, the spying scandal, an \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent literally testified the \uc2 FBI\uc2  offered \uc2 Christopher Steele\uc2  one million dollars to corroborate the lies in the dossier. But, of course, Steele couldn't corroborate anything.\par \par \uc2 And we also learned that Danchenko told Clinton operative Charles Dolan another source for the dossier that their goals, quote, clearly coincide. It was always one giant hoax designed to help Clinton and destroy \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2016, and clearly, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was on board with all of it.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, Wisconsin Senator Ron Johnson.\par \par \uc2 Senator, let me get this straight. So we know that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was warned by Bruce Orr in August of 2016 not to use the dossier, that it was a political document. They used it anyway, says on the top of a FISA application verified. We know that it was unverifiable because it was all false.\par \par \uc2 And then as we move forward and they have three subsequent renewals, in the interim, Danchenko tells them none of that dossier is true. But then they put him on the payroll, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is paying him. Then they offer, again, after they already passed off as the dossier to get the FISA warrant, then they offer a million dollars to \uc2 Christopher Steele\uc2  if he can corroborate it. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  -- is that -- that sounds like a bounty on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's head if they can prove it that he's guilty after the fact, after they got the warrant, then we'll give you a million dollars? Does that sound ethical to you?\par \par \uc2 SEN. RON JOHNSON (R-WI): Not at all, and this is another stunning disclosure. It was my staff that uncovered the classified footnotes to Michael Horowitz's FISA report that showed the \uc2 FBI\uc2  knew that the Steele dossier was tainted with Russian disinformation from Danchenko probably, as early as October 2016.\par \par \uc2 Certainly by January 2017, and yet they continued to use that had moved ahead with the Mueller probe, put this country through four years of political turmoil. Now, the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , at some of the highest levels, some of the actors in there are just corrupt. This needs to be fully disclosed, fully exposed and we need full accountability.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me go to your election. Your opponent Mandela Barnes is also a radical like Fetterman, like \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 . Your -- Mandela Barnes wants to defund the police, no bail laws, he supports that. He supported draconian COVID lockdowns.\par \par \uc2 He wanted illegal immigrants to get in-state tuition rates and legal driver's licenses. He's a thousand percent in support of the new green deal. He wants no restrictions at all on abortion, you can have an abortion up until, you know, the day before birth. He wanted to eliminate the legislative filibuster and he won't apologize for mocking Steve Scalise after he got shot on that ball field and nearly died, saying, oh, he just took one for the team.\par \par \uc2 No wonder why I think "Real Clear Politics" has you up by nine combined.\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: Well, Sean, you're just scratching the surface in terms of what a radical leftist Mandela Barnes is. I put him up against Fetterman any day. My problem is he just raised $20 million, and the media --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: From whom?\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: -- is completely on it out -- from wherever.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Anybody in Wisconsin donate to that? I doubt it.\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: Well, maybe, maybe a couple. But again, $20 million, he's out raising me. The media is amplifying his lies, his distortions, his character assassination.\par \par \uc2 So, you know, we've got to assume that this is a dead even race. We've got to run hard through the tape through Election Day. I'm going to need the resources, RonJohnsonforSenate.com. Your audience has been very generous. Don't let me down now. We need to raise the resources to -- so we can compete and make sure that he never becomes U.S. senator.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Twenty-seven days, it is critical that you remain in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 . Ron Johnson, thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right. Coming up, Project Veritas infiltrated the \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  campaign. You're not going to believe what they were captured on films saying. We have the tape, that's next, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. More troubles tonight for Arizona Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  and his struggling gubernatorial campaign as Project Veritas has now uncovered even more bizarre behavior inside of the campaign, including not wanting to debate Kari Lake. And evidence that Hobbs is trying to hide her radical anti-Second Amendment agenda from Arizona voters.\par \par \uc2 As always, we let you decide. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KATIE HOBBS\uc2 , CANDIDATE FOR GOVERNOR, ARIZONA: And he's like, oh, what do you do? And I was like, I work for a campaign, and I don't know why I said, that, cause I just did not want to have this conversation and I'm like shut up, shut up, shut up