t.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR (on camera): He loves fabulous.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: He's going to be on Jesse's show this week. I think maybe later in the week. It's about the unsolved Gilgo Beach murders. You're going to want to read it today.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST (on camera): That's it for us. Thanks, book lady. SPECIAL REPORT is up next. Hey, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL ANCHOR (on camera): Hey, Greg. When is Vice President Harris coming on your show?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No. We got the feelers.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Soon. Soon.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right. Thank you. Good evening, and welcome to Washington. I'm Bret Baier. "BREAKING TONIGHT", I'm standing at the board. Why is that? We are 28 days from the November midterms, and that will determine whether President Biden and the Democrats continue their control really over the legislative process or Republicans are able to capture the majorities in the House and or the Senate.\par \par \uc2 First, to look at some of the other headlines today. Russian forces showered Ukraine with more missiles and other weapons after widespread strikes killed at least 19 people.\par \par \uc2 The United Nations calling the attack, particularly shocking, and amounting to potential war crimes.\par \par \uc2 Testimony has begun in the trial of a Russian national who is accused of playing a major role in the fabrication of a document used in the Trump- Russia probe.\par \par \uc2 Igor Danchenko is accused of making false statements to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . Remember, this is the \uc2 John Durham\uc2  investigation.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice-over): Stocks were mixed today. The Dow gained 36. The S&P 500 and the NASDAQ fell in a technology-led retreat on recession fears. The S&P down 24. The NASDAQ lost 116.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (on camera): All right, it's our midterm watch four weeks from tonight. And we have a new round of power rankings with shifts benefiting both parties -- a few shifts as we look at the governor's races.\par \par \uc2 The one shift we have in the governor's race is Maine, moving to lean Democrat. A battle between the incumbent Democratic governor \uc2 Janet Mills\uc2  and the former Republican Governor Paul LePage.\par \par \uc2 Now if we take a look at the shifts in the house, there are a couple of three for the Democrats to for the Republicans are power ranking still as Republicans forecast victory with 231 seat majority, 204 for the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Now, let's take a look at the Senate. And really this is where it all comes down to the control of Washington. If the Republicans control the Senate, and they control the House, it's a much different ballgame here.\par \par \uc2 Our Power Rankings forecast remains the same as it was in September. Four toss up races. Those are the ones in the yellow right here. They are expected to be the key to the Senate majority. There is also the pink and the blue. Those are lean Democrat, lean Republican. They also could be a big deal.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 RAPHAEL WARNOCK\uc2  (D-GA): We need you to turn out not on November 8. We need you to turn out on October 17th. There is no such thing as Election Day, it is election season.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (R), SENATORIAL CANDIDATE, GEORGIA: There is going to be a debate. There is going to be a debate. And I told him to quit running from me. Quit running, because I will catch you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  and incumbent senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , as we head down here to Georgia. This is a tight, tight race. And just look back to what happened in 2020. The presidential in Georgia and there you see the tightest of wins for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the state of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 As we look at this race, the RealClearPolitics Average has Warnock up five 