eople are out on the streets. Crime is through the roof, drug addiction.\par \par \uc2 So it really is these are very, very serious issues, serious issues for all Americans and certainly for Pennsylvanians and issues that \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  does not want to talk about with anybody other than those that support him and that's mainly the unions.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Sara Carter, great report. Thank you for doing that.\par \par \uc2 You know what? Maybe I'll have to go to Braddock myself. I'll have to show up there and offer him the camera right in front of him.\par \par \uc2 All right. Sara Carter, thank you.\par \par \uc2 We turn tonight now to Arizona where it is a very important -- we have very important elections going on in just 29 days from now. We have Republican Senate candidate \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2  is now surging in the polls after last week's beat down and the debate against Schumer wannabe Senator Mark Kelly.\par \par \uc2 Also in Arizona, gubernatorial candidate Kari Lake -- well, she is now in the lead, pretty healthy lead, and has been very impressive. But her Democratic opponent, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , is proving to be an awful terrible candidate for many reasons.\par \par \uc2 The starter, she supports amnesty for illegal immigrants, actually made the comment. It's ridiculous to even be talking about the border. I'm like you live in Arizona. And that should be discussed. It's on top of mind of everybody of in the state of Arizona, in the state of Texas, border states.\par \par \uc2 On the state level, she voted against tax decreases at least 13 times, but says she's for them. Her position on abortion is even more downright extreme. In fact, Hobbs is fully in favor of late term abortion, including up to the very moment of birth. No restrictions at all whatsoever. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KATIE HOBBS (D), ARIZONA SECRETARY OF STATE: Abortion is a very personal decision that belongs between a woman 