uc2 FBI\uc2  on an entire religion, are you?\par \par \uc2 P. VAUGHN: Absolutely not, and don't think because they've been trained that makes it okay. When my kids go out to the car to go to school, and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  pulls up armed, running to the door, and one of them goes to the kids and holds the kids with a long gun inside of my driveway and does not let them go into the house. That is absolutely, as my wife said in the video, unacceptable and there needs to be accountability.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, it's one of the most shocking things I think I've ever seen. I have to ask you. So the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , the Department of Justice, I can barely say that phrase with a straight face is claiming that you're a violent extremist who is a physical threat to others. Do you embrace violence? Have you ever committed violence? What are they talking about?\par \par \uc2 P. VAUGHN: No, I have no idea. There's absolutely no evidence of that. The only place that has ever even seen is in the documents that they made up and used to justify in their mind and through the justice system. The ones that signed off on this needed some kind of justification in their own minds to go after peaceful people that disagreed with them politically.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Peter Breen, thank you for working on this case, for defending Paul Vaughn. Do you think that this is actually going to go to trial?\par \par \uc2 PETER BREEN, ATTORNEY, THOMAS MOORE SOCIETY: Well, Tucker when you've got a Federal prosecutor after you, I mean, we always have to plan for that.\par \par \uc2 You know, Paul wasn't even arrested by the local police for trespassing. But those who did, who were arrested, we're leaning on the tradition of Dr. \uc2 Martin Luther King\uc2 . He himself was inspired by Mahatma Gandhi.\par \par \uc2 I mean, this is the great tradition of American civil disobedience.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 BREEN: And it's not the sort of thing that you turn into a 10-year felony. Paul himself, we believe we have very strong defenses and hope to beat these charges at trial.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: And I hope you do so with a country that rises up on your side because this is -- he wasn't even arrested for trespassing at the scene, and over a year later, they send the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to his house in front of his children. It's really just beyond -- I appreciate both of you coming on tonight. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 P. VAUGHN: Thank you, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 BREEN: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So Kanye West, now known as Ye, showed up at Paris Fashion Week last week with a t-shirt that said White Lives Matter and completely blew up the internet, but he was not alone. He was sitting right next to his friend and our friend, \uc2 Candace Owens\uc2 . She joins us straight ahead to discuss the response to that.\par \par \uc2 Plus, the Surgeon General of Florida also one of the good guys was just suspended from \uc2 Twitter\uc2  for posting a scientific study that \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  didn't like. Hard to believe, but true. He joins us as well.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Joseph Ladapo is a physician, he has got credentials equal to any doctor in the United States. He is now the Surgeon General of the State of Florida.\par \par \uc2 So on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , he recently announced the results of an analysis conducted by the Department of Health in the State of Florida and it found, "An 84 percent increase in the relative incidence of cardiac related death among males 18 to 39 years old within 28 days following the mRNA vaccination." So, that is a bombshell. Eighty-four percent increase of death.\par \par \uc2 So, you'd think that would be the lead in "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 ," but no, everyone is trying to make those facts go away. \uc2 Twitter\uc2  removed that tweet, which described the findings.\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  also suspended Dr. Ladapo's account.\par \par \uc2 Now even in this country in 2022, under