2  uses a tactical nuclear weapon to try to win the war on Ukraine, saying quote, "we have not faced the prospect of Armageddon since Kennedy and the Cuban missile crisis. We've got a guy I know fairly well. He's not joking when he talks about potential use of tactical nuclear weapons or biological or chemical weapons because his military is, you might say, significantly underperforming."\par \par \uc2 You would think with such an alarming statement, the president would be ready to answer questions and assure Americans. But look what he did instead. Literally running away. Lawmakers are taking note of Biden's weakness on the world stage.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. TOM COTTON (R-AK): Anti-American dictators around the world will smell the weakness.\par \par \uc2 SEN. MARSHA BLACKBURN (R-TN): They see a weak Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOHN BARRASSO\uc2  (R-WY): Right now, we have a president who is very weak at abroad and at home. And he's brought it to himself because of his policies.\par \par \uc2 REP. KEVIN MCCARTHY (R-CA): He also has put America in a weaker position. He threatened our security by making us dependent on other nations.\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 TOM MALINOWSKI\uc2  (D-NJ): The Saudis and their friends in the United Arab Emirates believe that they can do whatever they want to the United States.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: So, there you have it, man. I'll go to you first, Nikki Haley. Welcome.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI HALEY, FORMER U.S. AMBASSADOR TO THE UNITED NATIONS: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: It -- why, why now? Why now Armageddon. I know that Putin first mentioned, I believe it was in March of this year the possibility of using nuclear weapons.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: You know, I mean, what's interesting to me, it's so unproductive. Every time he speaks, it's just unproductive because on one side you're putting fear in Americans, which is not helpful, and it really questions his leadership. On the other side, if he knows Putin so well, he would know he should not be saying This is Armageddon, because Putin is hearing that.\par \par \uc2 Instead, what he needs to do is he needs to have strong, bold leadership. He needs to say, look, if you do anything with nukes, they'll be held to pay. He needs to remind China and Iran, are you supporting this conversation? And you know, he needs to just stay strong in what we have. Our military can handle this. We're not going to need to send troops on the ground if something happens. What he needs to do is have deterrence.\par \par \uc2 When President Trump was in office, you didn't see these dictators doing this because there wasn't the weakness that we're seeing today.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And you know, Jesse, to that point, I mean, you know, when Biden starts talking about Armageddon and you know, you've got Russia now, which is, as far as I'm concerned, in a pretty weak position. It's he's losing in Ukraine. I mean, his forces are being drafted or forced to fight. People are trying to get out of Russia and we like built them up as like this nuclear power.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: Yes. You have to keep also the country calm in times like this. FDR did it. JFK did it. Bush did it after 9/11. Trump did it during COVID-19. Could you imagine if Biden were president during COVID? He probably would've flown to Delaware and put on a body condom and never opened up the rest of the country.\par \par \uc2 You have -- it's a very fragile time in the United States.\par \par \uc2 GERALDO RIVERA, FOX NEWS HOST: He didn't do that.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: We've just recovered from this pandemic. People are anxious. You have a recession. You have an open border and a crime wave. You can't be just throwing around words that trigger people like --\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You don't have a CEO go on an earnings call and just say, Ponzi scheme, but you just don't do that. Like my wife, if we went out to dinner, wouldn't just bring up her ex-boyfriend. You know, I'd be out of there before dessert came. You don't go to San Francisco and just scream, make America great again. You got to know the room and you got to say the right thing and.\par \par \uc2 He always says these things, if you notice it, fundraisers. He said the semi-fascist thing at the fundraiser.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Now he says nuclear Armageddon at this fundraiser. It's because deep down he's a very insecure man. He's always felt inadequate and that's why he is always blustering about his pushups and how great a test scores he got in college.\par \par \uc2 He's a liar. So, he kind of over performs in front of donors to try to make them feel like this or that, and it usually backfires. If, forget about what he says. Well, look what he's done. You have the cartels running the southern border. You have little rocket man throwing up a bunch of rockets over the peninsula. There's a land war in Asia, the Saudis our allies just turn their backs to us.\par \par \uc2 So, you can't then drop this bomb rhetorically, and then run away to Marine One across the lawn while the media is like, can you clear this up a little bit, Mr. President? He's just not smart enough to be the president, which would be fine under normal circumstances. But Kamala is the number two.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Wouldn't you say, Will, that doesn't -- doesn't President Biden himself create the circumstance? So, when Jesse talks about a normal circumstance, if this were a Trump administration or if it were a \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 's administration, I mean, you know, this kind of thing you wouldn't -- you wouldn't be seeing a lot of this.\par \par \uc2 WILL CAIN, FOX NEWS HOST: Well, to be fair, Judge, to be fair, Jesse, he has clarified that he's not joking.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: He's being very serious. And by the way, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is not joking. I'm glad to know this is a very serious issue. Can you imagine the nuclear diplomatic talks? I may, -- I may launch the nuke -- nukes, just joking. Not really thinking about it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: It's like the person always says to be honest. I don't like it how you lead with that. Why don't you just always be honest?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Jesse, you said you want to calm the American people. In order to be calm, the American people need to be enlightened. They need to be informed. They can't be kept in a state of constant confusion. And for the past two years, and not simply on this issue, the American people have been propagandized. They had not been told the truth on almost anything.\par \par \uc2 And now you have \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  talking about a preemptive strike. I mean, this is all sloppy. It is all half-truth. And the American people, in my estimation still when we go to war deserve to have a say in the issue.\par \par \uc2 If we are going to tread up to lines, I would like to see it being done democratically, and that means we need to be told the truth on issues, particularly when it comes to national security, and we aren't even getting half-truths on what's going on in Ukraine and Russia.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: But that's why there needs to be leadership.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And, and you know, Geraldo, with \uc2 OPEC\uc2  deciding that they weren't going to provide the oil that apparently, you know, Biden was planning on, that they were going to cut back on their oil production. The president is looking to Venezuela. He isn't looking to domestic production.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Well, I bet that is, you know, I guess you could question the judgment on that. Saudi Arabia is run by a family of snakes. I think you're all burying the lead. Ask \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  if he thinks \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is projecting weakness. His troops are being killed by our drones, by our artillery, by our missiles.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine is winning this war. And what he said is absolutely the American people should understand the. This is \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  ranting and raving about using nuclear weapons. He is cornered, he is bleeding, he is humiliated. His army is crumbling right in front of it.\par \par \uc2 Everyone, remember the movies, he also the "Red Army" in going to sweep through Ukraine in two weeks or three days, whatever it is. And here is Ukraine. They have humiliated Russia. Russia is dangerous because it is wounded and I fear, you know, you plan your life. You have your family and your grandchildren, and you build your house and you have a future.\par \par \uc2 And then this nut job is talking about using nuclear weapons. And we're pointing blame at the -- our president when it is the president of Russia.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: No, he says Armageddon. That means both sides get hit, Gerald. That means both sides will be hit.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And that --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You mean United States and Russia?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But you know what?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: This is -- read Follett's book "Never."\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: It starts with one nuclear tactical weapon. Then the other guy has another tactical nuclear weapon that's one percent more. Then the other guy is two tactical nuclear --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, but everybody knows that everybody gets destroyed.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I mean, it's the end of the world. It's horrible.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, everybody knows that. But the point is Saudi Arabia could be a country of snakes. Putin can be crazy, but we've got a president who is reacting like crazy as opposed to reacting as a dignified leader of the greatest country.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Look how he has armed Ukraine. Look at Ukraine, this army.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I don't care about Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: His words --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: From nothing --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Go ahead, Nikki.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: His words need to exemplify that. What he's doing is he's gaslighting instead of keeping people calm. Yes, we're strong. Yes, we will control this. Let the people feel that. Let our enemies know that.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: If we're on the verge of what you describe, I hope we could have sobriety and clarity in leadership.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes. And not like, the Russians are coming.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Yes, but, shouldn't --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Anyway.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Shouldn't we point to where the blame is, isn't the blame on Putin?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK. Coming up, Kanye West tearing into the left for trying to silence free thinkers during his explosive interview with Tucker. And we've got an exclusive new clip.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Kanye West, who now goes by Ye, sitting down with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  for a headline making interview. The rap icon and fashion designer slamming liberals and the media for trying to silence free thinkers like himself. Take a listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KANYE WEST, RAPPER: My so-called friends/handlers around me told me like if I said that I like Trump, that my career would be over, that my life would be over.\par \par \uc2 We are in a battle with the media, like the majority of the media has a a godless agenda and the jokes are not working. It was wild that I didn't know how close my own wife was to the Clintons, there was some manipulation. Me not saying I like Trump --\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WEST: -- was a form of manipulation. It just represents life and pro-life. Fifty percent of black death in America is abortion. So, I really don't care about people's responses that I perform for an audience of one. And that's God.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HALEY: You can catch more of Tucker's interview with Ye later tonight. And here's an exclusive new clip.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WEST: It drove me crazy to not be able to say that I like Trump. It drove. Because think about it's me. Imagine me not being able to say what I wanted because you got something you're thinking, but you're told you're not allowed to say it in public.\par \par \uc2 Well, I never actually told people that I like Trump when he was running because I was bullied by Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HALEY: I mean, there was a lot to unpack with that interview if you all watched it. Jesse, what did you think?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I thought the lanyard around his neck was an interesting fashion statement and the hat the beat said on it. The next year, 2023, I think you're going to see a lot of that in the streets pretty soon.\par \par \uc2 The left is tenacious with the way they keep their base in check. He has to be destroyed because he is a black star. And he's moving away from the Democratic Party. Nationally, the Democrats can't win if they don't have about 92 percent of the black vote.\par \par \uc2 So, if he walks away from the Democrats and you see a stamped of other black voters follow him. Democratic Party's future is toast. So, they can't have that. Now, it's also about the money because you cannot be Kanye West. You can't be anybody and expect to get showered with cash by woke corporate America when you say, you know, you're ultra MAGA and you're pro-life and they're killing black babies. That's too hot. That is too hot.\par \par \uc2 So, you're already seeing people kind of pull away from a medidas, is kind of getting squirrely. He had a concert canceled. The left says they don't believe in bullying. But if you're a black conservative, you will be bullied to death. The left says you can identify as anything. A tree, six genders. You cannot identify as a black conservative, and that's the truth.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: You know, it's always amazing to me if a minority has any conservative views. The liberals left, I mean, they just, their heads explode. They don't know what to do with it, and they come after us over and over and over again because we don't fit into their box.\par \par \uc2 What do you think about the fact that they continue to do this with minorities for just speaking their truths, Judge?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, you know, the truth is obviously you were the first female governor and you know, on my end, 20, 30 years ago, I was a first female, this, this, and this, and I got a lot of attacks. We do. Because they then can't control you. I mean, we don't fit into the narrative. If you are, if you're a minority, you've got to be with them and you've got to be, you know, subdued and be resentful of them being the conservatives.\par \par \uc2 But I got to tell you. I watched that whole interview last night. I was blown away by Kanye West. I really was. And I said to myself, I said, you know, Jeanine, you forgot this guy is a self-made billionaire. Billionaire with a B. OK. His mother, I believed, was an educator. And he is one smart guy. He talks about how you don't just believe what people are saying to you, you know, you look, you look beyond, and that's so obvious.\par \par \uc2 But when he was talking about the Kushners, for example, and Josh and Jared and what was going on, and he talked about Jared in the Middle East. Isn't it great what he did in the Middle East? But he was also doing other stuff in the Middle East. You know, he's nobody's fool.\par \par \uc2 And I was very impressed with him. I like a lot of what he said. I like that white lives matter. It's and it's not -- it's not just freedom of speech. He has the hutzpah to say it. He doesn't care. He doesn't care if he's in line. And I like that.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Well, you know, and the thing is he's a very talented musician. He's a great business person, but they are -- companies are now looking at reevaluating his endorsements.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Right.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: What is he supposed to do if they try and cancel him? How do you take on -- we already worry about how to take on the media. How does he take on the business community when they turn around and say, you know, and the other side of it is they love to say that minorities that are not liberal, that they're crazy, right? We're crazy because we don't know that we're supposed to be Democrats. How's they going to deal with the cancel culture on this?\par \par \uc2 CAIN: I think he'll deal with cancel culture in the business community with the same independence with which he forms his opinions. I imagine he will continue to be a radical, innovative entrepreneur that hopefully finds new avenues of commerce outside of corporate America, corporate global corporations.\par \par \uc2 Because as Jesse pointed out, you're talking about corporations like Adidas looking to distance themselves from Kanye. Judge, I did not know. I do not know what to make entirely of that interview. All I know was what I was watching was interesting.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CSIN: It was fascinating. This was an unvarnished, authentic human being giving you their opinion in all self-awareness. He steps back at moments in that interview and goes, I don't know actually how I'm coming across right now. And there -- there's such authenticity to that, that it just makes me want to hear more.\par \par \uc2 But my main takeaway is the same that both Nikki and Jesse have pointed out. And that is, the biggest reflection Geraldo in this, to me is the way people react to Kanye. It truly is. there's an ugliness to the reaction that reveals the ugliness inside people. And if I just may finish this thought. I'm going to use inflammatory language, but I don't care because I think this is exactly how ugly it is.\par \par \uc2 There are overseers on this plantation. They do not want an independent black man to have an independent thought, and they're willing to destroy his reputation for exhibiting that independence. And it is about the ugliest thing I can imagine to deny a human being their individuality, to form their own opinions because of the color of their skin. It is beyond ugly.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: You -- you've been around the block enough, Will, to know that Kanye West is a provocateur. He is doing this to get a reaction. I remember very clearly Katrina, 2005. And he said, George Bush doesn't care about black people. So that was Kanye West also, but he was on the exactly the opposite side.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 CAIN: But really -- are you saying he's inauthentic.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Let me finish.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Just to be clear, are you saying he's inauthentic?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I am -- I am saying that when you have someone who is an artist and a performer and an entrepreneur, how much of what they're saying do they really believe in, how much are they saying for impact and effect. He knew, Kanye, sitting down with Tucker, first of all, why did he choose Tucker to do this interview?\par \par \uc2 He knew that of all the people that make liberal's craziest, \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  would be the guy. So the area he sits with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , and he has the pendant that Jesse referenced. It doesn't have like a fetus in it or --\par \par \uc2 CAIN: It's an ultrasound.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Now, do people do that? Do people wear aborted fetuses, necklaces?\par \par \uc2 CAIN: No, no, no. It's ultrasound.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: That's an ultrasound.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Even if you take all of that aside, and I think that everybody wants to say that there's something wrong with him and how could he do this. And he had a lot to say. What I took away from it was, here is a minority male that is expressing conservative views. What I don't want is him being highlighted as an exception to the rule. There are a lot of --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Many.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: -- minorities out there, African Americans, Hispanic.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Latinos for sure.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Indians. You -- there are a lot of minorities out there who think like he does, and Republicans have to understand we have to expand the tent. There's a lot of Kanye's out there. He can only express it the way he did.\par \par \uc2 But I hope that we go and start really recruiting the rest of them because there are a lot of, especially African Americans who saw during COVID that, you know, here you've got liberals who think they can't pick the school for their children. Or they think that they can't go to the DMV to pick an I.D. so that they can go vote.\par \par \uc2 Minorities have been treated poorly by the Democrats for a long time. This is Republican's time to really see the -- seize the opportunity to have the discussion with them on why we focus to lift up everyone, not just a certain segment of the -- of the population.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Up next, President Biden giving out blanket pardons to marijuana offenders ahead of the midterms. But could it backfire?\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: America is going up in smoke. Literally, after decades of debate, President Biden finally announcing what I think is a long overdue executive clemency. A pardon for thousands of people with federal convictions for simple marijuana possession.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: The federal government currently classifies marijuana as a schedule one substance, the same as heroin and LSD, and more serious than Fentanyl. It makes no sense. So, I'm asking the secretary of Health and Human Services and the attorney general to initiate a process to review how marijuana is scheduled under federal law even as federal and local regulations of marijuana change.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: All right, good for you, President Biden. While most surveys indicate most Americans want pot legalized, 68 percent in two recent surveys. We want authorities to be laser-focused instead on eliminating the far more evil scourge of fentanyl, the synthetic opioid that is killing tens of thousands of Americans each year, many of them teenagers.\par \par \uc2 I dive deep into this topic in my new Fox Nation series, the Doping of America. Here is a sample.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Fentanyl is absolutely deadly.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: It doesn't give a damn what your zip code is.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: It's being made in bath tubs by people that can't even spell chemistry.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: It doesn't discriminate at all. It's an equal opportunity menace.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: It's delivered like a sandwich to your door.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: It's killing our kids. And that's where I draw the line.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: We found out the hard way.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: You know, dope stories, particularly, Judge, people's eyes glaze over. We know, we know, we know. But fentanyl, you know, I've been on this beat for half a century. I've never seen anything like this poison.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: This -- you know, 109,000 overdose deaths in the last 12 months 100 -- that's twice as many as we lost in the war in Vietnam for 10 years.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Exactly, exactly. It's 300 a day. And it's not by people who are drug users. It's people who are being poisoned in this undeclared war by China against the United States. But what's so interesting about this is that the President -- you know, it's great you're talking about pot, it's a wonderful thing. States have, you know, decriminalized it. Talk about fentanyl. Let's talk about what we're going to do to stop it. What we're going to do to punish those individuals who are bringing it into this country. With cashless bail, even if we do catch them, they're letting them out.\par \par \uc2 But you know, last -- when I was a DA, meth was a big thing. And we were passing laws to make sure, you know, people couldn't buy this much Advil or this much of that, you know, so that they couldn't mix it. But now, there is no stopping. There's no way you can stop it. It is here. The artery is here. They come to the southern border. It's all set up. We're sitting ducks now.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Your generation has kind of lived this -- not you personally, but this schizophrenic life. On the one hand, you don't want to admit the drug use, you don't do it publicly. On the other hand, you go home and you get loaded or in the backyard or whatever.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Not Jesse.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Not you personally. Not you personally. I made that before. But isn't this finally time where you have liberals, conservatives, libertarians, you know, right left, everybody -- the surveys indicate want pot legalized.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I smoked pot for many years and never inhaled, ever.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Did it stunt your growth.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It made me dumb. It did by not inhaling, but it did make me dumb. And I do not start off with a lot of brain cells, so any decrease in brain cells is catastrophic. I don't want my children doing it. I don't recommend people doing it. I couldn't handle it. I could not -- some people can handle it. They do it. They can handle it. Not me. So, I don't recommend it.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: How long did you not handle it? How many year?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I didn't inhale for many years, Geraldo.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: How many years?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Many years I did not inhale.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: It took him many years to discover.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Many years I did not inhale, all right. It was mostly contact ties.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I get you.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: But I'm still holding my breath the whole time.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Got you.\par \par \uc2 WATTER