e. That's why people I think were drawn into this permissive culture because they said the authorities don't know what they're talking about. I smoke pot. I'm not an addict. I didn't go to harder drugs. I am -- I'm a functional person. I am more functional than my dad who's drinking all the time.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: But it's not a big deal. And that's why \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is focused on marijuana. Look, the administration says that nobody is in federal prison for simple pot possession.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I totally disagree it's not a big deal.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Well, I'm going to explain to you why it's not.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: How many people went to jail for half a joint?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: There's no one in federal prison right now for possession of marijuana. There's not one person.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: This is -- this is -- it involves five to 6000 people, but it's (INAUDIBLE).\par \par \uc2 CAIN: I'll explain it to you, so you'll understand it's not a big deal. This involves five to 6000 people.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Don't talk down to me.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: I'm not, Geraldo. This is fine. I know you're not even like that. This is five to 6000 people not who are in jail but who have their records expunged so they can get jobs, so it doesn't sit on their records.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: So they can vote.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: And you know what --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: So they can vote.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: You know what though, I'm fine for second chances in society. Here's why it's not a big deal, because this is like student council running thing and put a Coke machine in the -- in the commons. This is what's going on student loan forgiveness with this -- with this marijuana program. He won't talk about fentanyl because it is a big deal and he can't solve it. There's no cheap votes to get. It's tied to our border policy, and it's tied to our China policy. So, we can't solve fentanyl. It's hard. He won't talk about it.\par \par \uc2 He'll talk about mari