es of this reckless slander, while police departments across the United States can't find willing recruits, they're down 300 400, sometimes 600 officers in one department. Huge shortfalls mean more communities are vulnerable to the rising crime that we're seeing all over the country. That is the shameful truth.\par \par \uc2 Biden and the rest, I'm sorry, the frauds, they're hucksters. And they're cruel to the bone while pretending to be the most compassionate. It is their policies that are dashing the dreams of countless Americans, especially those who are most disadvantaged. They must never be trusted with power again, until they reform their party and rediscover its roots in people like FDR and JFK.\par \par \uc2 A return to sanity, frankly, would be nice at this point. Now, who knows when that will happen, if that will happen. But in the meantime, we're going to have to redouble our efforts to restore our economy, restore our schools, our foreign policy, and yes, our patriotic spirit. And that's "The Angle."\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is \uc2 Hogan Gidley\uc2 , former White House Deputy Press Secretary and Director of Election Integrity at the \uc2 America First Policy Institute\uc2 . Also with me is Ben Domenech, Editor-at-Large for the Spectator and Fox News Contributor.\par \par \uc2 Ben, it's great to see you guys tonight. We just learned that Biden is now, in his administration, is begging OPEC not to continue with its plan to dramatically cut oil production. So now Biden - it has a twostep going on, he's crushing our energy production here and then prostrating America before despots. How was this good for us?\par \par \uc2 BEN DOMENECH, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, it's super. It's super easy, Laura. I mean, every time that this prices go down, that's something that you can thank President Biden for, and every time they go up, it's someone else's fault.\par \par \uc2 Look, everything that you laid out there in "The Angle" is completely correct. This is an