d accepting of what was said to him. He was going to clean things up in the city, but it is -- we're far from there.\par \par \uc2 ZELDIN: Yes, no doubt. This is the reality right now. And it's the combination of pro-criminal laws they're getting past like cashless bail. You have district attorneys refusing to do their job as we see stories coming from \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  and others. You have (inaudible) judges releasing people back out on the street in cases where the prosecutor is asking for bail.\par \par \uc2 And then you have an issue with mental health. People out on the streets, and they feel like they're in control of our streets. And as you point out the original story up in Marist, why do you have kin evicted felons who are homeless there in that situation at all.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Loaded up with guns and explosives in a hotel room. And not to mention, the poor woman who got her head kicked when she was on her way to her job at an airport. She was on this morning talking to Bill Hemmer. It's also heartbreaking. Another person who obviously shouldn't be on the street, the mental health issue is out of control. And like I said every day, sadly, there is a front page story.\par \par \uc2 Thank you very much, sir. Good to see you, \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , gubernatorial candidate in the state of New York.\par \par \uc2 ZELDIN: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 DELK ADAMS: -- as we watch this, all these tragedies unfold. Our heart goes out to that family. I was at Parents Weekend last weekend, in a college too. The last thing I was thinking about when I was getting coffee in the lobby. So our hearts go out to them. Thank you very much. Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 ZELDIN: Got it. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, Joe Concha on the new speculation swirling about President Biden's intention and what he has just said about the 2024 race.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JEAN-PIERRE: If \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  says it's, you know -- look, here's wha