thing else. And, of course, it's also impacting wages.\par \par \uc2 So these are the same people who have who ran for office, condemning the Republicans, condemning the work of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , condemning Trump's economy, and what they have ushered in here every enemy of this country is laughing at.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats have done more damage to this nation than enemies have over the last several decades, certainly al Qaeda could never have imagined, even the attacks on this country did not thrust us into this kind of desperation.\par \par \uc2 And right now, you've got experts, according to "The Intercept" saying that we're giving Ukraine $110 million a day. That is there -- that's an estimate -- and we're fighting over at some point how much money to give Florida and other hurricane-affected states.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wow, great point.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: So who are this -- this Biden administration really concerned about? The new global environment or the American people? If you just look at things on the ground here, it's certainly not the American people and it's not the American family. They're demonizing us while they send all of our money it seems abroad.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, I can't say it any better. You're dead on accurate, and people are suffering as a result.\par \par \uc2 You know, if I were to write the book, \uc2 Stephen Moore\uc2 , and it was going to be called had a record an economy for dummies, everything they're doing would be in that book. I don't know short of an election when in November, in 39 days, and then we have to win the White House back in 2024. Short of Republicans getting back in power, I don't see an answer.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MOORE\uc2 , ECONOMIST: Well, first of all, Sean, you're exactly right. I mean, if you -- if people always ask me is what -- is what the Biden administration doing on the economy intentional? And I say I don't think it's intentional but if it were intentional and you did want to destroy a country's economy, you do two things, Sean.\par \par \uc2 First, you would destroy its currency, and when you've got inflation out of control, that's what it does. It destabilizes your currency.\par \par \uc2 And the second thing you would do, Sean, is destroy its energy supply, and that's exactly what hap -- what has happened under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Now, here's what I'm why I'm so frustrated with our current situation. By the way, the numbers just came out today confirming I've always asked -- are we going to go into recession, I said, we're already in a recession, Sean, come on. The first two months of this -- two quarters of this year were negative, that was confirmed today.\par \par \uc2 We're in an economic morass. We're on a financial meltdown right now as a country, and my biggest frustration, Sean, I think this is something you agree with is this -- it was completely unnecessary. We should be booming right now this economy. We came out of COVID.\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was still president, we wouldn't be talking about a recession. We wouldn't be talking about 8 percent inflation. We wouldn't be talking about, you know, these declines in family incomes. The economy would be booming. And that that is I think my greatest regret about what's happened.\par \par \uc2 And when you put people like \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , and people like \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  in charge of the economy, they can't get us -- they don't have any kind of experience. They know not what they're doing. And who -- you talked about -- you talked about the president and the vice president, you're right. They don't know anything about the economy.\par \par \uc2 But who does, Sean? Who knows anything about how to run anything in this White House? Nobody does.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: \uc2 Steve Moore\uc2 , well said. Tammy, great job as always. Thank you both.\par \par \uc2 All right. Now to a brand new report from John Solomon at justthenews.com. According to hi