te their own records and trying to pretend they're actual moderates when they're not, despite all the overwhelming evidence of far left radicalism.\par \par \uc2 In the state of Michigan, for example, Republicans there on the rise, gaining momentum and vowing to undo all the damage done by the Democratic machine. And that's \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  and the damage done by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here with more, Republican gubernatorial candidate in the state of Michigan, Tudor Dixon is with us.\par \par \uc2 Now, you're running against the governor -- correct me if I'm wrong -- that said that she didn't want the people of Michigan to go to Florida. She went to Florida and got caught lying about going to Florida. And isn't this the same governor with draconian shutdowns that herself was seen in a restaurant that was supposed to be closed, whose husband was launching his boat when other people weren't allowed to launch their boats? Is that the same person you're running against?\par \par \uc2 TUDOR DIXON (R), MICHIGAN GUBERNATORIAL CANDIDATE: Absolutely. Even more extreme, she shut down businesses like greenhouses and threatened them with jail time. And they came to me, and they said, but you could sell marijuana curbside, we couldn't sell Easter lilies. It's the same growing process. That's how bizarre it was in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Isn't this the same governor that also said that she created 84,000 jobs in Michigan, when in fact you lost 84,000 jobs?\par \par \uc2 DIXON: Yes, we have tens of thousands of jobs that are gone, and she continues to lose jobs even from our legacy industry. We are seeing \uc2 Ford\uc2  who's now invested and a half billion into Kentucky and Tennessee breaking ground in Louisville, Kentucky, we have battery plans opening in Ohio and Indiana. But these are not jobs that are coming to Michigan.\par \par \uc2 We are reaching out to the unions and saying, why are you supporting someone who is watching your jobs leave the state and ignoring it? In fact, when \uc2 Ford\uc2  announced, she said, I think we didn't know \uc2 Ford\uc2  was leaving the state.\par \par \uc2 Can you imagine the chief executive officer of the state not knowing your - - one of your largest businesses was going to build elsewhere?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What about her position on abortion -- I understand I believe without restriction. Her support of the group \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2 , that's the group on tape that said, "What do we want? Dead cops. When do we want them? Now."\par \par \uc2 The fact that she's bought into this climate alarmism, her position on domestic energy production. Where is she in all those issues?\par \par \uc2 DIXON: Energy is I think one of scariest ones because she is trying to shut down a pipeline in the state of Michigan. We already see rising gas prices in Michigan again. We already see rising prices to heat our homes in Michigan again.\par \par \uc2 But she continues to say she wants to shut down line five, which would be catastrophic for the entire Midwest. But for Michigan, it's the propane for heating homes, it's our jet fuel out of the Detroit airport, it's our diesel fuel for trucks and it's the starter chemicals for plastics which is what we make in the state of Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Her energy policies are the most radical. You talk about all of her policies are radical, her education policies are radical, her energy policies. And you talked about her abortion policy.\par \par \uc2 You're right. She wants abortion up to the moment of birth. She doesn't want parental consent. She doesn't even want you to be a doctor to perform an abortion.\par \par \uc2 It's more radical than anything we've seen in the United States. The only other place we see that is China and North Korea.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Tudor Dixon, it looks like that race has tightened quite a bit. You have an opportunity to defeat Whitmer, I think one of the worst governors in the country. We're going to follow the race closely and we wish you the best. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right. Now, we go to the state of Washington. Believe it or not, there is a real opportunity for a massive flip from blue to red as Republican Tiffany Smiley is surging in her race against the incumbent \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 . This is absolutely now a winnable race. Murray is on defense over her record, which is the same as Biden's record. She basically is a hundred percent with Biden.\par \par \uc2 And the record of the far left Democratic socialists, take a look at your screen. A new poll from Robert Cahaly and Trafalgar, look at that, this race is neck and neck within the margin of error.\par \par \uc2 Here to explain more, Republican Senate candidate in the state of Washington -- I didn't think I'd be saying that often -- Tiffany Smiley is with us.\par \par \uc2 Tiffany, I am hearing from friends that live in the state of Washington that you could win this race that this would be the upset of the year and it is now within the margin of error. What's it going to take to get you over the top?\par \par \uc2 TIFFANY SMILEY, GOP NOMINEE FOR U.S. SENATE IN WASHINGTON: Yes, Sean, we will absolutely win this race. I have been at this for over months, listening to the voters of Washington state. I was 11 years old when \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  was first elected and I asked everyone in every single room I go into, is your life any better? You know, over the last two years, is your life any better?\par \par \uc2 You know, Senator Murray stood with President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  with the American rescue plan. She was even touted for her efforts in that, and we were told we're in a better place now.\par \par \uc2 We are not in a better place now. Patty Marry allowed a billion dollars to go to criminals. She's touting the Inflation Reduction Act, which does nothing and this isn't coming from me. This is coming from the CBO to actually combat inflation, and if there was any hope to combat it