't do it in studio with them because I can't -- I can't take in that second hand smoke.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Am I going to be able to get in more than three questions because you won't stop talking? You won't do it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, I won't. It's impossible. No, no, you know that, because --\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Oh, please.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And by the way, talking to you pot, kettle, by the way. There you go.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Me? Not for that, not for that. I'm a listener. I'm a listener. I'm a good dude.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I better be careful, I don't want to become your partner. I know what happened to the last one.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: God, there you go. There you go. I'm not going there, Sean. I'm not going there with you. Not today.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Listen, we're proud of you. I'm -- I'm honored to call you a friend. It's called "Know Mercy". Stephen A. Smith, can't wait to be on the air with you. What day am I on? Do you know?\par \par \uc2 SMITH: You're coming on a week from today.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: A week from today. Okay.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: From today, I'm ending the week with you because people will need to recover after listening to your dribble. They'll need to recover, OK?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They need the whole weekend to recover.\par \par \uc2 SMIHT: Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Stephen A., my good friend. God bless you. I'm proud of you.\par \par \uc2 And straight ahead, crime surging all across New York and an EMT was stabbed 20 times, murdered in broad daylight. Also, the victim of that brutal subway attack, she will join us with a message for the mayor and the governor of New York. She may lose her eyesight as a result of that beating.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (NEWSBREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And tonight, more senseless, violent crime all across New York City as we're now learning that a female FDNY EMT who was working on 9/11/2001 fatally stabbed in an unprovoked attack in Queens, New York, yesterday. Police say the 34-year-old male suspect followed the victim, began stabbing her repeatedly. The victim identified as Alison Russo Elling was a 25-year vet of the FDNY, a 9/11 first responder and just months away from retirement. Sadly, it's only one of many despicable acts and violence all across the city of New York.\par \par \uc2 Take a look at your screen, September 20th surveillance footage. We showed you this once before, from the Howard Beach subway station in New York, showing a homeless man attacking and beating an innocent woman. I mean, pounding on this woman, blows to her head, upper body.\par \par \uc2 Now, the suspect, 41-year-old Wahid Foster is a career criminal, with at least seven prior arrests, including beating his own grandmother to death back in 1995. Why is this guy still out on the street, as New York is now continuing their practice to coddle violent criminals. Why are they doing that?\par \par \uc2 And, of course, victims -- they're the ones that suffer.\par \par \uc2 All right. That video in the subway, joining me now is that victim. Elizabeth Gomes is with us, along with her husband, Clement Tucker.\par \par \uc2 And, Elizabeth, I hear you -- first of all, I watch this. My heart goes out to you. I'm so sad, so sorry that you had to go through something like that. I honestly and I'm a mix I do mix martial arts, I can't believe you even -- were able to stand up after this meeting and now there's a possibility you might lose your eye?\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH GOMES, VICTIM OF NYC SUBWAY ATTACK: Yes, that's right.\par \par \uc2 CLEMENT TUCKER, HUSBAND: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When you -- when you've heard about this attacker's record, killing his own grandmother, all these other -- all this history of violent crime, and he's out on the street to beat you without mercy like this, what do you have to say to the politicians that are allowing this to happen?\par \par \uc2 GOMES: Right, like how could it allow somebody like this to be in the street who's the person who's supposed to be making sure he's inside and getting treated or whatever it is to make sure he's -- where he's supposed to be and harming people, like you're absolutely right, we're like where are these people that's supposed to be keeping these people inside.\par \par \uc2 Let me -- let me ask you this. You may lose your eye over this. This guy had seven prior arrests, still out loose, killed his grandmother. It wasn't that long ago. What do you say to \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , your governor? What do you say to your Mayor Eric Adams about this? What do you want them to know and what do you want them to do?\par \par \uc2 GOMES: Well, I want to know because of the negligence and keeping us safe and making sure we have the proper security that we need in our city that something like this has to happen and an innocent person has to lose the eyesight, have to have a change of life, have to think about where they're going to go from here on forward if I don't have a way to get my eyesight back. So --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Is there a chance you could lose sight --\par \par \uc2 GOMES: Where is the security --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Is there a chance you'd lose sight in both eyes?\par \par \uc2 GOMES: Well, like they say, if too much strain go to one side of the eye, then there's a chance. Yes, later on down the line there is a chance, but that's what we're trying to prevent. You know, any kind of changes like that, like we you know sometimes it hurts to even think about what's really going on.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Our prayers are with you. Clement, that's very nice. I know you're taking good care of her. We're praying for you. We're praying that your eyesight gets restored and we're praying that the law has changed so this doesn't have to happen to other people.\par \par \uc2 We'll update the story in the future. We wish you the best to help. Thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 GOMES: Thank you so much. Really appreciate it. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's so unnecessary, so preventable.\par \par \uc2 More HANNITY, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Unfortunately that's all the time we have left this evening. As always, thank you for being with us. You make this show possible. We can't thank you enough. Please set your DVR. So you never miss an episode of HANNITY.\par \par \uc2 Don't forget, for news any time, foxnews.com, hannity.com.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled, Laura Ingraham, "THE INGRAHAM ANGLE" is next. Have a great weekend. We will see you back here on Monday with 36 days to go until the midterms.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020221001ei9u00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Hurricane Ian's Devastation Continues; Government Employees Were Stealing From You During COVID; Waste Your Money: What Government Does Best In A Crisis; Stimulus Resulted In Double Dip Of Taxpayer Waste; Opportunists Dined Out On Your Suffering; Man Who Relishes Spotlight Claims Otherwise; The Angle Was On To Fauci Before Anyone Else; The Fauci Grift Is Stunning In Scope; Bombshell Report: Fauci Got $5 Million Richer During COVID; Indiana Republican Congressman Candidate Jennifer-Ruth Green Interviewed On Her Views Of Abortion; Hurricane Ian Makes Landfall On South Carolina; President Biden Appears To Forget Recent Death Of Congresswoman; Model Hailey Bieber Accused Of Cultural Appropriation Over H