par \uc2 The official who's in charge of overseeing the distribution of the relief has called this the biggest fraud in a generation. It was the theft of as much as $80 billion, or about 10 percent of the $800 billion that was handed out in that Paycheck Protection Program. Now, remember, that's on top of the 90 billion to 400 billion believed to have been stolen from the 900 billion COVID Unemployment Relief Program. That's a lot of money.\par \par \uc2 The second part of this story surrounds the tidal wave of inflation, that all this unchecked spending, and then the fraud actually caused, the adverse effects of pumping trillions into the U.S. economy with no safeguards. The Fed predicted that the COVID stimulus alone is driving 30 percent of the current inflationary effects.\par \par \uc2 So that means all those big fat frauds sitting at their Mexican resorts during COVID, collecting their checks, Zooming into meetings, ordering their \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's with their COVID down payments, helped cause the inflation mess that we're in now.\par \par \uc2 The third part of this story involves the other opportunists, you know, the so-called public servants, they ended up using our national suffering, in some cases, to build their own brands, while they padded their investment portfolios.\par \par \uc2 I'm talking first about Dr. \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , who President Trump should never have put in charge of our COVID response. Now, looking back on the entire saga, we see all along, it was all about Tony. The cover of InStyle, a place on TIME's 100 Most Influential documentaries, all the profiles, and who could forget the children's books? But he wants you to believe this fame thing was never anything he asked for.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DR. \uc2 ANTHONY FAUCI\uc2 , DIRECTOR, \uc2 NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF ALLERGY AND INFECTIOUS DISEASES\uc2 : I didn't seek it out, but I became the symbol for people which made it an unrealistic things like, you know, they're kind of cute, but it's, you know, bobbleheads and candles and things like that.\par \par \uc2 ANDERSEN: I do have some at home.\par \par \uc2 FAUCI: Yes They send them to me. So what I've learned to do is not get taken away, ego wise--\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So gross. From the beginning of the whole pandemic, I had my doubts.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You're satisfied with all of the transparency coming out of China today about the trajectory of the disease and the origin of the disease?\par \par \uc2 FAUCI: In my direct interaction with Chinese scientists and Chinese health officials, I can believe what they're telling me.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'm surprised that you would say that given what we know about China's pattern of lying about critical issues, Dr. Fauci.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: With all due respect to Dr. Fauci's expertise, no one elected him to anything.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now we see that my early suspicions about Fauci, his sucking up to China, and his entire pro-lockdown approach proved to be on target. But it wasn't until May of this year that we began to really understand the other ways that Fauci was benefiting. That's when our friends at OpenTheBooks published this bombshell.\par \par \uc2 "Between fiscal years 2010 and 2020, more than 350 million in royalties were paid by third parties to the agency and \uc2 NIH\uc2  scientists who are credited as co-inventors." Well known scientists receiving payments during the period included \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , who received 23 so-called royalty payments. Now when Fauci was asked about this and specificity, he tried to dismissed the concerns.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. RAND PAUL (R-KY): Can you tell me that you have not received a royalty from any entity that you ever oversaw the distribution of money in research grants?\par \par \uc2 FAUCI: You know, I don't know as a fact, but I doubt it. According to the regulations, people who received royalties are not required to divulge them even on their financial statement.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: If there's nothing to hide, why the secrecy Tony? And how self- satisfied he always comes across? And tonight, we might have further proof as to why. The same OpenTheBooks group that uncovered the \uc2 NIH\uc2  royalty payments, published this. "Fauci's net worth increased by a whopping 65 percent or $5 million during a three year period of time that includes 2021." In other words, during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 So as the elderly were left to die alone, because of the stupid COVID rules he supported, as children were being robbed of their education because of closures that he supported, and as you were missing church and weddings and graduations, because of the edicts that the COVID taskforce wanted in place, Fauci was getting rich.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Dr. Fauci said the school closures are quote "worth it." I wonder if he's spoken to folks like these.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: --children in our city, many of who are students, are missing out and losing out on opportunity, because out schools are closed.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The common sense that has been applied to shutting down schools has been abysmal. Who lobbies for the single parents?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Who lobbies for the children?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Who lobbies for the children?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, not \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 . He only had time to lobby for himself.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Adam Andrzejewski, CEO and Founder of openthebooks.com and Jason Chaffetz, former House Oversight Committee Chair and Fox News Contributor.\par \par \uc2 Adam, you said getting these documents has been a painstaking process. So why is the \uc2 NIH\uc2  slow walking?\par \par \uc2 ADAM ANDRZEJE