ctually serve to regulate and are involved in, I don't - or if that's not happening, tell us what is happening?\par \par \uc2 Adam, here's another theft. More than a third of COVID-19 recovery funds in 21 developing countries were scooped up by big corporations. Now those are the findings of report released Wednesday by the Financial Transparency Coalition. Adam, explain this for us because I have to say even I was flabbergasted when I heard that little factoid.\par \par \uc2 ANDRZEJEWSKI: So Laura, this is exactly why we need Read the Bill legislation and everyone can come to our website at openthebooks.com and sign the petition, which would give us 72 hour legislative time out, so legislators would simply read the bill. So the people, the politicians, the pundits so we can see what's in these massive things.\par \par \uc2 Think about the $2 trillion CARES Act that was passed at the height of the pandemic in March-April and nobody knew what was in there. Up to $400 million worth of initial Paycheck Protection Program loans, 95 percent of those turned into grants were paid to companies owned by the Chinese Communist Party.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh my god.\par \par \uc2 ANDRZEJEWSKI: \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  out of Florida got that stopped on the next COVID aid bill, but that's why we need to read the bill.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Jason, you are there, and I know this has happened so many times that you want to pull your hair out. I hear this about China, you know, getting any benefit whatsoever. \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  was still out praising this today watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 NANCY PELOSI\uc2  (D-CA): When you talk about the American Rescue Plan, it was there to make sure that we put money in the pockets of America's working families. That gave people more of a chance to rebound from COVID and it was about fairness.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Jason, and IG report released this week says that at one point, the American Rescue Plan was sending out $200 million in fraudulent or wrong payments every month. So what are the Republicans have to do to when they get back in charge here?\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Well, look, there are literally hundreds of billions of dollars that went out in waste, fraud and abuse. First of all, you need to starve the beast. Stop sending out this money until you can actually control what's there.\par \par \uc2 The other thing that I would love for them to do is, there need to be term limits on members of Congress, but there need to be term limits on the federal bureaucracy. Those people in those higher echelon, those people also have to have term limits, because you're not going to get fresh new voices and new looks at things unless you actually have those as well.\par \par \uc2 But they have got to uncover this. It's going to take years to unravel this. But they got to send some people to jail. And I really, really want to see the likes of Jim Jordan and Senator Paul and Ron Johnson go after \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  and his wife and figure out how much money they were making decisions that they and they alone were making.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You bet. Jason and Adam, thank you both tonight. So important.\par \par \uc2 All right. Last night, "The Angle" explained that the current destruction of our economy, our schools, even our superpower status, well, that is the Democrats' actual intended goal. They've come to despise America, our traditions, our heritage, our history. They have complete disdain for our Constitution and believe our founding was illegitimate, because they believe our founders are unabashed racists.\par \par \uc2 Now the goal is simple, a leveling of the old America in order to create something new - a new order that gives them all the money and all the power. Since most people won't voluntarily, of course, choose a lower standard of living and less freedom, the Left knows that this radical change must be forced on the people. And this is being done through fake emergencies and phony self-generated crises.\par \par \uc2 So they cite climate change to justify the rapid phase out of gas powered cars. And of course, the banning of gas appliances and the cancellation of permit leases for oil drilling. They cite systemic racism to justify their new twisted school curricula, and their DEI dictated corporate hiring practices. And they point to amorphous domestic threats to justify partnering with social media giants to moderate online content, which of course, just means banning opposing political views.\par \par \uc2 Today's Democrats will always have a reason to take away your money and your freedom. And they found their new model for what this new America should look like. Can you guess what it is? Go west, my friends go west, to California, where there's not a lot of dreaming happening anymore, frankly.\par \par \uc2 It's hard to find a state that's more screwed up than the ones Golden State, which of course makes it the logical exemplar for the screwed up Democrat Party. Of course, California still has its natural beauty and amazing potential. But the Democrats super majority running the place has really done a number on it.\par \par \uc2 After they declared themselves a sanctuary for illegal immigrants, they also became a sanctuary for criminals, freeloaders, drug addicts, the homeless, and now they're adding something new to the mix. Late last night, Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  signed a law that would make California a safe haven for families who want to mutilate their children with trans surgeries and other treatments.\par \par \uc2 Now think about this, when gas is backup at $6 a gallon in California, this is what \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 's priority is. When homeless are camped out in pretty much every municipal park in the state, this is what their priority is. When crime is skyrocketing up and down the state, this is what their priority is.\par \par \uc2 And yes, this is exactly what the modern Left wants for the rest of America, a government that forces change on the voters, not one that serves the voters. So I want you to keep all of this in mind when you vote in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Kevin Kiley, Republican, California State Rep and congressional candidate. It's great to see you tonight. Thank you for joining us. You know, I have such great affection for California. I'm a member of the California Bar. I lived out there for a while as a young associate at a law firm, and I've spent a lot of time in California, a lot of family there. But it's California the model, should it be the model for the rest of the country?\par \par \uc2 KEVIN KILEY (R), , CALIFORNIA STATE REPRESENTATIVE: Well, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  sure seems to think so. And thanks for having me tonight, Laura. He said again, and again, that California is a model for the nation. And what you just said, California has so much going for it. I love California, a lot of the people who are leaving love California, too. They just hate the politics.\par \par \uc2 And you know, you mentioned how they use it's all about sort of control. And it reminded me of what \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  said on April 1 of 2020. This was less than a month in the whole COVID situation. He said that this was an opportunity for, quote, "a new progressive era, and opportunity to reshape the way we do business and the way we govern."\par \par \uc2 He said that out loud, that this was a chance to just fast forward this entire progressive project, which is exactly what just happened. Which is why for 170, straight years, California had a growing population, but under \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  for the last two, for the first time ever, our population has declined.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, in California, when I was growing up in the 1980s, and 90s, California was the place people wanted to move to. Now it's the place that people want to move from. I mean, that dynamic alone 