ation seems to care. Instead, they're out there focused on more important issues like renaming the \uc2 Atlanta Braves\uc2 ? Really?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: The president hosting the \uc2 Atlanta Braves\uc2  today. Wondering if you or the president has any thoughts about some of the controversial about the Braves name, the so -called tomahawk chop? Any thoughts on --\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: So we believe that it's important to have this conversation. We should listen to Native American and indigenous people who are the most impacted by this.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, there's a top story of the day.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now, "FOX and Friends" weekend co-host Pete Hegseth, along with former Trump White House chief of staff Reince Priebus.\par \par \uc2 Reince, start with you. Forty-two days, Americans can change course dramatically. They're -- the Republicans have now laid out a vision. It's very specific. Now, they will be able -- they'll be able to implement their plans, stop the Biden agenda, and then if we win in 2024, we can get the country back on track.\par \par \uc2 Will that happen in 42 days?\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS, FORMER WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF: Yeah, I think it's going to happen and I'll tell you why. While Biden is debating whether the Braves' name needs to be changed, 74 percent of the American people out there say that the economy is the number one issue, followed by gas, followed by public safety, followed by inflation, and what you laid out is exactly what the problem is that the American people see, which is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in their administration that this conduct this result of their conduct is purely intentional.\par \par \uc2 All you have to do is go back to look at day one. I challenge everyone to go back and look at the first week of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's presidency and go look at his executive orders. This -- what di