ou know, we are winning it every single day because our children's lives depend on it.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: All right -- all right.\par \par \uc2 SMILEY: Anyone can join us in spite and holding \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  accountable, @smileyforwashington.com. This will take all of us, but we can do it.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: All right, Tiffany Smiley, thank you very much. We'll be watching this race closely. And as I said, \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  is invited to come on and talk about her race as well. Very interesting to watch this, and we thank you for your time today. Good to have you here.\par \par \uc2 SMILEY: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, could it come down this time to yet another run off in Georgia. A new poll shows Democrat Senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  in a statistical dead heat.\par \par \uc2 So, we may have to wait weeks to find out which party will control the Senate was a cliffhanger. Last time in 2020, could be a cliffhanger again, this time around.\par \par \uc2 Senior national correspondent Rich Edson joins me now, reporting live from Washington. Hi, Rich.\par \par \uc2 RICH EDSON, FOX NEWS CHANNEL WASHINGTON CORRESPONDENT (on camera): Good more afternoon, Martha. You know, it takes at least 50 percent of the vote to secure this election outright without a runoff with a tight race between Democratic senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  and the Libertarian candidate. This one could very well need a second round.\par \par \uc2 A recent Marist poll has Warnock up five percentage points. Some polls have tightened over the summer or shown this race is within the margin of error. That's the case with this recent Atlanta Journal-Constitution survey, it gives Walker a slight lead, less than two points.\par \par \uc2 Abortion has become a major issue in the campaign. Warnock says women should have the right to choose. 