ean politics unless they're very bored or work at some think tank and that's understandable, but it's a shame, really, because if you look closely what's happening in Europe, you can learn a lot about what's happening here.\par \par \uc2 Despite the castles and the funny accents and the smelly cheese, Europe is not actually that different from the United States, at least in this way. European leaders run their countries pretty much the same way our leaders run our country. They yammer on endlessly about democracy, but then at the same time, they do their best to avoid democracy's most basic requirements like free speech and representative government.\par \par \uc2 A few years ago, the Prime Minister of Italy at the time, \uc2 Paolo Gentiloni\uc2 , bragged to the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  about his plans to "bring more social justice to the country" by which he meant importing many more thousands of poorly-educated economic migrants from the Third World into Italy. "We are very open on migration," he said. "We are saving lives at sea."\par \par \uc2 Oh, saving lives, huh? Congratulations. You're such a good person. But the question is, and it's a relevant question in a democracy, what of the people who live in Italy, that would be your constituents, think of that idea?\par \par \uc2 Well, as the Prime Minister explained, he didn't care. "A demand for more democracy not only is wrong, it's even dangerous." You following this? You run a country in the name of the people. You're not a king, you're a democratically-elected leader. You run it in the name of the people who live there, but at the same time, it's "dangerous" to let the opinions of those people influence your decisions. Does that sound familiar? Oh, it does, because it's exactly the kind of democracy that we live in, which is to say a fake one.\par \par \uc2 In fact, there is no majority in any country on Planet Earth that thinks open borders are a good idea or that considers global warming the single biggest problem, or that thinks it's wise to quarantine the entire population because of a flu virus.\par \par \uc2 No large group of people anywhere wants these things. But in the West, everybody gets them anyway because politicians don't care what you think. Your opinion is dangerous. "Shut up, racist."\par \par \uc2 So, it goes without saying this can't last. A system like this cannot endure forever because it's inherently unstable. You can't tell people they're in charge of their own government (It's a democracy, we promise) and then ignore over decades their most strongly held opinions on things that matter. That doesn't work long term. They will rebel, guaranteed; and the best you can hope for is that they will do it peacefully.\par \par \uc2 In Italy, they seem to be doing just that. This summer, a conservative populist called \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  started showing up with strong support in the polls. Meloni was no radical. Her views would have seemed perfectly ordinary just a decade ago, but because she resolutely refused to bow to the twin gods of climate and mass migration, people panicked. The President of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , in fact on camera, commanded Italians not to vote for her. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 URSULA VON DER LEYEN, \uc2 EUROPEAN COMMISSION\uc2  PRESIDENT: So, we'll see if things go in a difficult direction. I've spoken about Hungary and Poland. We have tools. If things go in the right direction and people, as a body, that is always, where always governments have to be accountable to play an important role.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Oh, if "things go in the wrong direction." In other words, if voters disobey "we have tools." Oh, you do, do you? Well, that sounds like a threat, because of course it is a threat, but it turns out Italians are so desperate, they no longer care. They're not afraid, and they're not afraid because neo liberalism, which that lady is just espousing, has destroyed their country.\par \par \uc2 Energy prices in some places in Italy are now up more than 400 percent over last year. Why? Well, a pointless war on Ukraine and self-destructive climate policies. It's not an accident and everyone knows it.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, parts of Italy are becoming flat out dangerous. That hasn't happened before outside of Sicily, but it's happening now. Why? Everyone knows why, and government statistics show why. It's migrants who are driving much of the crime, a huge amount of the crime.\par \par \uc2 So, these aren't mysteries, but you're not allowed to acknowledge them in public, period. In some places, it's illegal. But Meloni is one of the very few politicians who doesn't care and has been willing to say the obvious, the truth, out loud and as a result of that, because she has been willing to say what everybody actually knows, last night, her party called Brothers of Italy, won an overwhelming victory in Italy. They took both majorities in the Houses of Parliament.\par \par \uc2 By Italian standards, in fact by American standards, this is a revolution, but unlike most revolutions, the person at the front of it can actually explain what she is about. She can articulate it in a way people understand. She's smart. This is part of the speech she gave earlier this year that led to last night's results. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GIORGIA MELONI, BROTHERS OF ITALY PARTY: Everything we stand for is under attack. Our individual freedom is under attack. Our rights are under attack.\par \par \uc2 The sovereignty of our nation is under attack. The prosperity and well- being of our families are under attack. The education of our children is under attack.\par \par \uc2 In front of this, people understand that in this age, the only way of being rebels is to preserve what we are. The only way of being rebels is to be conservative.\par \par \uc2 They will try to take everything away from us, but they cannot take away who we are. And you know what? Cherishing who we are, knowing what we stand for is all we need to face this challenge.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: She is not kidding. She's as serious as the moment we are currently living through. "Our rights are under attack," she said, "The sovereignty of our nation is under attack" and critically "the prosperity and well-being of our families is under attack" and that's true. That's why it's resonant, because it's real and not just in Italy. It's true here. American families are facing the very same onslaught from the very same poisonous ideologies.\par \par \uc2 The difference is that in this country, it's rarely acknowledged except on the fringes. Meloni is not on the fringes, she is the new Prime Minister of Italy, she will be and she is saying it out loud.\par \par \uc2 Contrast that to what's happening in the United States.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans just spelled out what they're running on. It's a document called "The Commitment to America." It's fine. Probably not much in it, you disagree with it. Have you heard of it? No, you probably haven't. You probably haven't read it. Nobody really cares. Why? Because there's nothing real in it. There's not a single word in that document about the attacks on the American family that you see every day. That's at the center of most people's concerns. How are my kids? Will they have a life that resembles mine?\par \par \uc2 That was called the American Dream. Does it still exist? Will they be able to afford to live the way they grew up? Will they have the opportunities that we had? No.\par \par \uc2 People are upset about that. Why wouldn't they be? But nobody says it and that's odd because we know and now it's been proven that when politicians are brave enough to tell the truth about what's actually happening, they tend to be rewarded for it.\par \par \uc2 Once again, here's the incoming Prime Minister of Italy and as you watch this, ask yourself if you would vote for a candidate like this if you had the chance in our country.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (GIORGIA MELONI speaking in foreign language.)\par \par \uc2 TRANSLATION: Why is the family an enemy? Why is the family so frightening? There is a single answer to all these questions. Because it defines us. Because it is our identity. Because everything that defines us is now an enemy for those who like us to no longer have an identity, and to simply be perfect consumer slaves.\par \par \uc2 Chesterton wrote, more than a century ago -- let's see if I can find it -- "Fires will be kindled to testify that two and two make four. Swords will be drawn to prove that leaves are green in the summer. That time has arrived. We are ready." Thank you\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So that's the person is being described all over American television, including on channels they should know better as "far right." That's far right, really? Because she acknowledges that American families are under attack. Of course, they are. You think it's accidental? No, and she explains why and it's simple.\par \par \uc2 If you want to establish totalitarian control over a country, of course you have to destroy the family first, because nobody with deep family loyalty, the one thing every person should have, no one who has that will ever pledge absolute obedience to a politician. Why would you?\par \par \uc2 So, if you want absolute obedience, you have to sever family ties and that's why State schools brainwash your children with values that you despise and then instruct your children to turn you in as a thought criminal if you object. That's happening. It's not your imagination and it's happening for a reason.\par \par \uc2 Wokeness is not just a political ideology. It's not just something annoying that emerged from college campuses that we can ignore. It's a State religion that supplants actual religion, which is also being destroyed. There's a reason the strip bars and the liquor stores and the weed dispensary stayed open under COVID, but the churches didn't.\par \par \uc2 If you can't draw the connection between those dots, you're missing it, but Meloni didn't miss it. She understands it perfectly. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MELONI: Only a few months ago, \uc2 European Union\uc2  bureaucrats brought a document, hundreds of pages long, telling us that in order to be inclusive, we had to exclude all references to Christmas -- Jesus, Mary, and all Christian names were to be removed from all official communication -- will we surrender in front of this? No, we will not. We will fight it. We will find it standing tall.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, they hate your family, they hate your religion, and you don't actually have to put up with it because it's a democracy, and you're supposed to be in charge, you being the population. That's a radical message? God, family, country. That's not radical. It's hard to imagine a more wholesome message, a more pro-human platform.\par \par \uc2 Fascists don't believe in God because God is a rival to their power. Of course. This is a person publicly professing faith in God. That's so scary, but it is so scary. It's so scary to the people running and benefiting from our current system and why is that?\par \par \uc2 She's not the first person to say this. People have said it before, but she has just been rewarded for saying it. That's the point. The population likes it. This is what they actually want. They're not that worried about global warming. They don't want open borders. They think the woke stuff is absurd. They want to say what they think.\par \par \uc2 And now, it's obvious, because she just won and so even in this country, the people running and benefiting from a deeply corrupt and doomed system are hysterical. Watch the reaction to that.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MEDHI HASAN, MSNBC HOST: I want to start today by talking about a politician on the right we should all be worried about, who is on the rise today, a politician who has brushed off accusations of fascism.\par \par \uc2 JOE SCARBOROUGH, MSNBC HOST: What separates us from, let's say, Italy, who elected a fascist.\par \par \uc2 EDWARD LUCE, "FINANCIAL TIMES": She is from fascist roots.\par \par \uc2 ABC ANCHOR: A very far right political party whose roots go back to post World War II neo fascist.\par \par \uc2 DAVID IGNATIUS, MSNBC: A party that has its roots in Italian fascism.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: "Its roots in Italian fascism." Define that for us, if you would, Joe Scarborough? Oh, I'm sorry. You're an idiot. You can't.\par \par \uc2 But the point is, fascist means unacceptable. Whatever this chick is saying, you're not allowed to agree with. They're very worried that that many Italians do agree with it. So, she has to be completely unacceptable.\par \par \uc2 Don't read further. She's a fascist, and in case you missed the theme, a recent "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " piece on Meloni mentioned fascism or fascist 29 times, not a subtle newspaper. Apparently, she's on the verge of invading Poland. We should be worried. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHRIS LIVESAY, CBS NEWS CORRESPONDENT: They said it could never happen again. One hundred years ago, Mussolini marched into Rome, plunging the country into two decades of dictatorship in an alliance with Hitler and a second World War.\par \par \uc2 Today, the fascist party is gone, but many say these are their political heirs -- The Brothers of Italy, once on the fringes, they've ballooned into the biggest party in the country. Now their leader, \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  is poised to have the most hard-right government since El Duce.\par \par \uc2 The 45 year old firebrand insists she is no fascist, just a proud conservative and nationalist, comfortable nonetheless with some of the hallmarks of Italian fascism like this motto:\par \par \uc2 (GIORGIA MELONI speaking in foreign language.)\par \par \uc2 LIVESAY: God, fatherland, and family\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: "God, family, country." Well, that's pretty scary. Not a word about climate or equity, but again, it's their hysteria and their total unwillingness to ask obvious questions that lets you in on the secret, which is they're panicked because they know the current system is doomed and in fact, what happened last night in Italy is the best case scenario for them, because it was a peaceful transfer of power. That's a good thing. That's what you want.\par \par \uc2 In a democracy, people should be allowed to have some influence on the priorities of the government that claims to represent them and when they speak in an election, the people who've been repudiated have a moral obligation to pause just for one second and ask, "Why didn't they like what I was offering them?" They have a right to an opinion. In fact, their opinion is at the center of our system, this democracy, but they never ask themselves that. They never take any blame whatsoever. They didn't in 2016, when Trump got elected. They immediately blamed Putin or Macedonian bot farms.\par \par \uc2 They never blamed themselves and so they never learned a single thing from what happened. That's exactly what's happening, not simply in American television, but also in Italy and also in the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bureaucrats who drove Italians to seek a change peacefully at the ballot box are completely unwilling to learn from that vote. They'll just keep ramming their unpopular garbage down the throats of a deeply ungrateful nation until there's an actual rebellion. Let's hope that doesn't happen.\par \par \uc2 All of this got us thinking about politicians in this country who dare to tell the truth and are attacked for it and Kari Lake was at the very top of that list. She is running for Governor in the State of Arizona and she joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, thanks so much for coming on.\par \par \uc2 So, you were one of the very first American politicians to weigh in on this election. You were paying attention, which I appreciate. What do you make of this?\par \par \uc2 KARI LAKE (R), ARIZONA GUBERNATORIAL CANDIDATE: I'm so excited. You know, it's funny, I looked this Italian, Miss Meloni up, when I heard about her about a week ago, and I couldn't find any, just straight up information on her.\par \par \uc2 Everything was, she's a fascist, she's a racist, she's this, she's that, and then I thought, "Wow, this is somebody who I can relate to because they're doing the same thing about me."\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 LAKE: And it makes me realize that if they're not calling you all of these slurs, if they're not attacking you, then you're probably not truly representing the people of your country.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: But it's just so interesting that this is a change if you're elected in Arizona, it will be a change. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was a change. The people who are rejected by voters in this representative democracy that we have never for one second learn anything from that rejection. Why do you think that is?\par \par \uc2 LAKE: I don't know. I can't get into their minds. But I mean, I think of the Marjorie Taylor Greens' of the world, the Congressman \uc2 Paul Gosar\uc2 's, the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's of the world, what's happening in Italy, myself -- the people who are truly understanding what's happening in this country, which is we're losing this country are the ones who are being attacked.\par \par \uc2 And I'm on the campaign trail, we're working six to 10 events a day. We're working really hard and I had somebody reach out to me the other day and say, "Kari, you are fearless. You are so fearless. You're not afraid of anything." And I stopped him. And I said, "Actually, I have great fear. I'm not afraid of the fake news. I'm not afraid of the globalists. I'm not afraid of anything that I'm facing on the campaign trail. I am not afraid of the cartels. What I'm scared to death of is what happens if we don't step in right at this moment and do something. I'm afraid of the world that our children will live in. That's what scares me to death."\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Amen.\par \par \uc2 So, you spent your career working in news, so you know how totally fraudulent it is. It's a burden some of us bear who work in this business. Maybe that's why you're not afraid.\par \par \uc2 LAKE: Thank God for you. Thank God for you.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Because you know, it's fake.\par \par \uc2 LAKE: Truly.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Kari Lake, Godspeed. Thanks for joining us tonight.\par \par \uc2 LAKE: Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So we went out to Las Vegas last week to meet with a really interesting person. If you follow sports, you've heard of him. He runs the UFC. His name is Dana White. And he is in a lot of ways and inspiration in that he didn't care what they said about him. He persisted and he turned the UFC into one of the fastest growing sports in the world, even in the middle of a pandemic.\par \par \uc2 We thought it would interesting to learn how did he do that and why. Our interview just ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So we went to Las Vegas last week to meet and interview the President of the UFC, Dana White and we're not exactly sure what to expect. We were highly impressed.\par \par \uc2 It turns out that his experiences of the past several years are very similar to the experiences of millions of business owners in this country. The difference is, he found a way to keep going.\par \par \uc2 He told us that during the COVID lockdowns the government tried to shut him down completely. And of course, the media were intent on helping the government do that. \uc2 CBS\uc2  for example reported that: "Dana White has an epidemic on his hands."\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " reported that, "Epidemiologist blasts UFC President, Dana White," of course, there was never any evidence that Dana White had in any way contributed to the pandemic. It was a lie.\par \par \uc2 So the point of the story, however, is that Dana White kept UFC alive during the lockdowns, he did not bow to pressure. He persisted, didn't lay off a single person. It's an inspiring story. Here is part of it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Dana White, thank you for having us.\par \par \uc2 DANA WHITE, PRESIDENT, UFC: Thanks for having me.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I've never done an interview with human blood on the floor and I like it.\par \par \uc2 So, the first thing I noticed having watched a lot of UFC is how small this is. The Octagon in real life, there is no place to run.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Yes, so this is a smaller version of it that we use here at the Apex, but when we go into arenas, we use a bigger one. This would look like a matchbox in some of the arenas that we go to.\par \par \uc2 The one that they fight in on Pay Per View in arenas is much bigger.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: What do the fighters think of being locked into space this small?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: It's funny because we used to talk about, you know, fights are probably more exciting and more -- there is more engagement in a smaller Octagon, but it's not true. We actually did studies on it and there are just as many finishes in the big one as there are on the small ones.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Interesting So, this is your arena where a lot of your fights take place in your building in a world you completely control.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: One hundred percent. So this, ironically was built, we were literally putting the last nails and screws in this place right when COVID hit. So, it couldn't have been more perfect if we were actually allowed to use the arena because they shut Nevada down. And, you know, we couldn't even do it in our own facility that we controlled and that we could have created a bubble here, but they -- you know, the government wouldn't let us.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, you're in the sports business. And I should say, you're really the only figure left in American sports who controls the sport.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Right.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So that's not a model that exists anywhere else. But you're responsible for the sport, and now you can't have in-person events. Where does that leave you at the beginning of COVID?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Yes. It was tough. You know, I say it all the time, COVID is the -- was the toughest thing I've ever had to navigate in the history of this company, and if you look at where we came from, that's actually saying something.\par \par \uc2 But my attitude and my thought process was, this is America, we don't quit, we don't give up and we definitely don't run and hide in our houses. So, I figured there had to be a way.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So COVID happens, companies start laying off big percentage of the workforce, they don't know how long the quarantines are going to remain in effect. They're indefinite and they've got these payrolls they have to meet. You did not lay people off.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: No. My people -- a lot of my people around here have been with me for a long time, 10 to 20 years. And, you know, we do events every weekend. These people work hard. They've been dedicated to this company and to me.\par \par \uc2 And you know, if you look at COVID, it's probably the scariest thing that ever happened in the history of my life, and to all of a sudden just dump my employees the minute something bad happens, it's just not the way that I'm built. It wasn't going to happen, no matter what.\par \par \uc2 I'd rather have seen the whole company burn and go down in flames before I would hurt my employees.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So you paid everybody?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: I paid everybody.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So that introduces a math problem, though, into your life, because you've got a lot of money going out and no money coming in.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Right.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, what do you do?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Figure out how to put on events, you figure out how to keep the show alive and keep it going.\par \par \uc2 At the time, you know, I'm close to the Royal family in Abu Dhabi and they were doing testing over there. Well, if they were doing testing, we could do testing here, it was just a matter of figuring out how to do it, and figuring out a place where we could go where we could build a true bubble, and make sure that people were safe and put on events.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So you went to Abu Dhabi.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Yes. So originally, we were looking for an island. Islands made sense.\par \par \uc2 Mike Tyson called me and had some guys, I don't remember what island it was, that said you can come to our island and do the fights. There was literally no way.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: It was a private island?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: There was no infrastructure there. No nothing. So that was out. And then we ended up talking to Abu Dhabi and they suggested Yas Island in Abu Dhabi and it was really the only true bubble that existed in sports, because they brought people in. There were workers. The workers in the hotel, the workers in the restaurant, all the people that were at Yas Island were tested before they went there, and they were there for weeks, being tested regularly before we even got there.\par \par \uc2 Then the people that we were bringing over, we tested, flew over on our own private plane that only we were on, got to the island, we were tested again, and tested multiple times up until the event happened and then everybody would go home. It was the only true bubble that really existed.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, that allowed you to keep your sport on the air when everything else was shut down.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Right.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Why didn't everyone else do that?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: I don't know. I don't know. You know, what, I took a lot of heat, took a lot of bullets, took a lot of --\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: On what grounds?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Criticism. That's what the media does. The media does nothing. They never built anything. Nobody depends on them for a paycheck, but all they do is sit back and criticize.\par \par \uc2 "I'm going to kill people. I care more about money than I do human life." I heard it all. And "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 ," as you can imagine was blasting me daily.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Because you were trying to keep your employees paid and fed and keep your business going.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Right. Because you're trying to figure out solutions to problems. You're trying to, you know -- everybody felt like there was this narrative during COVID that if you didn't run and hide, you were reckless. You were a monster. You didn't care about other people -- and the list goes on and on.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So how did you take that criticism?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: They were working.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: They were working. That's a good point.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: They were writing stories every day.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: They were criticizing you.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: These guys had nothing to worry about. They were writing horror stories every day, and they were all working.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: But how did you keep that out of your head? I mean, it's easy to say I don't care about criticism, but when you are criticized like that in "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 ," the biggest newspaper in the world, it's hard to keep it out of your head.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: It really wasn't. You know, I live in like my own little world over here, in our own little bubble and I knew that if I went, and I figured out a way to do it, that my team would go with me and I knew that the fighters would fight.\par \par \uc2 So as long as we were all aligned and everybody felt the same way, and, you know, we weren't a hundred percent aligned. There were some fighters that were scared and a little nervous. And they didn't have to fight if they didn't want to. Nobody was being forced to fight.\par \par \uc2 If you wanted to fight you could, because that's how these guys feed their families, too. And how, you know, so, yes, I kept everybody working.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Was there any COVID death around you? I mean, "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 " said you were killing people, did you?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: There was no COVID death. You know, there were people who caught COVID and I was sending out weekly videos to my employees. Listen, enjoy this time that you have with your families. Relax. If you get COVID, or anybody you care about gets COVID, make me your first call and we'll get you taken care of, we'll get you looked at.\par \par \uc2 If you need toilet paper -- toilet paper was a big deal at that time -- we'll get you toilet paper. If you need food, and you can't get groceries or you need anything, call us and we'll take care of you.\par \par \uc2 Through COVID, me and my team became stronger than we've ever been and then once it was time to get back to work --\par \par \uc2 I mean, there are still companies today that people aren't back to work yet. My whole team has been back to work, like maybe like, three to four weeks into the beginning of the pandemic. We've been working straight through this whole time.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Did you lose anyone?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: We didn't lose anyone. No. We didn't lose anyone.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, you were loyal to your employees and you never had staff problems.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Hundred percent. I was loyal to my employees. My employees were loyal to me for the last 20 years, when the [bleep] hit the fan, I was very loyal to my people and they were loyal back and we've gotten through this thing. We threw one hell of a Christmas party last year and we had a blast and we partied and had fun.\par \par \uc2 And we brought Kid Rock in. Kid Rock came and played.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: No way.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Kid Rock came in and played for everybody, and it's almost like it never even happened here.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, you're basically showing the rest of the country how to stare down adversity and achieve and thrive despite it. It is a pretty impressive story.\par \par \uc2 Did any politicians call you to say "I'm really impressed by what you're doing?"\par \par \uc2 WHITE: You know, the President at the time did. You know, obviously, he was very into it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: You know, Florida was massive for us. You know, Florida, I would -- I would equate Florida to Abu Dhabi during these times.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, what did Florida do?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: You know the Governor, Governor DeSantis and the Mayor of Jacksonville, Florida told us "Come on in. We'll host you here. You can do your events here."\par \par \uc2 I have fighters from all over the world. So, the fighters that were from other countries, we all brought into Abu Dhabi. All the Americans, we fought down in Jacksonville, Florida. So we were still able to run our business like nothing was even going on other than we didn't have fans. We didn't have a live gate because of them.\par \par \uc2 Then \uc2 Tilman Fertitta\uc2 , down in Houston, was saying "I need you here in my Arena in Houston. How quick can you get here?" I said, "I'll be there as soon as your mayor lets me," you know, so we figured out a date and then then it became Houston, Texas; Jacksonville, Florida; and Abu Dhabi.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: You just heard Dana White say that one of the people called him was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Most people who run big businesses would not admit that, Dana White is happy to talk about his decades' long relationship with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It's interesting and that is straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: It's interesting to find out what famous people are actually like. A lot of prominent people are not that great, honestly. And you know that because they're not loyal to the people who work for them.\par \par \uc2 Loyalty is a prerequisite for an honorable life and Dana White has demonstrated it to the people around him. He is also loyal to his friends, even if his friends turned out to be the most controversial people in the world and Dana White is friends with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . They've been friends for decades.\par \par \uc2 And as a result of that, he spoke when Trump asked him at the Republican National Convention in 2016. He took a lot of heat for that, but he didn't care. He's not afraid, and that maybe it's the most obvious point about Dana White. He's just not afraid. Maybe because he doesn't work at some dumb nonprofit or "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 ." He's in a very violent sport.\par \par \uc2 In any case, he is not afraid to tell us about his relationship with Trump and it was worth hearing. Here's part of it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So I talked to Trump yesterday about you and he described you as the only essential person in all American sports. He said, "You could take key people out of any sport and the sport would continue. If Dana White left UFC, there couldn't be UFC." Now, I don't know what you think of that assessment, but it did make me wonder how long -- you're the same age as I am, 53. How long are you going to do this?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Well, I love him, and I appreciate that. And hopefully, I've built a business over the last 22 years that no matter who comes and goes, will last and continue to grow.\par \par \uc2 I also know for a fact that when I do leave, the right person needs to be in place to take over. Because there is a formula to this business. Many other people have tried it. Many people are trying it right now as we speak, and have not been successful. And I know why they haven't been successful. I know exactly why they haven't been successful and when I watch them, you know, running their businesses, I just -- I just shake my head and go, "Yes, yes."\par \par \uc2 So hopefully, when I do decide to leave, which isn't going to be anytime soon, because I still love what I'm doing, still as passionate about it as I was day one, I have the right people in place. Plus, I've built a phenomenal team here. Phenomenal team.\par \par \uc2 You know, no one guy just does anything. You know, you need a really great team to surround yourself with and I've done that. And that's why, you know, there's no way that I was going to let any of these people leave when COVID hit.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I knew that you knew Trump, and I knew you're a Trump supporter, broadly speaking, I didn't realize you were like a legit old friend of Trump's because of work. Can you explain that?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: He's a very, very good friend of mine.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been such a good friend to me. Since the day I met him, we originally -- when we bought this company, this company had such a bad stigma attached to it in the sport, that we couldn't even get into venues, venues didn't want us. And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  saw that this thing could possibly be big. Plus, he's a sports guy. He loves sports.\par \par \uc2 And he offered us to come and do the event at the Trump Taj Mahal in Atlantic City. Cut us a very fair deal. We went down there, and we did two events with him. He showed up for the first fight stayed till the last fight. And you can imagine back then Trump brand here, UFC brand down here.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: But he took us in and he was great. Everything that ever happened to me in my career after that day, the first guy who reached out and said congratulations was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Whether it was a letter --\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Amazing.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: We were on the cover of "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 " one time, and he said, "I always knew you were going to do it, Dana, congratulations," and sent me the paper. He sent me a pen one time congratulating me. You know, always sending something and saying congratulations, like a guy who is genuinely happy for your success.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: There aren't a ton of those.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: No. And then came the day he was running for President and he reached out to me, he called me one day and he said, he started the conversation like this: "If you don't want to do this, I completely understand and there are no hard feelings, but I would be honored if you would speak for me at the National Republican Convention." I said, "I'll be there."\par \par \uc2 WHITE (\uc2 RNC\uc2  CONVENTION 2016): Donald was the first guy that recognized the potential that we saw in the UFC, and encouraged us to build our business. He hosted our first two events in his venue. He dealt with us personally, he got in the trenches with us, and he made a deal that worked for everyone.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: He said, "You're the best man, you've always been a great guy to me. You've been a good friend of me." And I spoke that day. And let me tell you what, after that day, when I spoke for him at the convention, our friendship went to a whole another level.\par \par \uc2 This guy has been so good to me. It's unexplainable.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: That's fascinating.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: And a window into something that we don't get to see, did you take a lot of abuse for that? Or did people just accept that this is a real friendship?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Oh, yes. You know, I am in the abuse business, we take abuse every day. So, I don't know, you'd have to explain to me what the abuse on the Trump side would be. You know, I get it. There's people -- you know, listen, this is what is sad. You know, obviously, I did not vote for President Biden. He's my President. He is the President of the United States right now and I'm an American. I don't dislike or hate anybody who voted for Biden.\par \par \uc2 The fact that you're the type of person that would actually hate somebody because of who they voted for shows me exactly who you are. I don't want to know you anyway.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: You're not my kind of person.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: That's a really good attitude.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: And I don't want to be friends with you either. So, the feeling is very mutual. And it's not because of who you voted for, it is because of how you carry yourself.\par \par \uc2 Who you vote for what you decide to do with your life means nothing to me, that's your own personal choice. In America, this is a free country and you can choose to vote or do whatever you want to do with your personal life.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: "This is a free country." Well, it's nice to be reminded of that. It's also nice to see a man who is loyal to his friends. You've got to be loyal to your friends more than to some greaseball politician who is promising to save your soul. He is lying. Your friends are not.\par \par \uc2 Working on a documentary for "Tucker Carlson Originals" about the UFC and Dana White. We got a lot of access to facilities, met a bunch of the fighters. We think it's interesting. It'll be out this winter on FOX Nation.\par \par \uc2 So, if the animal part of you is starting to tell the higher reasoning part of you that this is turning into a police state, don't ignore your instincts. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has targeted his major political opponents of course now the war against dissent has reached a new level. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  targeting Christians for their religious beliefs. That just happened. I am not making it up. Details straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, you tell yourself that it isn't happening because you don't want to believe it's happening because you're an American and you believe in our institutions, which for the course of your entire life have not really been corrupt, but now they are. The Justice Department, especially under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the DOJ spent the year trying to crush \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's political opponents and now they're moving to the tier beneath.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, dozens of \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents arrested a Catholic pro-life activist in front of his wife and children. The man's name is Mark Houck, now to give you some idea of who he is here he was in December of 2020. See if you can spot the criminal behavior.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MARK HOUCK, PRO-LIFE ACTIVIST: I was at an abortion mill last week. I turned the corner to go home and there is the abortionist at the end of the block. I've been praying for this man. And there he was and I've been praying for 20 years that I would meet him.\par \par \uc2 So, I went up to him and I said to him, keep his name out the airwaves, but I said to him, "When is this going to stop? When is the baby killing going to stop?' And he says, "Can you move on?" And I said, "Can't we dialogue?" And I had this wonderful dialogue.\par \par \uc2 We talked about women. We talked about healing. We talked about babies, and we talked about Thanksgiving. And at the end of that exchange, I shared the love of Christ with him. I told him we were praying for him.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So that guy is a dangerous extremist. You may not agree with him, but he is not a dangerous extremist. He is totally nonviolent. He is a man of faith. But Biden's Justice Department has accused him of the crime of obstructing access to abortion.\par \par \uc2 A guy came up to him and his 12-year-old son and got in the son's face. So, he pushed him back. The man's name was Bruce Love. Love was harassing his boy. That was it.\par \par \uc2 But for pushing the guy back, and by the way, the matter has also been thrown out of Court, but for pushing the guy back, the Biden administration is trying to send that man to prison for 11 years.\par \par \uc2 It's out of control.\par \par \uc2 Judge Jeanine Pirro is the co-host of "The Five." Some people's favorite co-host. And she joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Judge, thanks so much for coming on. So, it's hard to believe this is happening. This is one of the stories you need to read it twice: Are they really trying to send a guy to prison for 11 years for pushing a guy back that gets in his 12-year-old's face?\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CO-HOST, "THE FIVE": Not only gets in his 12-year-old's face, but tells them things that I can't repeat on the air.\par \par \uc2 Look, I mean, when you think about it, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  conducts an early morning raid at the home of an individual. They have 30 \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents with long guns. They have 15 vehicles that surround the house. They're pounding on the door, they've got a SWAT team, and they're pounding on the door, they almost break the door down. So when they opened the door, there are five guns aimed at the head of Mark Houck.\par \par \uc2 So let's go back for a second and say, "Why do you need a SWAT team to arrest this father? I mean, is he a drug dealer? Is he a violent criminal?" Because SWAT is specifically designed for specialized training and tactics for those individuals who are a danger or a threat to public safety.\par \par \uc2 The absurdity of using SWAT in doing all this is simply evidence of what the Biden administration is intending to do to intimidate people on the right. So, what they end up doing is with married, father of seven children all being homeschooled. He is someone who goes and prays on the sidewalk with his son, which is a constitutionally protected right. And he is charged with a Federal offense.\par \par \uc2 This is an example of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the DOJ weaponizing the Department of Justice. We saw it between the leak of the Supreme Court decision and the final release, and in the end, what we've got is a government that is a police state.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Those \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents -- never attack law enforcement -- they should be ashamed and they should resign in protest. It's shocking that they haven't and I appreciate you're describing that horrifying story to us tonight. Judge Jeanine Pirro, thank you.\par \par \uc2 We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: \uc2 George Soros\uc2  has spent millions getting Das who side with criminals elected. What's the effect? Well, this is from Philadelphia, which is in our country. It's a mob storming a Wawa and enjoying it.\par \par \uc2 Just to make it even more dystopian, a woman walked up to the staff mid- robbery and asked them, "Are you going to make my sandwich?"\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I'm walking out here, bro.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Are y'all making the sandwiches?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It's going to be a little while.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: That's the country they are creating. Want more of it? Vote for them in November.\par \par \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  right now.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document TCARL00020220927ei9q00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Laura Responds To Gov \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 ; Voters Around The World Are Rejecting The Elite; A First The Regime Media Doesn't Like; Populist revolution Built On God, Family & Country; Most Don't Want An Uncontrolled Flood Of Migrants; EU Voters Are Rejecting Open Borders; A Second Populist Wave Has Formed; Do You Imagine They're Still Happy?; Being A Lefty Means Never Having To Apologize; The Media Can't Spin Away This Populist Moment; Voters Around The World Are Rejecting The Elite; Populist Revolution Sweeping The Globe; Biden Shrugs Off Abysmal Economy; Wife Of \uc2 FBI\uc2  Whistleblower Has \uc2 Facebook\uc2  Account Suspended For Violating Community Standards; Singer Elton John Holds Concert At White House; New Orleans Police Department Turning To Civilians For Detective Work; \uc2 FBI\uc2  Arrests Man For Violating Freedom Of Access To Abortion Clinic; Democrat Congresswoman \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2  Criticizes GOP Congressman Bob Good Over Transgender Policies\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham \par \uc2 7,325 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Thank you for making this show possible. We hope you'll set your DVR, so you never ever miss an episode of "HANNITY". And in the meantime, you could let not your heart be troubled, because Laura Ingraham, and THE INGRAHAM ANGLE is next, and Laura's got a killer show tonight. Hi, happy Monday.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: OK, I've missed you for the last few days, you've been you know, Mar-a-Lago, I know you were you were in that crawl space where some of the documents where I saw that video, what was I supposed to say that?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How did you know, I was in the crawl space with the documents. I'm in trouble now.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I apologize. It was good, they had you there to crack the safe finally, they finally got that safe.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, I did hear a rumor has it, source has it, there was nothing in the safe, I wondered if they buy a new one.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I was going to make a joke, but someone would have gotten mad at me for that, you know, famous, open safe. I'm not going to make the joke.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We all know what you're talking about. You allow Geraldo, he's got a great sense of humor. One of the most lovable guys in the world, even though he's wrong sometimes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He can take a joke. He does. And he doesn't he like never age as, he looks the same as he looked 25 years ago. So that's why like him. Hannity, awesome show. I'll try to pick it up.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wait, quickly. I was on his daytime program once years ago.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You were?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes, we didn't have a fistfight or anything.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, my gosh, I thought that you needed at least a chair over your head at that point. That would have been good.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Not sense, into me. Bye, bye. Have a good show.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'll pick it up where you left off. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is THE INGRAHAM ANGLE from Washington tonight. Thanks so much for being with us. Gruesome, Newsom comes after Fox primetime hosts, including yours truly, I will respond. So stay tuned for that. But first, 'Wave Elections' that's the focus of tonight's 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Now, it's not just the arrival of crisp fall weather. There's other big change in the air as well. And it could tell us a lot about how things will play out here in the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: In Italy, exit polls show Europe's hard right to score another stunning success at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 DAVID IGNATIUS, AMERICAN JOURNALIST: Who could think that in Sweden, a party with right wing Neo-fascist roots would now be dominant and in parliament in France that the right wing parties would make such a strong showing under \uc2 Marine Le Pen\uc2 Marine Le Pen.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It turns out that regular working people are growing increasingly fed up with establishment politicians, not just here but abroad as well. So Italy's new Prime Minister, \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  is a first, as she's the first woman ever to be elected Prime Minister there.\par \par \uc2 Now you think about it our press is usually over the moon when the first is the liberal woman or a minority or gay, but not in this case.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Italy has elected its first female Prime Minister. Notice though, she is set to lead the most far right government in that country since Mussolini.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: For the first time since World War II, and the fall of \uc2 Benito Mussolini\uc2 , Italy will have a far right government.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Party with roots in Neo-fascism.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The fiery 45-year old is comfortable with some of the hallmarks of Italian fascism, like this motto. God, fatherland and family.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now three things the media despise, God, father's and the nuclear family. I mean, this is just ridiculous. If any group today comes close to Mussolini and his brutal, infamous use of big business and big government together, it's the modern left no nice try kids. Of course, the reason this first and Italy does not count is because she doesn't play their globalist game, she refuses to. She hasn't been bought off, instead, she calls out the failures of the majority parties, and refuses to submit to their woke crusade against national identity and national culture. This was Mussolini back in 2019.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GIORGIA MELONI, MEMBER OF ITALIAN CHAMBER OF DEPUTIES: (Interpreted) Why is the family an enemy? Why is the family so frightening? Because it defines us, because it defines our identity, and so they attack national identity. They attack religious identity. They attack gender identity. They attack family identity.\par \par \uc2 I can't define myself as Italian Christian woman, Mother, I must be citizen X, gender X parent one, parent two, I must be a number. Because when I am only a number, when I no longer have an identity or roots, then I will be the perfect slave at the mercy of financial speculators, the perfect consumer.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, I suggest that you watch her entire speech. It is fantastic. I'm going to post it tonight on lauraingraham.com.\par \par \uc2 Now, the fact is Europe is facing a largely self-inflicted energy crisis this winter, it's going to be horrific, although it's easier just to blame Putin, of course. And Europe has struggled with a stampede of migrants from the Middle East and North Africa. And remember this was forced on them by the EU years ago, especially in Sweden. The burden on social services, schools and law enforcement there has been nightmarish. Now crimes are unlike anything the Police have reported before in Sweden, including bombings have become commonplace.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Is humiliation crimes they have increased the last years. We also call it domination violence where a young person can be urinated at gunpoint, tortured for hours, just because he's so sweet. And there is such resentment among some people.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now this has overwhelmed the ones very placid country. So how can anyone blame the Swedish people for finally voting to try to stop this madness? To not do so would be insane? Something of a national death wish. And as the passage of Brexit was a bellwether in 2016 for Trump, could the recent populist victories across Europe predict similar GOP midterm successes? Well, the grim faces on the faux intellectual class seems to indicate, yes.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The victory of a party that has its roots in the Italian fascism, plain and simple is concerning to everybody. It accompanies, as you said, this move in Europe, there is this populist rage that's sweeping across Europe punches it swept across America in the in 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: There's no curiosity, no effort whatsoever at real reporting here. So those people who are serenely tucked away in their safe enclaves of their own, they simply dismiss these developments out of hand. Their analysis whiffs of a cursory Wikipedia search. It's lazy. The same guy that dynamic is playing out there well, populist candidates and the America first policies that worked under Trump were and are roundly ridiculed and resisted, without really any substantive argument by those same people.\par \par \uc2 It there's literally almost nothing when you look at it, nothing the bipartisan establishment, and especially now the Democrats, nothing they've touched that they haven't screwed up. The energy sector now we're all facing the skyrocketing energy prices just in time for the great freeze here in the United States and in Europe, of course, foreign affairs. They threw Russia into the arms of China with their idiotic handling of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 And then, of course, the climate change obsession, trillions borrowed, trillions printed, and eventually will be spent on Green Marxist policies that will just rob us of our freedom and our prosperity. Yes, we're all watching the financial markets down, down, down. All of this is dragging us into a global recession.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: You know, the past few years have strained and tested our transatlantic relationship. But the United States is determined, determined to reengage with Europe, to consult with you, to earn back our position of trust and leadership.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, yes, the European elites, they loathe Trump as America first policies. And they were thrilled to hear those kinds of words from Biden when he won. But how are things feeling now boys and girls? But being a radical globalist means never having to say you're sorry, or frankly, never having to change your mind about anything. Not for foreign policy disasters like the Afghanistan pullout, or on domestic policy with the COVID school closures.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We still feel comfortable with the way that school districts even you know, in your home state handled the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 PATTY MURRAY\uc2  (D-WA): I think we were under unprecedented times at that point where people really were struggling to figure out what was the best thing to do to make sure that their kids, their families, their children were safe. Remember, people were dying.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I didn't even recognize \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , she is going to be defeated by Tiffany Smiley by the way, in Washington State. So look, listening to \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , she can't offend her paymaster, the teachers unions, even when the teachers unions cruelly sacrifice our children's learning for their own convenience and their own power.\par \par \uc2 So there's only so long even the bluest of blue States like Washington State, Oregon, even New England, where law abiding Americans are going to tolerate ghoulish scenes like this.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Look, when you aren't safe, you aren't free. But again the party in power doesn't believe it bears any r