hat will win. And right now, the Republicans are doing well.\par \par \uc2 You saw the ABC/Washington Post poll that set all the issues that Republicans care about are the number one issues. You have inflation, you have education, you have the economy, you have crime. Those are the top four issues that people are worried about. Immigration is somewhere down there. That's an important issue to Republicans.\par \par \uc2 The things that are the issues for Democrats, they hate Trump. So, January 6th, they love the environment and abortion. They want everyone to be able to have an abortion. Those are their top three issues, but those are not America's issues. When you look at Thanksgiving, we're going to the grocery store. We used to spend, what, a $1.15 for a pound --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: -- for a pound of turkey, now it's $5. Families can't afford to pay a $100 for a Turkey, and a lot of people have 14, 15 people over at their house for Thanksgiving. Things are changing. We are trying to make choices. People have to make choices what they're going to buy at the grocery store. You're not going to buy the most expensive \uc2 Apple\uc2 , you're going to buy the cheaper one, the one in the bag that comes with five or six apples.\par \par \uc2 We're trying to heat our home. They're not as good, but you know, we're trying to heat our homes. You have to choose that. I mean, that's a necessity, especially if you have kids. But inflation is going up, paychecks are staying stagnant and people just can't afford it. That is the main issue. That's why Republicans are going to do well.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: So, I think the message I got from you is that the real winners here are the turkeys. Right?\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: That's true. Way long.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: Big turkey is claiming help.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes, yes, yes. Do you know, but there's a good point, Judge, that Psaki, Psaki, Jen, i