uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  just admitted her boss has a terrible record to run on and told elected Democrats to run away from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They've had two years with full total control and their midterm messages Republicans are extremists, which is a hoax. That's pretty crazy. I mean, they can't run on the infrastructure bill. They didn't build anything. But what else are they going to run on? Are they going to run on COVID relief? Everybody got COVID. Everybody got COVID.\par \par \uc2 What are you going to run on? COVID relief. And it actually triggered inflation. Are you going to run on the Inflation? Reduction Act? That didn't reduce inflation at all. Are you going to run on the border? Border crossing are up. You going to run crime? Crime is up.\par \par \uc2 Are you're going to run on foreign policy? Disgrace this in Afghanistan, and there's a land war in Europe. You can't run on that. What are you going to run? The economy? Stock markets down under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Wages are down under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . We're losing money.\par \par \uc2 And then the media comes out and you're spinning polls like crazy. He's got momentum. The Democrats are, you know, got the Republicans right where they want him. Joe is just lying. He's falling down. He's corrupt, and he's losing us money.\par \par \uc2 So, you're -- you're looking at a Biden presidency that's a total fraud. Eighty-one million votes. He can't even do a rally and the pool camera doesn't pull out because no one showed up.\par \par \uc2 And the Biden rally is free. I told you guys the other day, the whole motorcade crossed by deep blue Manhattan. No one clapped. It was like the prime minister of Yugoslavia.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: To be fair, they were getting mugged.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: They were getting mugged.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Their hands were in the air and they're say, please don't shoot me.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, yes. Someone is out of bandana around their mouth and they had a -- they're sticking them up. Same thing with Kamala. They gave us this great woman, first female vice president, you know, woman of color. She's a laughing stock.\par \par \uc2 You look at \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , she goes out in this deep blue city, goes up in front of a bunch of millennials. They're there for climate change and she gets booed. Democrats' midterm message should be, I'm sorry, I'm just here for the insider trading. It's true. That's the truth.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: What if the Republican message? We're not them?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I would just say --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I'm also here for the --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: -- you're losing.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: -- insider trading.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You're losing money. Crime is up, gas prices are up, inflation is up.\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: Border.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And your money is down. That's what I would say.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I haven't got no plans so you want to restrict women's rights.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I would say you're poor, and you're not safe.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: All right.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: We're not safe.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: There you go. And that's what we're going to talk about next. America's crime crisis emerging as a crucial issue for the midterms and voters know which party can handle it. Yes.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It's you.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: American voters know exactly who to trust when it comes to crime. It's not even a close contest. Republicans smoke Democrats with a monster 22-point advantage among registered voters when it comes to who would do a better job handling the surge in violence. And 67 percent of voters rank crime as one of the top issues this midterm election.\par \par \uc2 But it's no wonder voters or worried. A shocking video out of Philadelphia this past weekend shows dozens of teens just storming a local Wawa and completely ransacking 