ow, they're all out there. We're on the side of the criminal. We're going to give bail to the criminals and we're paying the price. It's about time we've got them out of office.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Have you ever been to a Wawa?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes.\par \par \uc2 You know, it's a religious institution in Philadelphia. A lot of people are thinking we should give these teens the electric chair because of what they did to the soft pretzels and all of the goodies in that Wawa.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: A lot people are saying.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Do you understand the feeling of the people of Philadelphia when something like this happens?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Not about the electric chair and the pretzels. But I spent a lot of time in Wawa. I went to college on the main line, so I spent a lot of time in Philly and the surrounding area.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: The main line?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: What?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Did to hang out in, what is it called? Manayunk?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I have been to Manayunk. Yes. I understand that people are upset about this. I grew up here in the city.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: And I find it devastating what's going on. I've talked not feeling safe to bring my daughter on the subway with me, which is a big difference. My mom had me in the subway every day. There was always --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I thought your mom delivered you in the subway.\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: My mom had me in the subway every day.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I would not have held out on that story for this long because that was the case, but there was always someone around to help with the stroller. Right? It was completely civilized and obviously it's not the case anymore.\par \par \uc2 In terms of the effectiveness of these attacks that featuring in the \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  race, Mandela Barnes, who's running against \uc2 Ron Johnson\uc2  in Wisconsin, was just hit by a bunch of ads talking abo