es and Veterans here in this state, they are hurting to make ends meet. I'm the one that's out there. I'm the one convincing them that change is on the way, that help is on the way, and that you need to invest in change. If you continue to send the same person down there, you're going to get the same result.\par \par \uc2 And you know her percentages are 100 percent with Biden, 96 percent with \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , and look what it's got us, high inflation. We're now a border state, high 200 percent increase in the opioid crisis, mental health crisis, homeless veterans.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Is the Republican establishment in your mind at this point where they'd rather lose with it with a Democrat than win with a more America first Republican. That's what I'm concerned about in some of these races.\par \par \uc2 BOLDUC: I think a lot of people are concerned about that in New Hampshire, but I've been traveling around, you know, going to the you know different GOP events and I've been pushing unity, unity, unity, and Governor Sununu has been doing the same thing. You know, yes, you know, I mean I'm not going to, not going to lie about it, you know \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  came in with a lot of money supporting my opponent, and that obviously has consequences. And when you have to turn around and have 48 days to run a general campaign, that kind of divisiveness in the Republican Party doesn't help the person who comes out as the nominee. And that's me. But we are overcoming that. We are working hard.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's a simple choice for New Hampshire. Your motto is live free or die. That means you've got to have your freedom. It's going away under the Democrats. You're losing your freedom every day. So New Hampshire has a very simple choice. General Bolduc will work towards restoring your freedom and prosperity. Hassan, we're going to go right down the tubes. That's it. That's the race. New Hampshire is going to do the right thing. General Bolduc, I don't mean to steal your thunder, but this is just -- there's no question of how people should vote in this race with our country in this mess. General, thank you.\par \par \uc2 We may have just found Kamala's' replacement. Plus, we're going to talk to folks about the newest Gen Z fashion trends for the office. Raymond Arroyo, has it all. Friday Follies is next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MARIANNE RAFFERTY, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Welcome to FOX News live. I'm Marianne Rafferty in Los Angeles. Tropical depression nine could strengthen into a major hurricane before reaching the U.S. mainland early next week. Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has declared a state of emergency in 24 counties ahead of what is forecasted to become a category three hurricane.\par \par \uc2 And Canada also bracing for hurricane Fiona, a powerful storm that's already caused widespread damage in Puerto Rico, the Dominican Republic, and Turks and Caicos.\par \par \uc2 And thousands of military aged men are joining an exodus from Russia on the second full day of a partial military mobilization. They filled planes and caused traffic jams at land borders to avoid being rounded up to fight in Ukraine. A six-mile traffic jam formed on a road in southern Russia leading to the land border with Georgia, and 6,400 Russians crossed into Finland.\par \par \uc2 I'm Marianne Rafferty. Now back to THE INGRAHAM ANGLE.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's Friday, and that means it's time for Friday Follies. And for that we turn to FOX News contributor Raymond Arroyo. All right, Ray, we played a little bit of President Biden speaking to the teachers' union. Who else is he going speak to at this point? But there was so much that we did not see.\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: You weren't alone, apparently, Laura. I'm going to show you some in the media and their reaction first. And then we'll show you the speech itself. See if this squares for you.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: He sounded like a candidate in a way I haven't heard him. He even was wandering with the mic. He could've stood at the podium.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: There's a lot more Republicans out there taking credit for the new bridges and those - collapsing, than actually voted for it.\par \par \uc2 You've got to say hi to me.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: We go back a long way. She was 12. I was 30. But at any rate.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: He sounds like a candidate for psychological and cognitive analysis, Laura. Come on. If any other candidate, any other politician dropped lines, dropped sense -- made no sense or issued these very bizarre references to a 12-year-old and you're 30, they would be ridden out of town or front page news. It's not the same for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Happy birthday dear la-la. Remember, he couldn't sing that.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'm sorry. I keep thinking of that. He doesn't remember the name. The happy birthday song. All right, Ray, the \uc2 U.N\uc2 . was a huge story this week as well.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yes, not only because it give the president another place to get lost in, Laura, but it marked the emergence of a new possible replacement for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . I know people wonder about Biden's ability to run again, but given Harris' proclivity for word salads, an understudy may have emerged. This is National Youth Poet Laureate Amanda Gorman at the \uc2 U.N\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 AMANDA GORMAN, NATIONAL YOUTH POET LAUREATE: The depths of death, despair, and disparity, atrocities across cities, towns, and countries, lives lost, climactic costs. We're strangers to one another's perils and pain, unaware that the welfare of the public and the planet share a name -- equality. The oldest ode we owe each other. We chime it for the