or of Braddock, Pennsylvania, Fetterman failed to pay more than $18,000 in property taxes between 2006 to 2019. That's money that would have gone to funding his local school district, which is one of the poorest and lowest performing in the state. The Woodland Hills school district reportedly placed nearly three dozen tax liens against Fetterman during that 13-year stretch and he was sued twice.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman's opponent, Dr. Mehmet Oz, is now attacking Fetterman for being hypocritical.\par \par \uc2 MEHMET OZ (R), PENNSYLVANIA SENATE CANDIDATE: \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  has advocated for increased taxes in his past positions. He was a strong supporter of President Biden's recent law that increases taxes for the middle class as well and he's got 67 liens against him for not actually paying his own.\par \par \uc2 LLENAS: The Washington Free Beacon reports overall 65 tax liens totaling more than $30,000 were placed on properties owned by Fetterman and his community nonprofit Braddock Redux, which bought properties. In his statement to Fox News today, the Fetterman campaign said John is proud of his work helping to revive Braddock. All of these properties were purchased by John and his nonprofit to provide homes for people in need or create opportunity for the people of Braddock. He eventually paid off the liens. But in some cases it took more than six years, Martha, and Fetterman went on to attack Dr. Oz, by the way, in that statement for benefiting from tax breaks he received for renovations on his multimillion dollar properties in Florida and Pennsylvania. Oz says, look, he abides by the tax rules. Martha.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes, all right. The hate of campaign season to be sure. Bryan, thank you very much, Bryan Llenas.\par \par \uc2 So a preview of my new podcast with royal expert Neil Sean, his final thoughts on the funeral of Queen Elizabeth and the scoop today on \uc2 Meghan Markle\uc2  when we come back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par 