s Senator Ted Cruz. He's been all over this issue.\par \par \uc2 Senator, you have been warning the country and you've been showing the country, you're the one that got us the video of Biden's kids in cages. They wouldn't let the media inside those cages.\par \par \uc2 How rich is this? Within 20 -- less than 24 hours, 50 migrants in beautiful Martha's Vineyard are kicked out of the island of millionaires and billionaires and liberals, and meanwhile, already your state of Texas this year at, what, 1.1 million illegal immigrants have crossed into Texas?\par \par \uc2 SEN. TED CRUZ (R-TX): Yeah, I got to say, today has really illustrated what screaming hypocrites the Democrats are the entire corrupt corporate media. They don't believe a word they said. Every word out of their mouth is a complete and utter lie.\par \par \uc2 You know, the Democrats did not think it was a humanitarian crisis when we pulled over 50 bodies and body bags out of a truck in Texas of illegal immigrants who died because the smugglers let them die of heat exposure and yet, suddenly, 50 illegal immigrants show up in Lilly white Martha's Vineyard where rich, liberals and billionaires sip chardonnay and it is -- it is World War III, they lose their stuff all over the place, and it just shows what utter nonsense it was.\par \par \uc2 You know, Sean, I'm reminded as you know, a year ago, I introduce legislation calling for illegal immigrants to be sent to wealthy liberal enclaves like Martha's Vineyard, like Nantucket, like Palo Alto, like Rehoboth Beach, Delaware, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  vacations.\par \par \uc2 And it was fascinating, you know, the response -- the leadership of Martha's Vineyard said they would love it. In fact, I want to read the response because it's too perfect not to revisit.\par \par \uc2 Dukes County commissioner Keith Chatinover said the following, I would love Martha's Vineyard to become a haven for new immigrants in this country but Senator Cruz has no idea what he's talking about regarding a border crisis. That's what he said last year that he would love Martha's Vineyard to become a haven. Now, with just 50, they've lost it.\par \par \uc2 And what did they do, within 24 hours, these leftist hypocrites load them on buses and deported them out of there.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, Senator, this is the rank hypocrisy and you can't even make this up. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been flying illegal immigrants in the dark of night to all of these obscure airports. For example, in New York, they're not landing at LaGuardia. They're not landing at Kennedy. They're not landing at Newark. They're landing in White Plains. They're landing in Long Island, at 2:00, 3:00, 4:00 a.m. in the morning so they -- so they don't get caught doing what they're doing.\par \par \uc2 And all these towns have to pick up food, shelter, health care costs, clothing, education and they're dumping it on pretty much every state in the country. So if there's any law breaking going on, that would be \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's actual policy, isn't it?\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: Yeah. No, that's exactly right. And then to put in perspective, Martha's Vineyard is a town. Its population is about 17,000. The median home price is over a million dollars.\par \par \uc2 Let's compare it to Del Rio. Del Rio is a wonderful town in Texas. It's down on the Rio Grande Valley. It has a population of between 30,000 and 35,000.\par \par \uc2 In one single day at Del Rio, there were 15,000 illegal immigrants, mostly Haitians crossing illegally in one day. As you know, I went down to the bridge and I videoed over 10,000 illegal immigrants under that bridge.\par \par \uc2 Martha's Vineyard lost their mind with and the little town of Del Rio and towns all up and down the Rio Grande Valley are dealing with hundreds, are dealing with thousands. Let me say, Sean, I commend Greg Abbott for sending the immigrants to these blue cities. I commend \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  for doing so, and they need to do more.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow, Martha's Vineyard needs a hundred. The next day, they need 200. The next day, they need a thousand.\par \par \uc2 D.C. says it's a crisis to get six thousand. They need ten thousand. They need a hundred thousand. They need 500,000 because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has allowed 4.2 million people to come in illegally.\par \par \uc2 And I know these rich billionaires say, well, gosh, you people just let them eat cake. Well, how about having the Obamas host these 50 people and their $12 million compound --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wait a minute, they got 30 acres.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: No, no, no. None of them.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They got 30 acres, Senator.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: They could literally set up -- exactly.\par \par \uc2 Maria Shriver said a tweet, complaining about this and saying that Abbott and DeSantis were heartless. And my response was great. The Kennedys are offering to host these 50 illegal immigrants at their compound in Hyannis Port. What utter and complete hypocrisy and it shows that they simply don't care. This is all politics.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, let's talk about the law. You're a lawyer, Senator. You've argued before the Supreme Court successfully. And from a legal standpoint, let's say I went down to the border and I brought a big truck with me and I picked up a bunch of illegal immigrants and I started transporting them across the country.\par \par \uc2 Would I or would I not likely be arrested for human trafficking? And what would it be illegal to do that for me if I did that?\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: For you a citizen, you could easily be arrested, although to be honest, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's justice department wouldn't arrest you. But in an ordinary Justice Department --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I disagree. They arrest me. If I was a liberal, I get away with it.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: True.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. But back to the law, the law is clear.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: It is clear and right now, the biggest trafficker on the face of the planet is Joseph Robinette Biden Jr. He has transported hundreds of thousands, millions of illegal aliens, populating them, now putting many of them in red states. He's happy to put them in red states where it's not the rich people's concerns, it's the little people's concerns.\par \par \uc2 You know, all of the folks on Martha's Vineyard happily voted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Well, they can live with the consequences of the lawless policies that right now the people of McAllen, the people of Laredo, the people of Eagle Pass, the people of Texas are feeling the price for this and Biden still won't change.\par \par \uc2 Instead what does he do, he lies to the American people. He sends \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  out to claim nobody is crossing the border illegally. It's a flat out lie, and all of the docile little sheep in the press room, they bow like sheep and they ignore the fact that she's lying to the American people. The media needs to cover her lies and this outrage needs to stop because, you know what, these blue governors and mayors are right, it is a crisis but it's not just a crisis when it's the millionaires who are inconvenienced.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, it's over three million people, Senator. We have to secure our borders. It's simple. Follow the law, follow the constitution and respect the laws and borders and security of our country. Simple.\par \par \uc2 Senator Ted Cruz, thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 All right. Here with more reaction, we have the Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  and Florida Attorney General \uc2 Ashley Moody\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ken, let's start with you. Get your take on this. To me, between Governor Abbott and Governor DeSantis, the best political jujitsu move ever in history, and look at the impact and look at the rank hypocrisy, Ken.\par \par \uc2 KEN PAXTON\uc2 , TEXAS ATTORNEY GENERAL: No, it's just -- it's amazing. They've done an amazing job. They've had to deal with this crisis over the last two years and I love that they're highlighting the hypocrisy that you and Senator Cruz just talked about.\par \par \uc2 They're dealing with a few hundred, maybe a thousand. You said Martha's Vineyard, 50. We deal with a day and we've been dealing with this for almost two years and as Senator Cruz talked about, Del Rio, a town of 36,000 had 50 percent more people show up at their door and we had to deal with it.\par \par \uc2 There was no complaining by the liberal elite. There was no complaining by \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 . We had to deal with it and we had no help.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, Ashley, I'm looking at Governor DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 There were -- he pointed out there, what, 70 flights to Jacksonville alone of illegal immigrants dropped off in Florida in the dark of night. Now, as the governor pointed out, Florida is not a sanctuary state. Jacksonville is not a sanctuary city, and they don't support law breaking. So he said okay we'll send these illegal immigrants to places that claim to be having sanctuary status.\par \par \uc2 To me, that seemed like the fair thing to do considering he doesn't have the authority to deport them.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY MOODY (R), FLORIDA ATTORNEY GENERAL: Well, keep this in mind the Biden administration has been breaking the law as it relates to federal immigration policy since their first month in office and Republican states like Texas and Florida have been fighting them every inch of the way. We've been telling them, Americans lives are at risk. Those coming over are in harm's way.\par \par \uc2 We've been begging them to pay attention. Just come to the border. Biden hasn't been there. They don't come. They won't witness it. We've even had folks that are transported to Florida by air Biden murder someone.\par \par \uc2 You know, this is a necessary exercise. I know folks are thinking, you know, they deserve this. This is a hypocrisy and it is all true, right? But this is a necessary exercise. At some point, they are in this liberal ignorant bubble they don't know what's going on. They are we have to put it on their doorstep to force them to see what it takes to deal with this record-breaking surge of flooding into our country. You know, at the moment, it's like they're Muppets offering commentary and opining on what everybody should do that's having to deal with us on a daily basis and deal with their reckless dangerous policies.\par \par \uc2 In fact, I think that anybody that passes one of these policies that breaks the law should have to go live in it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, I agree. Ashley, do you believe Governor DeSantis will keep this up? I hope he does and then I'll ask Ken the same question.\par \par \uc2 MOODY: Well, I know that he's asked for the funding to do so and you know in order to start getting some action out of Washington rather than utter lies, we've got to start forcing them to see what we on the front lines law enforcement are dealing with.\par \par \uc2 That's the only way that they're going to start taking action and if the American people see it, maybe they'll start holding this president accountable.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And, Ken, will Governor Abbott continue? I believe he should continue as well.\par \par \uc2 PAXTON: Yeah, this was his idea. It was genius because it highlights the hypocrisy that we're talking about and we're talking about again a few thousand a drop in the bucket compared to what we've dealt with. There's no doubt our governor is going to continue to send people to these liberal sanctuary cities.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Ashley, Ken, thank you both. I hope they continue.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  took a major shot at \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  today. It was a shot right across the bow, after the California governor suggested that he'd be brought up on kidnapping charges and the DOJ investigate Governor Abbott and Governor DeSantis. We've got the tape and we'll tell you all about Gavin's hypocrisy, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Right now, far left California Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  is more desperate than ever to fire up his left-wing base, bizarrely suggesting that Governors \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Governor Greg Abbott, that they are guilty of kidnapping for sending migrants to liberal cities, like Martha's Vineyard.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, he's now calling for a full investigation by the DOJ. Earlier today, as we pointed out earlier, Governor DeSantis fired back in a big way. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. RON DESANTIS (R), FLORIDA: The governor of California sent a letter to the Department of Justice saying you need to prosecute Texas and Florida governors. And all I can say is I think his hair gel is interfering with his brain function.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Every time Newsom battles DeSantis, he loses.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, Newsom's far left lunacy doesn't stop there, as the governor is now continuing to take aim at red states, now renting out billboards in Texas and other red states touting access to abortion in California. So, what, California is now going to be the sanctuary state for late term abortion, what some might call infanticide, people that want abortion up to the moment of birth?\par \par \uc2 But, of course, it is Newsom himself who has been embroiled a never-ending controversy. During the height of the pandemic, remember, it was him dining at the ritzy French laundry restaurant or telling everybody else they got to stay at home, notice he doesn't have a mask on either. His kids were going to in-person private school while private school children suffered under remote learning policies of his.\par \par \uc2 Homelessness, crime has worsened under his watch and most recently, California's failing energy policy was struggling to even keep the lights on. Please don't charge your electric vehicle. That's how bad it got.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, co-host of the hit show "The Five", Judge Jeanine Pirro, along with FOX News contributor and the guy that should have his own media show, Joe Concha.\par \par \uc2 Judge, let's start from a legal standpoint. As a judge, okay, is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  enforcing the laws of the land? And when he puts these illegal immigrants on these flights and drops down in these obscure airports at 2:00, 3:00, 4:00 a.m. in the morning, is he transporting illegal immigrants? Is that human trafficking?\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, "THE FIVE" CO-HOST: Well, you know, there is a -- there is certainly a train of thought where people would say that that's the case. But the truth is that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  by allowing illegals to come into this country is violating the federal statutes that say they have to wait in line like everyone else. So from the get-go, we've got a problem.\par \par \uc2 And the attack on Governor DeSantis is absurd. It is what the left does. They want to weaponize the Department of Justice, the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . We've seen them do it over and over again.\par \par \uc2 Look, these people are being processed. They're -- they go through the NGOs and then they have an opportunity to be flown around the nation. Now, if \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is guilty of kidnapping, then so is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has already done something like 900 flights in the last year, sending these people all over the country. I don't know if they've signed waivers to come into my county Westchester in the -- in the dead of night. I don't know if anyone's been notified.\par \par \uc2 But all of a sudden, it's illegal if a Republican does it, and this is the problem in this country. The Democrats are emboldened. Anything they think they do, they get the power of the -- of the law enforcement, and they enforce the law according to what their ideology is. And that's a bad thing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, Joe from a media standpoint, the judge rightly points out, you know, this has been going on with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  transporting illegal immigrants and giving them preferential treatment for 19 months. Now, all of a sudden, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  sends 50 people, 50, to Martha's Vineyard. That's -- they say they're inclusive, they say they welcome immigrants. They're a sanctuary island.\par \par \uc2 But yet they flip out, the media flips out with them, and I'm like -- have you just not been paying attention to what \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's been doing all over the country?\par \par \uc2 JOE CONCHA, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yeah, Sean, they're taking the sanctuary out of sanctuary city or sanctuary vineyard in this case.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, they kicked them out.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: In this outrage that we're seeing. Yeah, exactly, they're over in Cape Cod over the military base.\par \par \uc2 But this outrage that we're seeing from Democrats and their allies in the media, it's so patently phony. I mean, if \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , or MSNBC, CNN, "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " really cared about the health and well-being of these migrants crossing into this country illegally, then why don't we hear about the 750 people who have died this year crossing the U.S. southern border. That's more than two per day according to the DHS, the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And these people are coming in such huge numbers because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  invited them here as a candidate. And now, Governor Newsom is giving them free health care? I mean, who wouldn't want to come here?\par \par \uc2 And listen, this year alone, there's been 19,000 search and rescue missions carried out by border officials who are risking their lives?\par \par \uc2 And while they're doing that, fentanyl is coming into this country from China, through Mexico, at an alarming rate, killing an average of 300 Americans per day. But we don't hear much talk about that now, do we?\par \par \uc2 And it's obvious that Governor DeSantis, Governor Abbott, they're playing chess here while his opponents are playing checkers, by busing migrants to New York, Washington, D.C., Chicago, you know, Martha's Vineyard, they succeeded, yeah, in putting this issue front and center in the news cycle and all the hypocrisy from the left around it because when the Biden administration to Jeanine's point was trafficking illegal migrants to places like Westchester or Jacksonville, Florida, you didn't hear one peep about kidnapping from anyone on the left and certainly by nobody in the media.\par \par \uc2 So this issue is going to have a major impact during the midterm, Sean. That I can guarantee you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you -- I want to ask you, Judge, really specifically about the what is \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  now with these billboards, is he making California a late term abortion sanctuary state where you can have an abortion up to what an hour before you give birth?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh, no. I mean, you can. The mother can give birth and then decide make the make the baby comfortable and decide like the emperor with an up and down, north and like Virginia, they can decide, well, you know, I don't think I want to have this baby.\par \par \uc2 Look, if he wants to be that state, let him be that state. You're right. Every time \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  goes after \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , he loses. If he wants to be the far left progressive state where crime is out of control, where they taught the rest of the country about smash and grab, carjackings and everything else, let him do it. The truth is Americans do not want what \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  wants.\par \par \uc2 And the -- I got to say one more thing. I'm tired of the Democrats calling the Republicans un-American, saying that they're involved in you know in what is like human trafficking. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 : sending poor Venezuelans to Martha's Vineyard.\par \par \uc2 Hillary, you go to Martha's Vineyards all the time. Why is sending poor Venezuela is there a problem? You like it. Why can't they go there?\par \par \uc2 And you know what? I'm going to say what nobody else is saying, when Mayor \uc2 Lori Lightfoot\uc2  says it's racist for Abbott to send these people to Chicago, maybe if it's racism that is judge at the core of this.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Judge, she kicked them out. She put them on buses. She kidnapped them and kicked them out, to use their own language, racist and xenophobic.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Right and she's redistricting, that's what they're doing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You really can't make all this up. I mean, it is hypocrisy, rank hypocrisy. It's pretty unbelievable.\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you both. Judge, good to see you. Joe, thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right. Straight ahead tonight, Dr. Oz rising big time in the polls as questions about \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 's health continue. You're not going to believe the latest on his campaign poll. Dr. Oz will react as we continue this Friday night.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And breaking news tonight out of Pennsylvania where Dr. Mehmet Oz is on the rise in the race for the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 . A new poll from Trafalgar, that's Robert Cahaly, finds that Dr. Oz is now closing the gap dramatically. He's now surging. He is now down by under two points, 1.7 points, against struggling \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , the lieutenant governor that's nowhere to be found. That has only campaigned less than an hour the entire campaign and has never answered a press -- question from the press.\par \par \uc2 This comes as he has now agreed, Fetterman has, to one debate but it's in late October and, by the way, he says he will need the assistance of closed captioning and that raises a whole host of other questions about Fetterman's fitness for office.\par \par \uc2 Now, when you debate somebody this late in the race -- well, that's not fair to the people of Pennsylvania because early voting starts in Pennsylvania on Monday. He's talking about October 25th. So, Fetterman clearly is trying to run out the clock amid his endless struggles on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 And amid more and more scrutiny of his far left extreme positions, let's see, like wanting to release a third of Pennsylvania prisoners from jail, wanting to eliminate all fracking, are you kidding me? That's an $81 billion industry in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 He wants abortion on demand with no restrictions at all whatsoever. He is a new green deal socialist. He wants to destroy Pennsylvania's energy sector completely. He wants to legalize or decriminalize even hard drugs like heroin. He wants these legalized drug dens or safe shooting zones he calls them.\par \par \uc2 And we're also learning last year that he cast a lone vote to free a man convicted of murdering a woman with scissors. Why did he do that? Nobody's asked the question, nobody's asked any question.\par \par \uc2 Add to that, Fetterman's speaking struggles following his stroke back in May. Now, Fetterman was asked about his stumbles in one softball pre-taped interview as I understand it on MSDNC. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ALEX WAGNER, MSDNC HOST: A lot has been made of your health especially by Republicans. There are viral videos, mash ups of your, I think, cognitive or vocal errors, things that they think suggest cognitive decline. What do you say to Pennsylvania voters who see some of this stuff on the Internet, who hear the ads from Dr. Oz's camp and are worried about your fitness for office? I mean, what do you say to skeptics who think I don't know about this guy? Is it is he operating at a hundred percent?\par \par \uc2 JOHN FETTERMAN\uc2  (D-PA), U.S. SENATE CNADIDATE: All of -- all of my doctors on the team believes that I'm absolutely fit to serve. I just can confront -- I would just -- took a test -- just I think it was yesterday that that confirmed that I'm absolutely fully functioning and in the range as well too.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How about an independent doctor make that observation and make that conclusion? His campaign now is saying he passed a cognitive test but for whatever reason they won't release any results. MSDNC doesn't count as any vetting at all. They are key questions that he needs to answer, like for example, why did he pull a gun out on an innocent African-American jogger back in 2013, even he admitted he probably broke the law? Why does he want to legalize the use of hard drugs like heroin and others? Why does he have such a pro-criminal agenda to release all these even violent criminals?\par \par \uc2 You know, when are they going to vet his phony, spoiled socialist trust fund brat status? The guy's never had a job. He tries to look tough in his hoodie with his tattoos. He's never had a real job. He's been living off his parents for decades until he's 50. All while he lies and pretends that he's some sort of self-made man of the people. Well, we now found out that he owns eight properties in the town where he was mayor but barely showed up for city council meetings in Braddock.\par \par \uc2 So, how did the trust fund brat who never had a job in a hoodie pay for all of this? And why didn't he disclose it as the law requires?\par \par \uc2 Now, sadly, Fetterman isn't the only Democrat that doesn't want to debate. Same thing with New York Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , she doesn't want to debate \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , and we need debates now, not a week before the election after maybe what 50, 60 percent of the voters votes have already been cast.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, Pennsylvania Senate candidate Dr. Mehmet Oz.\par \par \uc2 I don't know your reaction. I'll tell you my reaction. To debate you and wait until -0- Monday starts voting in Pennsylvania. So, what, we may have 50 percent o