ll the American people the truth, I mean, when the President United States says everything is OK, and has James Taylor out there, you know, singing "Fire and Rain."\par \par \uc2 I mean, rather than a ballot about suicide and addiction, and grief, maybe he should have done one of his other numbers, one of my favorites. It's only a "Paper Moon." It's a Barnum and Bailey world, just as phony as it can be. But it would be not, it would not be make believe if you believed in me. That's what they're trying to sell is a phony view of the world as it is. And it's going to disconnect him from the voters and they'll suffer accordingly at the polls.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Karl, the only thing that would have made that better is if you actually sing it for us. But I'm very impressed with your lyrics recall.\par \par \uc2 ROVE: It's a Barnum and Bailey World, just as phony as it can be. No, you don't want to hear me say Martha, you do not want to hear me sing.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: OK.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: I can listen to this all day.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Maybe that, maybe that's true. Joe, you know, talk to us a little bit about what you think voters are thinking as we head into the eight weeks before the midterm here and they're watching this at the White House and they're seeing these prices go up and they're being told that they should just, you know, buy an electric car and everything will get better. But you do hear a lot of people asking, you know, what is it that Republicans would offer and we're seeing these races tighten up?\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Precisely. We talk about bumper stickers on the show last week. It has to be such a clear and concise message. I mean, I get the Obama Biden campaign in 2012 a lot of credit. Very simple slogan to absorb. (INAUDIBLE) is alive and Bin Laden is dead, OK? So, you just need, basically, two sentences, something more along the lines of and I don't have it off the top of my head. But you know, are you better off than you 