ll. I am very proud of myself.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, he was talking and I didn't think he bragged enough because that was a big, big time catch. Tonight, "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME," we have Senator Lindsey Graham Dan Bongino, also Kat Timpf, but before Greg, and Mike Pompeo. So, check us out at 7:00. Jessica?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Awesome. So, disabled athletes are getting another opportunity to compete in sports with wheelchair lacrosse. So, wheelchair lacrosse was designed in Colorado and adapted from lacrosse by being played on a roller hockey rink or hard surface lacrosse rink. The sport involves wheelchairs similar to those used in wheelchair basketball.\par \par \uc2 And due to its growing popularity, each team is allowed three able-bodied players who was also -- who also must use them, the wheelchairs. National attraction is growing with Wheelchair Lacrosse USA holding the national championships annually. So --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: That's nice.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes. So, what you do is you get the best lacrosse players in the world. You tell them they have to be in wheelchairs, and they'll learn enough so they could just totally dominate all the people that are really on wheelchairs.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Are you saying --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I'm coaching. I'm coaching it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No, no.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You don't think so? You think --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Let it go. Don't touch it anymore.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: All right. I'm allowed to have opinions.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK, it's my turn. It's my turn. OK, so, everyone deserves a little rest and relaxation. So, a woman in Philadelphia heard a little rustling on the back porch. And she turns out that there's a raccoon hanging out in her hammock outside her Philadelphia home. And she said the raccoon stayed the night after spending a little time getting comfortable there.\par \par \uc2 But the woman who owns the hammock is no stranger to animals. It turns out she's a squid biologist, Greg. She drives a car called the squid mobile. Joke on that one.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Can I add something on my "ONE MORE THING?"\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, please.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Well, I didn't read -- I didn't read far enough. OK, so that mom, Ricki, she was in a huge rush. She usually makes peanut butter and jelly but she didn't have peanut butter. So, she just put butter and jelly on the sandwich for little --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: (INAUDIBLE).\par \par \uc2 PERINO: It's Abe and his mom Ricki. So that's what happened. It's a butter and Jelly sandwich.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: That is the greatest fact check ever.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I agree. Terrible sandwich.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes. She should have done cream cheese and jelly.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Be better, mom. That's it for us. "SPECIAL REPORT" is up next with Bret Baier.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXFIV0020220915ei9e00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Interview with Sen. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  (R-FL)\b0\par\par\uc2 John Roberts, Sandra Smith \par \uc2 1,666 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Live Event\par \uc2 FXLV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SANDRA SMITH, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Florida Republican Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  joining us now. He's the chairman of the National Republican Senatorial Committee.\par \par \uc2 Thank you very much, sir, for joining us.\par \par \uc2 Your tweet caught our attention, because you said what many were thinking: "Democrats celebrating our economy show they live in a total fantasyland. Americans' grocery bills just increased, again, and inflation is still sky- high at 8.3 percent."\par \par \uc2 It was actually hard to believe at one point. Neil Cavuto coming in with an epic takedown at 4:00, looking at the fact that there was a celebration happening while Americans are watching their retirement funds go down, the stock market plunging, and inflation running sky-high.\par \par \uc2 What was there to celebrate?\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 RICK SCOTT\uc2  (R-FL): You know, they're living in fantasyland.\par \par \uc2 So let's think about it. A family in Florida is going to spend about 9,000 more dollars today just for cost of living per year in increase over when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  got elected. That's number one.\par \par \uc2 Number two, we have got businesses that can't afford their food, their materials, and be able to pass that on. So they're losing jobs.\par \par \uc2 Here's an example of what's happening. We got more people going to food banks than ever before in Florida. We have got people delaying their retirement, come out of retirement, and taking multiple jobs.\par \par \uc2 By the way, in August, we didn't generate new full-time jobs. We lost 242,000 jobs. What we added was part-time jobs. The White House forgot to tell you about that part.\par \par \uc2 So, if you look at this economy, and the retirement plans are going down. If you're on -- if you're -- if you're on fixed income, you're -- what you have -- what you saved is worth less.\par \par \uc2 JOHN ROBERTS, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Yes.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: I mean, you just name it, nothing's good.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: So, clearly, Senator, the numbers would not be in favor of the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 But can between now and November 8 Republicans effectively leverage the economy to override the Democratic message about the Dobbs decision and democracy that has been pretty darn effective in narrowing the gap between them and the Republicans now and turning what looked like a Republican tsunami into a ripple?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Oh, I think we're going to have a great year. We just got numbers out of Wisconsin. Ron Johnson is up five, 49-44 or 45 over -- 49-44 over Barnes.\par \par \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2  up is up three over Beasley. We got consistently now \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is up three. We have our new candidate in New Hampshire, who I think is going to do a great job. \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2  is in deep trouble. So you -- I can I can see a great win. We're going to get the majority. And I think we have -- we're going to continue to work hard. And I think we're going to do really well in November.\par \par \uc2 Look at all the poll numbers. They are heading our direction.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: I mean, as far as the potential victory for Republicans, that margin has been shrinking, though, Senator. Obviously, you can acknowledge that that has been happening.\par \par \uc2 Are Democrats winning, albeit a lot of bad things happening right now? Are they winning on messaging?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: As we have come out of these primaries, we have invested early.\par \par \uc2 Take Barnes' race in Wisconsin. In the last month, Barnes' positive versus negatives, Barnes was 16 points up on fave/unfave. He's now down two. So what we have done is, we have invested. In every one of our swing states, Biden's numbers, approval is under 40, and all of our Democratic opponents are under 50.\par \par \uc2 Now, we're -- if you look at the -- if you look at the numbers over the last three months, our investments in these -- what our campaigns are doing, what Republicans are doing is paying off because we're continuing to move up. I mean, look at Wisconsin. Everybody says, oh, that's a really hard state to win. Ron Johnson is up 49-44 right now.\par \par \uc2 And even the Democrat poll, the Marquette poll has him up one. So, we look around the country, we are heading in the right direction. I'm excited about our candidates. I'm excited about November.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: All right. So, Senator, you were given a gift yesterday with the inflation number, and it looked like Republicans were eager to jump all over that and pummel the Biden administration with it.\par \par \uc2 And then Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  came out and said this:\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 LINDSEY GRAHAM\uc2  (R-SC): I think we should have a law at the federal level that would say, after 15 weeks, no abortion on demand, except in cases of rape, incest, to save the life of the mother. And that should be where America is at.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: So, after Republicans were saying all across the country that what the Dobbs decision does is, it simply throws the abortion issue back to the states and takes it out of the federal government's hands, \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  comes out and goes, oh, we need a federal law here.\par \par \uc2 And a lot of Republicans and other people have suggested that he scored a goal on his own net with that. Where do you come down on that?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, if you go around the country, what people are focused on is their economy, their kids education, and public safety.\par \par \uc2 With regard to abortion, the Democrats are clearly focused on abortion. Every Republican candidate has taken their position.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: But it's very effective. It's very effective for them, Senator.\par \par \uc2 They have they have outpaced the Democrats in registering women, particularly in the suburbs -- outpaced the Republicans -- sorry -- on registering women, particularly in the suburbs.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Let's go through the polls. That's who -- likely voters. Ron Johnson is winning. \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2  is winning. \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 's winning. Adam Laxalt is tied to up one. We have had -- we're barely down in a variety of states.\par \par \uc2 We're down by one in Colorado. We're three points in Washington, two to four points in Arizona. We are actually heading in the right direction. The Democrats, they don't want to be seen with Biden. They -- he's toxic to the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 So, if we stay on our message, talk about inflation, about the border crisis, about crime -- this is not where the country wants to go. The country says this -- the country is heading in the right direction. The Democrats control the House, the White House, and the Senate.\par \par \uc2 So we are going to win in November. There will be a lot of noise out there about how Republicans can't win. But look at the polls. We keep getting better week after week after week.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: What about in New Hampshire, these closely watched races there, where you have got a pair of MAGA candidates, MAGA Republican candidates, winning their races there, Democrats seemingly getting what they wanted.\par \par \uc2 Obviously, it would be -- they see it would be tougher to go up against some of these moderate Republicans in these races. How do you interpret that?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, Don Bolduc ran -- Bolduc, he ran -- he ran very proper. He won.\par \par \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2  has spent, I think, $9 million. Other Democratic groups have spent tens of millions of dollars. And her approval -- approval is like at 43-44 percent. Biden is underwater. I mean, you can see that we're going to win.\par \par \uc2 So, we have got through the primary. We're going to be all in to make sure we win in New Hampshire. We will win in New Hampshire. \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 , her problem is, they know her up there and they don't like her.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: So, let's look ahead to after November the 8th. If Republicans take back control of the Senate, the question is, who's going to be the majority leader?\par \par \uc2 And the other day, at the National Conservatism Conference, you deferred when asked if you would support \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 . Here's what you said.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: You know, I -- we will see what he wants to do. I mean, if we're going to -- we will have an election. And after the November elections, I'm confident that we're going to get a majority.\par \par \uc2 And so, we will make a decision then.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: So, the two of you have been working together to try to win back the Senate, but do you have concerns about his leadership?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, he will decide if he's going to continue to run. I assume he will.\par \par \uc2 I'm focused on the November Senate races. We got a lot of elections coming up. We got a presidential race coming up. We got a lot of other elections. I will focus on those when I get to them. Right now, my focus is 100 percent get back to Senate.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: That sounds like another deferral, Senator.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, I have said -- I have said I'm focused on the -- I'm focused on the Senate.\par \par \uc2 And I have a good working relationship with \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 . And I'm going to focus on getting the Senate back.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: All right, we appreciate you joining us, sir. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: Thanks, Senator. See you again soon.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FXLV000020220914ei9e00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 John Solomon: \uc2 FBI\uc2  Paid Russian Accused of Lying As An Informant Against \uc2 Donald Trump\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Newt Gingrich, Joe Concha, Pete Hegseth \par \uc2 8,288 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: All right. And, Tucker, and thank you.\par \par \uc2 And welcome to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 My monologue coming up in a mere moment. But first we begin tonight with breaking news from the Washington swamp. Tonight, two major reports from investigative reporter John Solomon first a new bombshell from the Durham probe. According to brand new court filings, we now know that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  paid a Russian man with ties to Moscow's intel agency for three years to be a confidential informant against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And it goes deeper, this individual was the primary source for \uc2 Christopher Steele\uc2 's dirty Russian disinformation dossier that Hillary Clinton paid for and is now on trial for lying to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . In other words, the bureau was so desperate to get Trump that they paid a Russian agent to spew anti-Trump lies for three years. They also knew directly from him in early of 2017 that the dossier was completely false but people like \uc2 Jim Comey\uc2  continue to sign off on the FISA warrants even though they knew without the lying dossier would never have been approved. Where is the rate of Comey's home? Where is equal justice in America? It seems to be dead for the moment.\par \par \uc2 Now, the second explosive report, again, from John Solomon involves January the 6th. One former intel analyst for the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  is now blowing the whistle, telling Solomon that clear and direct warnings about the dire security situation at the Capitol way prior to January would totally completely ignored by those in charge and that would be including ultimately \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here with all these explosive details he's their editor-in-chief at justthenews.com, John Solomon.\par \par \uc2 John, I'll let you start wherever you want. Two big stories tonight.\par \par \uc2 JOHN SOLOMON, EDITOR IN CHIEF, JUSTTHENEWS.COM: Yeah, listen, you hit the Danchenko thing right on the head. Just to think about this, the primary source for the \uc2 Christopher Steele\uc2  dossier which was funded by the Hillary Clinton campaign is a person that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  believes starting in 2008 was tied to Russian intelligence.\par \par \uc2 Why did they believe that? Because they had evidence he was soliciting Obama administration appointees, saying he would pay them if they would leak him classified information. He was working with the Russian intelligence agencies. He leaves the country. He comes back. They find out that he's the primary source for \uc2 Christopher Steele\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  fires \uc2 Christopher Steele\uc2  because he was leaking to the media. They then hire this guy to be a confidential human source. They hire him after they detect in their first interview with him in many years, in January '17, that he lied to them, that he denied being tied to Russian intelligence, they had to say, listen, buddy, we know you're tied to Russian intelligence. He corrects himself then.\par \par \uc2 They then go and put this man on the payroll for three years, trying to dig up dirt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . It's an extraordinary thing. And now, we know that while he was doing all that work for the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , getting paid by American tax dollars, he was lying to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , not once, not twice, five times in the indictment. And \uc2 John Durham\uc2  says he's going to reveal many more lies that Igor Danchenko told the \uc2 FBI\uc2  during this time.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2 's case against for Russia collusion couldn't be any more embarrassing than what we now know.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Hey, John, remember, it was \uc2 Andrew McCabe\uc2  that it said, no, if you don't have the dirty dossier and again, he was the primary source, he told them in early 2017, that means two FISA warrants were signed after and McCabe said without that dossier, there would be no FISA warrant granted.\par \par \uc2 SOLOMON: That's why the Justice Department withdrew two of those FISA warrants. There is no basis for them to stand under the law and now we know most of the crown financial informant information the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was getting about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was completely manufactured, including that famous pee tape, you know, the old the whole story about the Moscow hotel.\par \par \uc2 John Durham\uc2  reveals in tonight's filing, he's going to reveal that the Moscow and hotel employees who were allegedly quoted the steel dossier, they said they never told anyone. They didn't know anything about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , terrible things that went on there. It's not true.\par \par \uc2 Every part of the Steele dossier and Igor Danchenko's lies are going to get exposed at next month's trial.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay. Now, let's go on to the other breaking news story tonight, and this gets very alarming that as early as I think December 21st to 23rd I forget the exact date. I read your article, that in fact multiple warnings intelligence was saying that there were groups, radical groups out there planning to riot on January the 6th, and they were ignored completely?\par \par \uc2 SOLOMON: Yeah, absolutely. So, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , Homeland Security, U.S. Marshals Service and the Metropolitan Police Department all provided the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  with extensive detailed information they were intercepting through their sources of people planning to go to the January 6th rally and cause trouble, attack members of Congress, storm the capital. That's an exact word from the intelligence reports.\par \par \uc2 All of that is gathered up by the intelligence division of the \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  and it's disseminated to the leadership and other people and then nothing happens. In fact, the final plans for January 6th and all these documents are on just the news now, you can go see them, actually says there was no threat analysis, no known threat analysis, a complete lie.\par \par \uc2 But here's the most important thing: a whistleblower has stepped forward. His name is Eric Core. He's a decorated army -- military veteran. He is an intelligence analyst. He was the one of the best that the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  have. He now works for the \uc2 Homeland Security Department\uc2 , he's so trusted.\par \par \uc2 He says that he wrote a memo, actually we have the memo, on January 9th, three days after the terrible riots occurred, he wrote a memo to all his bosses saying, listen, there's no way to sugarcoat this. We knew in advance of all this intelligence and we didn't act on it.\par \par \uc2 We failed. We've got to learn from it. We can't cover it up. There's no way to spin this other than we had an opportunity to stop and he talks about how nauseous he was knowing that his fellow officers went out there on January 6 completely blind to the intelligence he provided his bosses.\par \par \uc2 This is a devastating whistleblower. I have confirmed he is working with Capitol Hill Republicans, House Republicans working on the House Administration Committee, Rodney Davis, they've interviewed him and several -- all the whistleblowers, if Republicans get control of Congress next year, an entirely different story about \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 's preparations for January 6 is going to burst onto the scene.\par \par \uc2 Tonight people get to see the first part of it the actual whistleblowers memos to his bosses three days after January 6, and all the intelligence he provided going back to December 21st, 2020.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And we expect that the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  chief who had requested the guard, he's coming out with the book and that's supposed to be equally as explosive?\par \par \uc2 SOLOMON: I've heard those reports. I haven't been able to confirm it, but I have -- I've heard that he's been writing on a book or some sort of a long expose on what he knows. But the documents that are out tonight are going to air will be show one \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  had plenty of warnings, specific detailed extensive non-stop warnings and when they alerted, when they got their police department ready for January 6th, they left all that intelligence out.\par \par \uc2 I encourage everybody to go take a look at the riot unit document, the document they gave the riot control units. It says there was no threat analysis at all. That is simply not true from the documents we made public tonight. Iroquois, remember that name, he's going to be a very important witness in the next year in Congress.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. John Solomon, thank you for those reports. We appreciate it. Justthenews.com.\par \par \uc2 Now, we are only 56 days away from the all-important midterm elections and frankly it can't come fast enough. Now, today, we got more horrific economic numbers. Inflation was even higher than expected, rising in August, again a 41-year high, 8.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 Food, rent, health care, electricity, all are way up, and also now at record highs. Gases and there's still more than double what it was before Biden became president, despite a dangerous political gimmick that he has been implementing -- implementing to empty out our Strategic Petroleum Reserves right before the election, how convenient. We'll flood the market with more energy, more oil, so gas prices will seem like they're going down.\par \par \uc2 The problem is, it's a major national security risk because now those reserves are at a 38-year low. All of this after a two-point interest rate hike from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 . Now, another rate hike next week is all but certain, likely another, what, 75 basis points, which is massive.\par \par \uc2 And that means the housing market is on the verge of completely imploding. New home, a construction will stop, sale of pre-existing homes will stop, home values will plummet, on top of your IRAs and your 401ks.\par \par \uc2 Keep in mind, when Trump left office, the average fixed rate mortgage was 2.77 percent, 30-year fixed rate mortgage.\par \par \uc2 Now under Biden, it is over six percent and it is now getting higher. So under Trump, a 30-year mortgage on a $500,000 house with a down payment had a monthly payment of one thousand six hundred and thirty seven dollars, you buy that same house today, it will cost you 2,369 bucks a month, a $730 difference.\par \par \uc2 Now, make no mistake, this hurts low-income Americans, middle-income Americans and especially those that are on fixed incomes. And simply put, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his fellow Democrats, they are now destroying the American dream for pretty much everyone attempting to climb the ladder, and those just trying to hold on. Two-thirds of Americans now, they live paycheck to paycheck.\par \par \uc2 And now, the market is also responding they posted the worst single day since the height of the pandemic in 202