ny times. It's about using the power of the Justice Department to influence our elections. It's about the partisanship that has infected the DOJ at the highest levels. That everyone who treasures the rule of law in America should be terrified about what is happening to our country.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And then we have the crime facing women in this country. Women just walking on the streets, families. This is terrifying. And this is what they're doing? This is what the focus is? The American people are the problem, or the criminals are the problem, the drug cartels are the problem?\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: I have a little girl, I have a wife. And I am terrified at the level of random crime that is happening on the street.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Depraved crime.\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: Depraved and completely predictable, and yet they're bothering Stephen, because he emailed and texted with people. It's ridiculous. I mean, it's absolutely absurd, but it's an indictment of our justice system that we have this going on in such an obvious way a vindication of everyone who has been saying from the beginning, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the DOJ were out of control, shot through with partisans and can't be trusted.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Stephen, I think the Republicans, they get - I think they're going to win the House and the Senate. I'm going to say it tonight. Maybe I'm wrong, but I don't think so. They are going to win both.\par \par \uc2 I think of this narrative of Joementum that is - I think, it's all BS. OK. I think in the end, the American people are going to have to see the Republicans step up with real solutions if they get back into power. If they get the presidency, they got to break up these big agencies.\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: We have to do something.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They can't just talk about it. I'm sick of hearing them make lists of things they want to do. It has to be specific. Break it up, make it accountable.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: And to the point that Ben was making, put the cartels out of business, stop going after your political opposition.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Ben, do you think it will happen? The Republicans have the kahunas, so they're going to do the same thing they always do and punt it down the road?\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: I mean, come on. Are you putting - are you asking me to put my faith in the Republican Party, the GOP, that has disappointed us?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, they are better than Democrats.\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: So long. I mean, I would like to see it. I would like to see it.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: It's an existential moment. I really do believe that.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. It has to be done. Stephen and Ben, get your solar panels from of the closet. All right. Great to see you both.\par \par \uc2 All right. The other day, I took to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . The boys will like this, to note that \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  had failed to include Queen Elizabeth in this new book she wrote about gutsy women. Well, that didn't sit well apparently with the former Secretary of State and failed presidential candidate, who took time out of her very busy schedule to respond.\par \par \uc2 Tweeting, "Thanks for getting the word out about Gutsy, Laura. A book now turned \uc2 Apple\uc2  TV Plus docuseries. It was a challenge to narrow down who to feature, because it's true, there are just too many amazing women in the world."\par \par \uc2 Well, I don't disagree, Mrs. Clinton. And maybe I was being unfair to Hillary, guys. I mean, why include women like Queen Elizabeth, or mother - now St. Teresa globally recognized for their tireless service to others. When there are so many more deserving gutsy gals out there.\par \par \uc2 Just look at two who were featured on Hillary's TV series, like the foul mouthed comedian Amy Schumer, or Megan, the (ph) whop stallion, whose gutsiness is on display when she tells young girls to shake their butts and spread their legs. But maybe, I don't know, we