gs. So very graciously agreed. And then she negotiated behind closed doors to have it be independent and separate of each other, because she thought it would be a - her campaign said, they thought it would be a more productive conversation.\par \par \uc2 And for someone who talks about democracy all the time, the cornerstone of democracy in this country is healthy debate. And the voters of Washington State deserve to see the choice in front of them.\par \par \uc2 I mean, just look at \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 's most recent votes in her record though. She voted for the American rescue plan $1.9 billion, which Democrats and left-leaning economist said that that would cause inflation. Inflation is a tax on every single American.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. $1.9 trillion, I believe. Yes, it was - I wish it was billion. But fair point.\par \par \uc2 So these debate invitations were extended. You accepted them, she tries to do it solo. That's not a debate by the way. We reached out to Senator Murray's office, the campaign. And they responded a short while ago to us saying, "As Senator Murray has made clear, she will absolutely debate Tiffany Smiley this fall, just like she's debated in every general election."\par \par \uc2 But they didn't offer a date or a time. Why it's taken so darn long to agree to even one debate? And I think this goes to the point, the same point that we're seeing in Pennsylvania, Tiffany, that the Democrats really don't think the voters deserve to have answers during a very difficult economic time for American families at a time with enormous problem with crime. They don't think the voters need to hear from them.\par \par \uc2 SMILEY: Well, and that's where it's just at. It's absolutely wrong. I mean, the people want leaders. They're sick and tired of career politicians. I was 11 years old when \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  was first elected. And I told the ever editorial board, I said, I will end this just how I started it, talking directly to the voters.\par \par \uc2 And this reckless tax and spend agenda that the Democrats have imposed on all Americans. I asked anyone to come join us, because when I get into the Senate, I will fight for my recovery and reform agenda. That's what we can fight for.\par \par \uc2 And anyone who wants to join me can join me at SmileyForWashington to hold these career politicians accountable, and get our country back on track, rein in the out of control spending and start delivering results for the American people.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. I think, the dinosaurs have to lumber right off the stage at this point. They've had their day, now it's your day.\par \par \uc2 Tiffany, best of luck. We'll check back with you. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 And speaking of the midterms, the spinmeisters are out in full force. We have been telling you for weeks that the media would begin to engage in the Biden and the Democrats comeback story, that they would relentlessly sell that.\par \par \uc2 Well, Axios was the newest entrant in acing the administration's stenographer and pumping Bidenomics, giving the administration a chance to rehabilitate its poor standing with no pushback whatsoever. But like everything else, this is just another mirage.\par \par \uc2 And one surprising source is stepping forward to offer a note of caution. \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 ' Nate Cohn writes, "The polling warning signs are flashing again. Democratic Senate candidates are outrunning expectations in the same places where the polls overestimated Biden in 2020 and Clinton in 2016." Interesting.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now Charlie Hurt, Fox News contributor and opinion editor for \uc2 The Washington Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Charlie, these comeback stories to me seem geared toward suppressing the Republican vote, demoralizing Republicans, think, Oh, it's all hope is lost. And it seems to be things are tightening quite quickly and not surprisingly.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, WASHINGTON TIMES OPINION EDITOR: Yes, exactly. And of course, that's always their strategy and it's nice to have the media entirely in your pocket, because Democrats do this every election. And even though I think we see it coming, a lot of people fall for it anyway.\par \par \uc2 But you're exactly right. And President Obama, the problem with the Biden- nomics storyline and all of these claims that somehow things are turning around brilliantly, is that you can't really hide from the economy. People have to fill up their car. They have to go buy groceries. They feel the price of things. They feel the economy in their own lives. So no matter how much the media tries to lie about it, no matter how much the White House blatantly lies about it, it doesn't really work if people are at home and they feel the pain personally.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: According to this new poll out, also, fewer Americas are listing inflation as their top issue. That was the big headline on the Hill. But then you dig into the article, and it says that it remained the issue most frequently cited as being top of mind ahead of abortion and health care.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Look, you can't deny what you're paying every month for your utility bills. I'm looking at mine, and it's pretty astounding.\par \par \uc2 HURT: Exactly. Exactly. And why we turn to these people for polling every election just baffles me. And of course, the one pollster who gets these things more right than anybody else, Trafalgar, has Washington state as a three or four-point race. If Washington state, the Senate race in Washington state is a three or four point race, it's going to be an absolute bloodbath.\par \par \uc2 But the one thing, and I think all of these polls are going to show a very different picture in about a month from now, and that's because when things are as bad as they are right now in terms of the economy, in terms of crime, in terms of the open border, people tend to check into the election much later. And it's not really all that surprising that a lot of people are sort of looking at this casually right now. But when it comes time to actually cast a ballot, they're going to think about all these things that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has done and Democrats have done to make their lives personally more miserable. And they're going to punish \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think a lot of people feel that pain has been inflicted on them with school closures and high prices. And I think at the ballot box, they're going to inflict some pain at the incumbent party that has driven these policies. I don't believe that with the choices between I want more abortions across America, or I want more money in my pocket, people are going to choose they want more abortions. I just don't think -- I think that's the loser argument as much as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and everyone else wants to argue otherwise.\par \par \uc2 HURT: Yes, and they are not just going to lose among Republicans and independents. They're also going to lose among Democrats because Democrats don't want to pay $5 a gallon gasoline, and they don't want inflation going through the roof. And by the way, also, as you have always pointed out going back years, they don't want open borders. Regular Democrat voters don't want open borders. The only people who want it are these lunatics in Washington.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Charlie, great to see you tonight, as always, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Why are we still allowing our greatest geopolitical adversary to buy up our farmland? An Angle investigation in moments. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What if I told you that the largest pork processor in the U.S. was owned by another country? And then what if I told you that much of our farmland was also being bought up by the country? Then what if I told you that some of the farmland was set near U.S. military bases? That's pretty bad. But what if I told you that the country doing all of this was a major adversary of the United States, the adversary of the United States?\par \par \uc2 The Angle has been warning about this for months, and over the weekend, "The Wall Street Journal" put it the most starkly ever. "Chinese ownership of U.S. farmland leapt more than 20-fold in just one decade from $81 million in 2010 to $1.8 billion in 2020. Beijing hasn't outlined a strategy, but large-scale state backing for these investments indicates there is one.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now are the authors, two authors of that piece, both from the Lincoln Network. Lars Erik Schonander is a policy technologist, and Geoffrey Cain is a senior fellow. Lars, how long is it been since our own government has audited, carefully audited these purchases?\par \par \uc2 LARS ERIK SCHONANDER, LINCOLN NETWORK POLICY TECHNOLOGIST: So the last time the program that tracks these investments has been audited was in 1989 according to the J.O. So ever since then, there has been no formal audit of the program.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Geoffrey, how is this possible? You have the CCP approving these purchases, clearly, because no one's going to buy this without approval from the CCP. And yet this is just like we're just going along though. This is fine. Tell us the worst of the worst, here.\par \par \uc2 GEOFFREY CAIN: The worst of the worst is that the CCP is buying through private companies in China massive tracts of land, many acres of land that are right near military bases. So there's one example in North Dakota, another one in Texas. It truly is a wild situation to see Chinese companies openly buying land where they can spy on American military bases.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Can we do that in China?\par \par \uc2 CAIN: No, that's not allowed.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So we're not allowed to do any of this in China, but they can come here and buy whatever they want?\par \par \uc2 CAIN: China is a communist country and people cannot own land. The state owns land. We can't go there, we can't buy land, open a factory on that land. But Chinese companies are free to come here. This place is open.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Lars, \uc2 Smithfield Foods\uc2  website addressed concerns of their own ties to China. They claim they're not a Chinese state-owned enterprise. They don't undertake commercial activities on behalf of the Chinese government. Lars?\par \par \uc2 SCHONANDER: It's understandable why they do that, but I would point out it's very strange that when the deal came through in 2013, the company that brought out Smithfield Food, W.H. Group, was given a $4 billion loan by the bank of China, a state backed Chinese bank, to do said loan. That's, all things considered, very strange that they were being fronted the money to buy our largest pork producer.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But can't we just cut to the chase though. Nothing that Chinese interests do in the United States is not approved by the CCP in some way, shape, or form, correct?\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So the CCP is buying land. I'm sorry, you guys are a little academic. I'm going to say it the way regular people talk. The CCP is approving every single purchase that's made in the United States, one way or another.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: In one way or another, because in America we have separation of private business and government. We have liberty. We have freedom. In China, that doesn't exist. Private companies are ultimately accountable and must answer to the Chinese Communist Party. There's no way around that, and if they're buying land by a military base, that is open to abuse, it's open to spying. That is a major red flag, and I don't how this situation happened, but it is absolutely ludicrous.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They shouldn't be able to buy anything here. They have millions of people enslaved in labor camps, and we're welcoming here.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Adam Minter of "\uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 " wrote a piece implying that the Chinese investment in U.S. farmland, to ban that would be a national security, or food security issue for us. He also went on to say it was racist, this is a "\uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 " writer, racist to ban China. I guess the libertarians think this is all open markets, open borders, they're still peddling that nonsense. Your reaction to that, Lars?\par \par \uc2 SCHONANDER: There are concerns about that by \uc2 Grace Meng\uc2  in a different bill a few months ago, but the boring response to that is that there are other adversaries that have been raised concerns about that, from North Korea, Russia, Venezuela. It isn't just a Chinese thing. Any country that's an adversary of the United States should be shown the door.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Roughly 40 percent of U.S. domestic farmland will be transferred to new ownership, it said, in these -- this is just, this is crazy. And Lars -- I'll go to Geoffrey on this, it just mentions, but last year Congressman Newhouse added this amendment to the Agriculture spending bill that would ban agriculture purchases from Chinese parties. Democrat Congresswoman \uc2 Grace Meng\uc2 , as you noted, strongly opposed the amendment. Listen to her logic. Everyone has to hear this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. GRACE MENG, (D-NY): I understand the issue and the concerns and the intentions behind it, but I am also concerned about singling out China, and the repercussions that it will have on the health and safety of Asian Americans here in the United States.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Geoffrey?\par \par \uc2 CAIN: This is one of the major red flags of the Democratic left. They say that worrying about our national security against the most authoritarian police state in the world, which is China, is going to be conflated with racism against Asian Americans. These are separate issues. We can promote equality at home. We can promote the rights of minorities.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's a fake issue.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: It's a fake issue. We can also fight China. We can defend against Chinese incursions, Chinese Communist Party incursions into the country. These are separate.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You know what this reminds me of, the Wuhan lab. You could never talk about the Wuhan lab and the origins of the virus because that's racist. It's a total non sequitur, but they throw sand in the wind and hope you can't see anything. Guys, great to see you tonight.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Thanks, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Why are credit card companies working with Democrats to monitor and track gun purchases? The Congressman who recently schooled Democrats on the gun issue, \uc2 Greg Steube\uc2 , is here in moments. He'll react. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Democrats, they have been really ramping up the pressure, haven't they, on their corporate cronies to target political adversaries. And among them are law-abiding gun owners. Earlier this month, Senator Elizabeth Warren and over two dozen Democrats sent letters to the CEOs of major credit card companies and they demanded that those companies start tracking gun sales.\par \par \uc2 Last week, New York Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  tweeted in part, "Everyone needs to do their part to combat gun violence. \uc2 American Express\uc2 , \uc2 Mastercard\uc2 , \uc2 Visa\uc2  should categorize firearm purchases." Then on Friday the \uc2 international organization for standardization\uc2  approved new merchant codes for gun sales, which would clear the way for credit card companies to do what Democrats were asking.\par \par \uc2 So guess what happened. \uc2 Visa\uc2 , \uc2 Mastercard\uc2 , and \uc2 American Express\uc2 , just like that, all caved and will now categorize gun store sales separately, meaning your purchases can now be tracked.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Florida Congressman and gun owner, proud gun owner, \uc2 Greg Steube\uc2 . Congressman, if you all take back the House, will you launch inquiries into the way this pressure was put on these companies?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 GREG STEUBE\uc2 , (R-FL) HOUSE FREEDOM CAUCUS: I'm very much looking forward to the ability to issue subpoenas from the Judiciary Committee to get communications from the DOJ, the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , the Biden administration, Democratic senators and congressmen and women that asked these different credit card companies to do this, because I would not be shocked that in a year from now we find out that it was the \uc2 FBI\uc2  that asked these credit card companies to start keeping track of this data, just like they asked Zuckerberg with \uc2 Facebook\uc2  to diminish Russian disinformation on the Hunter Biden laptop story.\par \par \uc2 I would not be shocked if the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was involved in this. And if we take the House back and we get the majority back, we will absolutely be issuing subpoenas to get the real information and the facts and the communication that went on between the administration and these companies.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, the Second Amendment provides a constitutional right to keep and bear arms. The Supreme Court has ruled on the individual nature of this right. Are there other rights that they can then put into some tracking system in order to surveil, or any other things that they could regarding the First Amendment? Maybe church attendance? They treat the Second Amendment differently for a reason. They don't want individuals to be able to own the types of weapons they want to own. I'm not talking about machine guns. But they want to get into people's gun lockers if they can, and make sure they can track every single weapon for law-abiding people.\par \par \uc2 STEUBE: Yes, and they've been doing this. Just look at the bills that they passed through Congress. And in other first amendment right, other constitutional amendments, look at what California is doing on what doctors can and cannot say about vaccines. They just passed a bill recently, I read an article that they're limiting what doctors can say about the vaccine and COVID-19. They are absolutely taking steps to take away your constitutional rights. It starts with the First Amendment. Then it goes to the Second Amendment. And they're going to keep on and keep on doing what they're doing until law-abiding citizens start standing up and taking back our country.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Here's what CNBC's \uc2 Andrew Ross Sorkin\uc2  thinks, Congressman, about what these credit card companies are actually doing. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANDREW ROSS SORKIN\uc2 , CNBC HOST: There is a lot in this country, which is to say, that effectively says we do not keep a master list. There is no mastered database in America of guns. And some people look at this and say, is this a backdoor shadow list? That's not the goal.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, if that's not the goal, then what is the goal?\par \par \uc2 STEUBE: That's absolutely the goal. They know they can't pass through Congress with 60 votes in the Senate a gun registration nationally for every American or for every gun that they own, so they do it in the backdoor way. They get these woke corporations to agree with what they want to do, and they do it inadvertently. And then when the \uc2 FBI\uc2  or the DOJ wants those lists of what Americans own what firearms, they'll just do a subpoenaed to \uc2 Visa\uc2  or \uc2 Mastercard\uc2  or \uc2 American Express\uc2 . Congressman didn't pass a law. And they get the information that they wanted to because these corporations are at the will of progressives and this administration. It's got to be stopped.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, if Republicans take back the House, the Senate, there has to be real reform, not just talk of reform, but moves to break up these companies, these major, like ATF, total corruption in ATF, they have to be broken up, yes?\par \par \uc2 STEUBE: \uc2 FBI\uc2 , DOJ, rest assured that myself and Jim Jordan and the Judiciary Committee will stop at nothing to ensure that freedom is back in America, that investigations are done to show how deep the deep state is.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We need to do it. Congressman, thank you.\par \par \uc2 A pool party and an \uc2 NFL\uc2  game? The Last Bite will explain.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The weather was so bad in Chicago during the Bears game yesterday, a lot of folks were wondering whether they should start looking for animals in the big wooden thing. But that slippery field didn't stop the \uc2 Chicago Bears\uc2  from celebrating their upset in an unforgettable way.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (CHEERS)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, I love that. That is like the breaststroke and the butterfly all in one.\par \par \uc2 "GUTFELD!" next.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020220913ei9c00001\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\cl